{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.108562Z","id":"5820c9221d99f2ba90540d9569cb078db6551f7650dbeab74665eb27239cc3e9","body":{"detail":"Deferred by the owner (D5, line 31): version 1 keeps current identity systems; reporter tokens minted by the deployer's backend (§5.3) cover filing without a Clax identity.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":438},"content_hash":"d57e8df1c79607b1e70dfc4ec2addbe90e02b723af407580d7b1af1e26d68141"},"summary":"Deployer-defined identity: OIDC sign-in and RFC 8693 token exchange against the deployer's IdP","supersedes":"395bca448814296a21c55a58c207dc4974216621af8851130cf5fadc5f2dcdf0","tags":["revisit:a deployer without a backend (a pure SPA) needs to mint reporter tokens","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.209455Z","id":"37ab530e5199d28179dbc2c937f9a3d4d8f2bcb6f6d5e93885c799d77a7f4bf6","body":{"detail":"Accepted for version 1: running it in Kubernetes is out of scope (D4), and one replica with a persistent volume is the supported shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":439},"end":{"line":440},"content_hash":"397d8aa0be732f8bdee5662903082203c70572dd00e73312b7102ff38628f5a1"},"summary":"A deployer's Clax runs as one replica: the store is SQLite with one writer","supersedes":"27e20e31cbd0a85f83f6278b33c3a069a38c8f92195d35df98bfcbb1b71b262c","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.312127Z","id":"d513ae48f63b046773b1d1348cd1233742b0150e6ada62a42e71505a7e814a35","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner asked for opaque metadata Clax does not interpret (D6, line 33); a schema and an index are only needed once Clax filters by it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":442},"end":{"line":442},"content_hash":"4660a2ab6bcfdb863d8dd3f20eda5f87cef2cf69bfe528e0b659cb140e638dd2"},"summary":"Registered sources with a JSON Schema for metadata, and queries over metadata","supersedes":"7c9e0e9f41418762d86bd419699adab5fc8c9052783e8420fb76fedf04c4a29d","tags":["revisit:an agent or app needs to list reports by a metadata field","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.416852Z","id":"3956282045cb7dd6b2113edaf1bb9ee22105b25dd793dd8e9215d3a62f8b351b","body":{"detail":"Not now: it needs a migration of the live-page tables, which installed databases have; external artifacts are a new kind beside live instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":443},"end":{"line":443},"content_hash":"1ba59b3f3f5075ec0d89d733f34a2b50e0305c59a45fbb75fed5640d62d84968"},"summary":"Make live pages external artifacts of a built-in web source, one model instead of two","supersedes":"15ff2f16280128d6701b7b90ee05a8e9053d07bb5a680f368138110ce0d64258","tags":["revisit:a fix has to be made twice, once for live pages and once for external artifacts","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.523912Z","id":"a86586e51ba37503694e82e5d84c6b8eb5baeb39f2d418a3c4a6abb3654e1765","body":{"detail":"Proposed in §5.1-§5.2; not yet accepted. Today the extension's credential is the owner identity (crates/clax-http/src/extension.rs), which cannot be right on a hosted Clax the extension must reach (D1).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"305d6308c9ffb2a9934fcdafecbb622e25f6c8d5ede4fdf24b202b97012353a9"},"summary":"Decide the credential model: browser session and signed grants only, consent only in a browser session, daemon token as a bootstrap, the extension's cxe_ credential replaced by a grant","supersedes":"283da5c7043b66639902fca475fb1aebf95ec9f2531f2f83a7d30e1551ff10aa","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.629550Z","id":"469ff1217f49422f29b9a0f4cfa46341982f946e4ed66d79ea7f6139fb960621","body":{"detail":"Per instance lets everyone on one organization's instance share an artifact by its external ID; on clax.dev an ID another person holds is then 409 external_id_taken to someone who may not read it. Per person never collides, but two colleagues get two artifacts for one record.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":464},"end":{"line":468},"content_hash":"dda02cdf311ff69548e88c1cc59f58bfedbd2b32db88fe412023cebb4c9e6643"},"summary":"Decide the uniqueness scope of external_id: per instance (proposed) or per creating person","supersedes":"7817911aa2dde3311dc6d040e2b57778aea54ef671810c45e14c366c0edac1bd","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.734242Z","id":"0daa09552e4d5456d0408a92763056f8da60237b74065448ee8743bd99e366c1","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"92d117b022d6f61ff8b6829446a617637a40f4e3579a5302f41e5d830d747c60"},"summary":"Decide who may write an artifact's metadata: anyone who may edit it (proposed) or only its creator","supersedes":"392bbc7508a14791eefe0f07fc7483a1edfb3a364d067e29d1681c8612879689","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:22:34.839113Z","id":"bd228eda7de5697457c560ae565b35049087548135c08c2e265cee524aea6912","body":{"detail":"§6.1 and §6.4 read D6 this way; the owner stated the opaque identifier and metadata without naming what they attach to.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"fd28ced0a83952818697ca5e7d4de32a54114cd514293280e27cad305f3cce23"},"summary":"Confirm the opaque ID and metadata of D6 attach to both artifacts (external_id, metadata) and threads (reporter_id, metadata)","supersedes":"a908b6f897f8cdacf4c1a6600debba746d0c2c2f9ee41b68a8af25abc4fe44d1","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:47.868439Z","id":"5b99b3540ad0e7afc06fbb66bf0fe8034627f34b22cc922f88247c2b023711b7","body":{"detail":"Rejected by the owner (D2, line 23): the contract is generated from the Rust routes, so it cannot drift from what the server answers, and route auth extractors become the contract's channel and rights fields (§5.2).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"b1848067578525f927b23d7990c501926d6ffa5dac6dc584ea86244d02abe3e9"},"summary":"Write the API contract first (OpenAPI by hand) and generate the Rust route types from it","supersedes":"ebd2196c21502882f803f2706d6f848a7f1674ffff65fb4d8e7bdcee60eea8ad","tags":["revisit:a consumer needs a contract change published before the Rust routes for it exist","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:48.012532Z","id":"99ab48a65abb13834d41a1d24a019a6e67b6d84dba9eb282a042fcc35684b6e1","body":{"detail":"Not taken: generated bindings bring unsafe code, which AGENTS.md allows only in crates/clax-embed/src/ffi.rs; clients generated from the contract need none.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"eb212cf8e6d3eb1e4b434edc43cff3b37fba939f85b1d414f450a3187832baad"},"summary":"Native SDKs for Swift, Kotlin or Python through FFI bindings (UniFFI) over the Rust client","supersedes":"33dc49b364cd87a051f0889ca8b57812586bfd0380ea31ae7cb7d39ccaa65900","tags":["revisit:a deployer needs a native SDK in a language the contract generator does not cover","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:48.145287Z","id":"71418d389f3d0a37f22e37ed31a8466b3e9aeb087e84861e8cd1e6227b3f439e","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the shell and extension carry bundle budgets, and a wasm core adds its size and an async bridge to every call; a hand-written TS core over generated types keeps modules tree-shakeable. Two cores (TS, Rust) must then agree on retry and signing rules, which the conformance suite in §12 checks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":155},"content_hash":"c4f7059bbfeedb78dc27f4172528b3f5c402ca462efca90c79bd6961687b0551"},"summary":"Compile the Rust client core to wasm and use it as the TypeScript SDK","supersedes":"1a8b61a6f5020b643cd502831e8087d45dda85c02f2654b76d22a86ea049737e","tags":["revisit:the TS and Rust client cores disagree on a retry or signing rule that the conformance suite missed","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:48.294523Z","id":"0110c9b7099de6d4bca54f9e8443a690bd7c6e725d7182711e0198b67867d6a4","body":{"detail":"Rejected by the owner (D11, line 45): employees sign in to the deployer's app and nothing else. The cost is that reporters are not Clax people and have no Clax inbox (§7.5).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":238},"content_hash":"846bc412be4958d2af0b74ec88de4b71f527fe1cd89ee9819cf381094ad5a4ce"},"summary":"Each employee signs in to the Clax instance (popup sign-in giving an origin-bound grant) before filing","supersedes":"0ba0de7affdd3ca5ad13593164619dbb122eb435e3a64bbb4077f97353f46de3","tags":["revisit:a deployer needs replies to reach reporters in a Clax inbox rather than the overlay or webhooks","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:48.423352Z","id":"9243a5b60d76bdeb02fb5bf64f42e3bd99e0bc9fd941aceea71a941f6bfc9e61","body":{"detail":"Accepted: the service grant reaches one queue, is revocable (ending every token it minted), and is rate-limited; a deployer's backend that misnames employees misattributes reports only within its own queue.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":227},"end":{"line":234},"content_hash":"44e8585e88050c8f77d635b9d848e3406e44bb76ff54a4a90a5ad986006e2c85"},"summary":"Clax trusts the deployer's backend to name reporters: a service grant can mint a token for any reporter_id","supersedes":"de9fde792bb5faa286e55cff47bd6a04dd9b67fe98cc60f7f40b00d503a813b7","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:48.553743Z","id":"e2466608395abdac1f0d1dc1e8b28da717d8e9087a8113b9956045885d8aeb7f","body":{"detail":"Accepted: metadata is opaque and unencrypted by design (D6); docs/contract.md must say it holds no secrets.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":266},"content_hash":"003a4b1d9692640c0ec1dc637f0dab4eec6aa2c0c3f3d1c560be0b230b42ad11"},"summary":"Artifact metadata is readable by everyone who may read the artifact","supersedes":"67f94b5f07d8e83bbd1c1dcd3e338ccaf3923e1f6ffb8e9e0dddf17eba5c9358","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:48.704126Z","id":"d45fb772b8491baed40b5463bdf34bb230327dd5f92895cb6d71426d10e61716","body":{"detail":"Rejected by the owner (D10, line 41): an agent that stops working without ending its session would hold a report indefinitely; a lease that expires, renewed by working, frees it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":366},"end":{"line":383},"content_hash":"02d83c491767768560cac301ca3940ac6e4bf6c001d36dcfcc25a644fd94f8be"},"summary":"Claims as today's thread ownership, held until handoff or the claimant's session ends","supersedes":"691d6e6b9abe000ab374c39b1e28e043c6064c6c9f0b418fae21dee5ec0aa6cb","tags":["revisit:lease expiry releases reports from agents that are still working on them","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:48.827215Z","id":"ce04711fa60dfc91b8967bba245d8178599ace6adb6448cfb457c74cc795780d","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the browser asks the employee on every capture, against D11 (line 45); DOM-rendered clips need no prompt but can be partial (§8.2).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":410},"end":{"line":421},"content_hash":"61232b045d05c05e20c4b8fdb06f462c20683c681b22cd1c519f56994768a55e"},"summary":"getDisplayMedia screenshots as the overlay's default clip","supersedes":"51a7aec1834142caf04a25fc8a3a78ab21e83ab3678a874e220f64d64279ab82","tags":["revisit:most clips in a queue are reported partial","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:48.947566Z","id":"646444811ad2b3f30bbe625f1dadcd176297c6d1334da90ba0cc76c296112968","body":{"detail":"Accepted: clips are always taken (D9) without a prompt (D11); what was not rendered is listed with the clip, and the extension's pixel-exact capture is used when it is installed.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":412},"end":{"line":415},"content_hash":"a78daa7b0b8e00c2b450bc6824ef2f38dea7dc294f37b0c95392aa406b26d618"},"summary":"Overlay clips rendered from the DOM can be partial (cross-origin images, canvas, video, cross-origin iframes)","supersedes":"f7a9479d9be463a8782b6576a3525271d9c230025c402f514190fdfa58710fc7","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:49.065141Z","id":"5555f8be3529db40978a290318ec89476c3650bb598558166ded7e9641a93367","body":{"detail":"Deferred by the owner (D5, line 31): version 1 keeps current identity systems; reporter tokens minted by the deployer's backend (§5.3) cover filing without a Clax identity.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":450},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"d57e8df1c79607b1e70dfc4ec2addbe90e02b723af407580d7b1af1e26d68141"},"summary":"Deployer-defined identity: OIDC sign-in and RFC 8693 token exchange against the deployer's IdP","supersedes":"5820c9221d99f2ba90540d9569cb078db6551f7650dbeab74665eb27239cc3e9","tags":["revisit:a deployer without a backend (a pure SPA) needs to mint reporter tokens","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:49.184495Z","id":"247e7c2d5c9e279ae28126dfd443f895453166043eaa5674ad4769c2a6a7704e","body":{"detail":"Accepted for version 1: running it in Kubernetes is out of scope (D4), and one replica with a persistent volume is the supported shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":451},"end":{"line":452},"content_hash":"397d8aa0be732f8bdee5662903082203c70572dd00e73312b7102ff38628f5a1"},"summary":"A deployer's Clax runs as one replica: the store is SQLite with one writer","supersedes":"37ab530e5199d28179dbc2c937f9a3d4d8f2bcb6f6d5e93885c799d77a7f4bf6","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:49.304341Z","id":"51d3dffb03be4c36530b3e1b4c98c24fc1a46690b34e8f886e8e4820be6300d4","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner asked for opaque metadata Clax does not interpret (D6, line 33); a schema and an index are only needed once Clax filters by it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":454},"end":{"line":454},"content_hash":"4660a2ab6bcfdb863d8dd3f20eda5f87cef2cf69bfe528e0b659cb140e638dd2"},"summary":"Registered sources with a JSON Schema for metadata, and queries over metadata","supersedes":"d513ae48f63b046773b1d1348cd1233742b0150e6ada62a42e71505a7e814a35","tags":["revisit:an agent or app needs to list reports by a metadata field","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:49.445299Z","id":"23e8857e55120640168b963b530294a7c2020526137c2cdadd9df815ddd2f529","body":{"detail":"Not now: it needs a migration of the live-page tables, which installed databases have; external artifacts are a new kind beside live instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":455},"end":{"line":455},"content_hash":"1ba59b3f3f5075ec0d89d733f34a2b50e0305c59a45fbb75fed5640d62d84968"},"summary":"Make live pages external artifacts of a built-in web source, one model instead of two","supersedes":"3956282045cb7dd6b2113edaf1bb9ee22105b25dd793dd8e9215d3a62f8b351b","tags":["revisit:a fix has to be made twice, once for live pages and once for external artifacts","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:49.574724Z","id":"65a0af16bb7958d42dda0cb6a6131a8d20bfbcd7a6a1405e1e9241c7aa25c0f2","body":{"detail":"Per instance lets everyone on one organization's instance share an artifact by its external ID; on clax.dev an ID another person holds is then 409 external_id_taken to someone who may not read it. Per person never collides, but two colleagues get two artifacts for one record.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"4a66b6f70c22aaa7ce411d26e0234264664e774b4993b6a947a0f5e02c71f984"},"summary":"Decide the uniqueness scope of external_id: per instance (proposed) or per creating person","supersedes":"469ff1217f49422f29b9a0f4cfa46341982f946e4ed66d79ea7f6139fb960621","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:44:49.698953Z","id":"3ad50c23725cea95d54adfa052dc83a5234594bec45dd46ea296f292afafa96a","body":{"detail":"Accepted (D17, line 58): an ID names one artifact per instance and integrators choose unique IDs; each queue's threads stay its own (lines 344-347), so only the artifact-level fields are shared. On clax.dev two deployers that pick the same ID see and can edit each other's artifact metadata.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":344},"end":{"line":349},"content_hash":"7951fc08ec74d5671bd996d5eee0998ac7e9a7a58526a28302fe6007d53bdf18"},"summary":"Integrators that reuse one external_id share the artifact's title, URL, metadata and revision across their queues","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:45:08.788176Z","id":"f382a99f394fe53b73f7f8872ce9f176d1a390719a8f63241201cd1f8419e1df","body":{"detail":"01 yes","kind":"comment","references":"a86586e51ba37503694e82e5d84c6b8eb5baeb39f2d418a3c4a6abb3654e1765","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"305d6308c9ffb2a9934fcdafecbb622e25f6c8d5ede4fdf24b202b97012353a9"},"summary":"Decided: two credential kinds (browser session, signed grant), consent only in a browser session, the daemon token as a bootstrap, the extension's cxe_ credential replaced by a grant","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:45:08.788853Z","id":"376f3c5300ebf1da519f0f09ce0dde547c22aeb988d384d831d117cda55aa67f","body":{"detail":"03 anyone who may edit it, keep a toolpath audit log","kind":"comment","references":"0daa09552e4d5456d0408a92763056f8da60237b74065448ee8743bd99e366c1","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"92d117b022d6f61ff8b6829446a617637a40f4e3579a5302f41e5d830d747c60"},"summary":"Decided: anyone who may edit an artifact may write its metadata, and every change is recorded in the Toolpath journal","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:45:08.789381Z","id":"91c4969afb7ed79eb517045562ca3b358afd761ea72f09d5846b7b04030b21c5","body":{"detail":"04 yes","kind":"comment","references":"bd228eda7de5697457c560ae565b35049087548135c08c2e265cee524aea6912","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"fd28ced0a83952818697ca5e7d4de32a54114cd514293280e27cad305f3cce23"},"summary":"Decided: the opaque ID and metadata attach to both artifacts and threads","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:45:08.789902Z","id":"c8609bb3e573c88e255c3530123ceae588dcbaf9c16b1ef5709e8093b9cd823c","body":{"detail":"When two different apps speak of the same ID, treat them as the same.  The external integrator can worry about providing unique identifiers for objects of interest","kind":"comment","references":"65a0af16bb7958d42dda0cb6a6131a8d20bfbcd7a6a1405e1e9241c7aa25c0f2","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"4a66b6f70c22aaa7ce411d26e0234264664e774b4993b6a947a0f5e02c71f984"},"summary":"Decided: one external_id names one artifact per instance; the same ID from different apps is the same artifact, and integrators provide unique IDs","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:23:06.926436Z","id":"6541487f6aeb4ad2bcf3e2ba3bb1f0a4a60e36b8306a951032637e68a8c1338d","body":{"detail":"accounts and account IDs are owned by the deployer as are external IDs\n\n1, each clax.dev account is its own deployer\n\nYeah, on clax.dev we shouldn't break the privacy system we've already laid out","kind":"comment","references":"65a0af16bb7958d42dda0cb6a6131a8d20bfbcd7a6a1405e1e9241c7aa25c0f2","summary":"Decided: the scope of one external_id is the deployer; on clax.dev each account is its own deployer, so one account's IDs never name another account's artifact (spec D18)","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T04:23:06.941446Z","id":"b8712b34236b1594b8afa270968bcc5bfcd5c4e2623f2f41e42eaa6e194831a0","body":{"detail":"external_artifacts is unique on (namespace, external_id) (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs, migration 55); crates/clax-server/src/routes/queue_reporter.rs file_report (1b9b10996) passes ExternalScope::Maker on a hosted daemon. Tests: on_a_hosted_clax_each_account_has_its_own_external_ids and on_a_local_clax_one_external_id_is_one_artifact in crates/clax-server/tests/api_queue_reporter.rs, one_external_id_in_two_namespaces_is_two_artifacts in crates/clax-store/src/external.rs.","kind":"comment","references":"3ad50c23725cea95d54adfa052dc83a5234594bec45dd46ea296f292afafa96a","summary":"Narrowed by D18: the shared title, URL, metadata and revision reach only queues of one deployer; on a hosted Clax, only queues of the account that made them","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-29-feedback-loop-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T04:52:53.366158Z","id":"36eb8cbf6e47d0d905c68888ce9e5e82bffb5b3464f4e2134fc538d2ee1cb45f","body":{"detail":"Reporters learn of a proposed fix in the overlay (badge, report view, spec §6.3) and, for the PR, through GitHub's own review request to reporter.github. Webhooks need durable at-least-once delivery with retries on both the daemon and the Worker, a larger piece than this milestone; they are the next step for integrators who want their own channels (Slack, email).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"b7ecf729f70e81e383f26651e2f919451a0d3c33dc1973af279d1c06f5375574"},"summary":"Outbound webhooks (SDK spec §9) left out of the feedback loop","tags":["revisit:an integrator needs reporters told outside the app (email, Slack), or changelist/pathbase adopt the loop","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-29-feedback-loop-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T04:52:53.366218Z","id":"9c7d57ca92a094576fd8d80480e1e6ee58380357adb7af6e814288553704b2b8","body":{"detail":"SDK spec D6 keeps thread metadata opaque. Putting release, commit and flags there would leave every client (triage UI, MCP, CLI, fixers) to guess each integrator's keys. A Clax-defined, versioned context (v: 1), immutable after filing and validated on receipt, lets every client render and act on it; metadata stays the integrator's opaque, editable channel.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":218},"content_hash":"c4dd12821babb6f47e9eb99882eb5f3befe572187f913c849337a0665c544272"},"summary":"Typed report context instead of release/flags inside the opaque thread metadata","tags":["revisit:integrators need context fields v1 cannot express beyond app","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-29-feedback-loop-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T04:52:53.366249Z","id":"752e5053f2835caabd1d657f4901d472fa60c3723a41f7b07f2db398e6c7d385","body":{"detail":"A person flag (feedback) set by an admin through the existing flags API keeps the decision in the integrator's backend, where SDK spec §5.3 puts it, needs no read:org OAuth scope, and is what an outside product would do with its own user records. GitHub org membership would admit every Empathic member automatically.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":375},"end":{"line":381},"content_hash":"de209d27811deb00a19b72d01054c0d9c1acde13334e9d3f8ee3bd82d4ef8058"},"summary":"Gate clax.dev filers on GitHub organisation membership","tags":["revisit:hand-setting the feedback flag for each Empathic person becomes a chore","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-29-feedback-loop-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T04:52:53.366275Z","id":"2328d3cc4aacaff41ee5cfc1767de19ec4a9ebba9c927abba5092415118e7c20","body":{"detail":"A Worker fetching its own hostname is unreliable, so the integrator module builds the same signed request an outside backend sends and hands it to the router in process (SDK spec §4.1 names in-process as a transport). The request, signature and checks are the public route's; only the network hop is skipped.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":382},"end":{"line":400},"content_hash":"0088d908061ea09cb4a35d7b7876dafed1aa87802d1381b9c971a1c50dc9fb8c"},"summary":"clax.dev's token route calls the reporter-tokens route over HTTP instead of in process","tags":["revisit:the integrator module moves out of the instance into a separate service","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:29.643244Z","id":"3931dbc318804949b115b1edd010aef1b1735f52e401c444cb68d1b7354a016a","body":{"detail":"A top-level site has no shell to ask, and the shell would act with the viewer's clax.dev authority on an untrusted page's behalf. The runtime on the artifact's own host is scoped by that host to one artifact.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":259},"content_hash":"c24bb4e91fbf6513374019967ebb3f057427a50bfbe8ad31ac698c788b6a73c0"},"summary":"Keep the page runtime in the clax.dev shell and reach it through postMessage from the framed site","supersedes":"acfbdeeca2690e2db3065621f6182e2c6c3bb1ad53d0e7537adf72ec6da1cf64","tags":["revisit:top-level sites are dropped as a goal","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:29.739608Z","id":"cdb054fa1801c30e5df32393f879a8c4d13e5be73b9c87748d67d21d771523e9","body":{"detail":"The isolation would rest on every query and check being right, next to people, sessions and rights; one app's load and size would fall on the instance everyone shares. A store per artifact makes the boundary structural.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":282},"content_hash":"0779843f0a0e5487ef899f5c000fe650f64b922f1c5c23582b9919d1fa97cc77"},"summary":"Keep app documents in the instance database behind stricter rights checks","supersedes":"8fcbc3a19ccfb7ad79a59540e83d1fc54f183146521f57e9326078b6318454d3","tags":["revisit:per-artifact Durable Objects cost more than the instance can absorb at the artifact counts reached","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:29.842666Z","id":"c645f4a11a4742eacfc093d457e5bfc8c5eb85fb4a9b2ddb5f0c4b497f0e6d80","body":{"detail":"Before the PSL entry ships in browsers, one <id>.clax.run can set Domain=clax.run cookies its siblings receive, and SameSite does not separate them. The platform's own cookies are host-only __Host- names, so this exposes artifacts' own cookies to cookie tossing from a hostile sibling, not clax.dev's session or the site sessions. Accepted because the PSL entry is external and slow and the exposure is bounded to cookies an app sets itself.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":342},"end":{"line":348},"content_hash":"8b91b8b16c6186fd643af9b25e69ad67181009f18d016a7749a0112d9a23503a"},"summary":"Until clax.run is on the Public Suffix List, sibling artifacts are same-site to the browser","supersedes":"b596c329b6eb99f3d0cfbdff72a1ab3d9a1e16501fd2c58a366cdcd0a895f52c","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:29.943877Z","id":"f898e97344380092e235dc413327fe6f9011bbbb63a8b9fc97fcb6f739b06084","body":{"detail":"Section 5.4 sends the top window to /auth/github?next=<artifact path>. A world visitor's page runs on the site domain (site_access, crates/clax-worker), not the public origin, so the session cookie the sign-in sets may not reach the site. Decide whether 5.4 needs a site hand-off (as /_clax/session?code=&next= does in crates/clax-server/src/routes/site.rs:114) before building it.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":296},"end":{"line":299},"content_hash":"ab94da118f6625a5fb156ae214deb696917dd4f5cabaab580d93fd904ef24b77"},"summary":"Hosted account.signIn: does a world visitor's site see the new session after /auth/github, or does it need its own hand-off?","supersedes":"6570249723bdcc404ad1e29204ca3a72b6d1fb30f507a31bb83cb5b28eeb80e4","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.049691Z","id":"9541bb4e7b81ce98e4fdaf3efa190bbbe118662e898930efef58d601986247ee","body":{"detail":"Options: (a) clax.dev is the only default and other origins need {\"account\": {\"origins\": [...]}} in clax.json; (b) any origin, with the shell's consent naming it. (a) keeps a page from steering the owner to an unknown public Clax.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":300},"end":{"line":301},"content_hash":"cff9aee04b7588c837876bc8008a35fd224b78e62b2b6b360decc838fc471697"},"summary":"Local account.signIn: may a page sign in to an origin other than clax.dev when it declares no origins?","supersedes":"9dc784717c2bf6d6e4b7f283d893654dafede15f66f5ebded8099ce2ceb709fd","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.148487Z","id":"1593ed13d52631374f7257cbdad1841753bbd392215b0dfe102d91610c3ec714","body":{"detail":"Without it, a page that only shows \"signed in\" must declare account and so ask for the sign-in permission it never uses.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":302},"end":{"line":302},"content_hash":"38d672f8cda001240d22f9373de6f603c57beffd900f2cd53541967855d7ccaf"},"summary":"Should account.status() work without declaring account, like user.isOwner()?","supersedes":"5258a719fba506da4a479aefda3ce5d368211e19702615d9652093652d139606","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.257601Z","id":"664d7546c03985aa304c8f94fdadededb9e61d8c0e29c0d0b2e711e1191472fc","body":{"detail":"Section 10 pushes new artifacts only (drafts excluded). The idea always-publish is still proposed; this only matters if it is accepted.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":305},"end":{"line":306},"content_hash":"c15948a6dfc1253a0ea3c8abed9d9004b621024bd58fc3221eb3a01951147a6a"},"summary":"Always publish: should turning it on also push existing artifacts?","supersedes":"2e78e26f82d5dd4d76b0efe98b924b89201fa2a8ef4832fae3aacb70238fb1b3","tags":["status:needs-decision","quickstart","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.364856Z","id":"5286eec1f8c9d472c309e0f3e20b27c123546ab66864455d6087aa3bc59ea9e9","body":{"detail":"Rejected by the owner (D2, line 23): the contract is generated from the Rust routes, so it cannot drift from what the server answers, and route auth extractors become the contract's channel and rights fields (§5.2).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":127},"content_hash":"b1848067578525f927b23d7990c501926d6ffa5dac6dc584ea86244d02abe3e9"},"summary":"Write the API contract first (OpenAPI by hand) and generate the Rust route types from it","supersedes":"5b99b3540ad0e7afc06fbb66bf0fe8034627f34b22cc922f88247c2b023711b7","tags":["revisit:a consumer needs a contract change published before the Rust routes for it exist","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.461830Z","id":"9fcc3e74420b904c9a35aa6ebb2c3a8efbceb7786634987275cbe41aab720ad3","body":{"detail":"Not taken: generated bindings bring unsafe code, which AGENTS.md allows only in crates/clax-embed/src/ffi.rs; clients generated from the contract need none.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":155},"end":{"line":167},"content_hash":"eb212cf8e6d3eb1e4b434edc43cff3b37fba939f85b1d414f450a3187832baad"},"summary":"Native SDKs for Swift, Kotlin or Python through FFI bindings (UniFFI) over the Rust client","supersedes":"99ab48a65abb13834d41a1d24a019a6e67b6d84dba9eb282a042fcc35684b6e1","tags":["revisit:a deployer needs a native SDK in a language the contract generator does not cover","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.560146Z","id":"dd0415886f3a615cb72a0ef7d078ce9c38dbfde370c71710592348c062679ac4","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the shell and extension carry bundle budgets, and a wasm core adds its size and an async bridge to every call; a hand-written TS core over generated types keeps modules tree-shakeable. Two cores (TS, Rust) must then agree on retry and signing rules, which the conformance suite in §12 checks.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"c4f7059bbfeedb78dc27f4172528b3f5c402ca462efca90c79bd6961687b0551"},"summary":"Compile the Rust client core to wasm and use it as the TypeScript SDK","supersedes":"71418d389f3d0a37f22e37ed31a8466b3e9aeb087e84861e8cd1e6227b3f439e","tags":["revisit:the TS and Rust client cores disagree on a retry or signing rule that the conformance suite missed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.661052Z","id":"0a7f6ea1a472033202058a170802e9265d2c14fb01d3de800ed315e3fad8b0ef","body":{"detail":"Rejected by the owner (D11, line 45): employees sign in to the deployer's app and nothing else. The cost is that reporters are not Clax people and have no Clax inbox (§7.5).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"846bc412be4958d2af0b74ec88de4b71f527fe1cd89ee9819cf381094ad5a4ce"},"summary":"Each employee signs in to the Clax instance (popup sign-in giving an origin-bound grant) before filing","supersedes":"0110c9b7099de6d4bca54f9e8443a690bd7c6e725d7182711e0198b67867d6a4","tags":["revisit:a deployer needs replies to reach reporters in a Clax inbox rather than the overlay or webhooks","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.758053Z","id":"cfc7c90675047e6af31fd527a362b22566e1933f8a00a1c5fffef573fe185c53","body":{"detail":"Accepted: the service grant reaches one queue, is revocable (ending every token it minted), and is rate-limited; a deployer's backend that misnames employees misattributes reports only within its own queue.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":232},"end":{"line":239},"content_hash":"44e8585e88050c8f77d635b9d848e3406e44bb76ff54a4a90a5ad986006e2c85"},"summary":"Clax trusts the deployer's backend to name reporters: a service grant can mint a token for any reporter_id","supersedes":"9243a5b60d76bdeb02fb5bf64f42e3bd99e0bc9fd941aceea71a941f6bfc9e61","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.856972Z","id":"f562976337bd4f3386c87abc0fa8c5c00dbba8eb1e7b04d80d271a2edcf4cf3a","body":{"detail":"Accepted: metadata is opaque and unencrypted by design (D6); docs/contract.md must say it holds no secrets.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":269},"end":{"line":273},"content_hash":"003a4b1d9692640c0ec1dc637f0dab4eec6aa2c0c3f3d1c560be0b230b42ad11"},"summary":"Artifact metadata is readable by everyone who may read the artifact","supersedes":"e2466608395abdac1f0d1dc1e8b28da717d8e9087a8113b9956045885d8aeb7f","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:30.950737Z","id":"181e90dfdbe57e631fe26c6382d3d8bf6281aaf3a4c981269d5c5ff9ce972714","body":{"detail":"Rejected by the owner (D10, line 41): an agent that stops working without ending its session would hold a report indefinitely; a lease that expires, renewed by working, frees it.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":374},"end":{"line":391},"content_hash":"02d83c491767768560cac301ca3940ac6e4bf6c001d36dcfcc25a644fd94f8be"},"summary":"Claims as today's thread ownership, held until handoff or the claimant's session ends","supersedes":"d45fb772b8491baed40b5463bdf34bb230327dd5f92895cb6d71426d10e61716","tags":["revisit:lease expiry releases reports from agents that are still working on them","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.048001Z","id":"1fb32306f94eb39dc0666e26506e0bd428d82e9822b524fd4c5fb909c3bacbf2","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the browser asks the employee on every capture, against D11 (line 45); DOM-rendered clips need no prompt but can be partial (§8.2).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":418},"end":{"line":429},"content_hash":"61232b045d05c05e20c4b8fdb06f462c20683c681b22cd1c519f56994768a55e"},"summary":"getDisplayMedia screenshots as the overlay's default clip","supersedes":"ce04711fa60dfc91b8967bba245d8178599ace6adb6448cfb457c74cc795780d","tags":["revisit:most clips in a queue are reported partial","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.148862Z","id":"f8be6a52b37f17f5c7dd89e721745309f53278568af4ace71b0edaefa1e281e1","body":{"detail":"Accepted: clips are always taken (D9) without a prompt (D11); what was not rendered is listed with the clip, and the extension's pixel-exact capture is used when it is installed.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":420},"end":{"line":423},"content_hash":"a78daa7b0b8e00c2b450bc6824ef2f38dea7dc294f37b0c95392aa406b26d618"},"summary":"Overlay clips rendered from the DOM can be partial (cross-origin images, canvas, video, cross-origin iframes)","supersedes":"646444811ad2b3f30bbe625f1dadcd176297c6d1334da90ba0cc76c296112968","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.243716Z","id":"87d8bd65c7c418cd0b4a56ef1840d0d54752ad17b4bee7cc2207a7f3121bec84","body":{"detail":"Deferred by the owner (D5, line 31): version 1 keeps current identity systems; reporter tokens minted by the deployer's backend (§5.3) cover filing without a Clax identity.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":458},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"d57e8df1c79607b1e70dfc4ec2addbe90e02b723af407580d7b1af1e26d68141"},"summary":"Deployer-defined identity: OIDC sign-in and RFC 8693 token exchange against the deployer's IdP","supersedes":"5555f8be3529db40978a290318ec89476c3650bb598558166ded7e9641a93367","tags":["revisit:a deployer without a backend (a pure SPA) needs to mint reporter tokens","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.339695Z","id":"eb45f77904811fed4f28186a792c05a1f8f0175ea35f5d119efd8615234b0c16","body":{"detail":"Accepted for version 1: running it in Kubernetes is out of scope (D4), and one replica with a persistent volume is the supported shape.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":460},"content_hash":"397d8aa0be732f8bdee5662903082203c70572dd00e73312b7102ff38628f5a1"},"summary":"A deployer's Clax runs as one replica: the store is SQLite with one writer","supersedes":"247e7c2d5c9e279ae28126dfd443f895453166043eaa5674ad4769c2a6a7704e","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.437562Z","id":"8599ebe4b6b0ba9991c4a1da968aca1197ac7ba70f019d725250eba93189dd79","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner asked for opaque metadata Clax does not interpret (D6, line 33); a schema and an index are only needed once Clax filters by it.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":462},"end":{"line":462},"content_hash":"4660a2ab6bcfdb863d8dd3f20eda5f87cef2cf69bfe528e0b659cb140e638dd2"},"summary":"Registered sources with a JSON Schema for metadata, and queries over metadata","supersedes":"51d3dffb03be4c36530b3e1b4c98c24fc1a46690b34e8f886e8e4820be6300d4","tags":["revisit:an agent or app needs to list reports by a metadata field","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.538636Z","id":"13895b78ae5443b5cc087b00cca7bbbb729e22dd5fc4c31a28b91acd7f7e7253","body":{"detail":"Not now: it needs a migration of the live-page tables, which installed databases have; external artifacts are a new kind beside live instead.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":463},"end":{"line":463},"content_hash":"1ba59b3f3f5075ec0d89d733f34a2b50e0305c59a45fbb75fed5640d62d84968"},"summary":"Make live pages external artifacts of a built-in web source, one model instead of two","supersedes":"23e8857e55120640168b963b530294a7c2020526137c2cdadd9df815ddd2f529","tags":["revisit:a fix has to be made twice, once for live pages and once for external artifacts","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.635916Z","id":"31d6dff06b094e0f75e60ce5dd9bcbc8de34b303e3313cf4275d45f334010271","body":{"detail":"SF Pro matches the web UI on macOS, but Apple's licence limits it to mockups of Apple platforms' UI, and a system font is not hermetic. Inter (SIL OFL 1.1) is fetched by Bazel by checksum.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":255},"end":{"line":265},"content_hash":"ddeb9c082a66708780a7c4345c0452e88f6452e241c0cd3e7ce57a8e8094f801"},"summary":"SF Pro (macOS system font) for the cards, through fframes' load_system_fonts","supersedes":"7a802873dda1afd34244af9f9cd955c3a2941ff806c797264a3871d7a401583e","tags":["revisit:the owner licenses a brand typeface for Clax","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.730770Z","id":"5bd001c24b929903533dbf5bc0f4b2d9db638d8eaf119dc363c742da3dee13db","body":{"detail":"ffmpeg-sys-fframes 9.0.0 reads FFMPEG_BINARIES_URL (file:// accepted), so Bazel could fetch a pinned archive by sha256 and point the build script at it. Not now: the archives are keyed by target and codec features, x264 still links from the system, and the composer is a manual, never-shipped tool.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":410},"end":{"line":425},"content_hash":"fdf0f0e9d95ad98ba718d39e2e937f4fbc9687137642ffc165a143de2569ccf1"},"summary":"A hermetic FFmpeg for the composer (FFMPEG_BINARIES_URL at a checksummed archive Bazel fetches)","supersedes":"aae1bcc51151b4b3008757427f6ae6492035820ac30558d3defd983eecbb36c9","tags":["revisit:a reel render in CI fails or differs because of the downloaded FFmpeg, or the composer moves into a gating target","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.824928Z","id":"63177fcdbf7321f34a8045688f6604ed431f711d5f6ea6194bd9cc223ea8b760","body":{"detail":"A cargo genrule is simpler and avoids crate_universe annotations for ffmpeg-sys-fframes' build script, but it bypasses Bazel's cache keys for the crate graph, writes a cargo target directory of gigabytes outside Bazel's bounds (docs/bazel.md 'Disk'), and is the cargo build in a worktree AGENTS.md avoids.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":410},"end":{"line":425},"content_hash":"fdf0f0e9d95ad98ba718d39e2e937f4fbc9687137642ffc165a143de2569ccf1"},"summary":"Building the composer with cargo in a genrule (shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR outside the worktree) instead of a second crate_universe hub","supersedes":"8d3bfd5cd67b191fb45fb3dc74078aa6b7285494e16116b53d0305d4787e8a38","tags":["revisit:@reel_crates makes bazel query //... fetch fframes' sources, or ffmpeg-sys-fframes' build script cannot run under rules_rust's cargo_build_script","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:31.924684Z","id":"06c98d0521f0630d0bfeb481394a650db545741a7b66dc6d2d8252b4b1f15698","body":{"detail":"fframes 1.3.0 composites video frames itself (Frame::get_synced_video_frame with DynamicMediaProvider::with_video, https://docs.rs/fframes/1.3.0/fframes/), so one fframes Video renders cards, transitions and clips in one encode. A separate ffmpeg binary would be a second unpinned tool on macOS arm64, where no checksummed static build is published.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":427},"end":{"line":448},"content_hash":"144e3c058c73dd5b4b674898b6b7fb3a9b72f05cbcb582a712aa96a15922c453"},"summary":"An ffmpeg command line (pinned binary) to join clips, with fframes only for cards","supersedes":"22152b869de4f686eb75a2519bffdf840be9580467841a1cad6921339955a27c","tags":["revisit:fframes cannot decode a vignette clip's frames in sync, or its memory for one composition exceeds 8 GB","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:32.020010Z","id":"ba764409929c2cc1302b380bc5dc9cd18a3afe5eaae76362b1aecf81708d223b","body":{"detail":"The owner's installed Clax already holds the clax.dev sign-in and the link to the public copy; asset upload, publish and push through it reuse tested paths, including the asset address rewrite, and keep the public artifact's URL stable. A direct client would need its own token handling.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":624},"end":{"line":643},"content_hash":"17f214ca9ce105eada46013bea07c26d3b7276c608b804e8a10b3bed2e86fefe"},"summary":"reel-upload talking to clax.dev's API directly with a token of its own","supersedes":"f23a22f70a158cf4b6d4a6b8f591142cffcdce3a90c13337183e167df686077d","tags":["revisit:the landing artifact is no longer published from a local artifact the owner's Clax links","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:32.115424Z","id":"474cc4956820d84c4d9d833695ef05bb437265d04f604905387af40d99ca827b","body":{"detail":"A poster is a build output of the reel, which is never committed, and the binary carries only web/quickstart's SHIPPED files. Seeded copies show a link card in the page's own styles instead.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":665},"end":{"line":705},"content_hash":"57720b87bdba4cedafb03873842b9eae5e2cd5618d42214ea6dfc6cb8558a74b"},"summary":"Shipping a still poster image in the binary so seeded quickstarts show a frame of the reel","supersedes":"d89cad9596a83f77a6bbe7f3b5511d3d34dc0e7e4417afb7aa2edcf60f485915","tags":["revisit:the owner wants seeded galleries to show a picture of the reel","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:32.211292Z","id":"4d52f8459b522c9456ed4e7613fd6d1315724765c6cf11553d3abd743ce68967","body":{"detail":"A published file is capped at 16 MiB (file_too_large) and is kept again in every version's content; an asset (20 MiB cap) lives outside versions and the push uploads it once (docs/contract.md 'Pushing'). Only reel.json, the small pointer, and reel.gif are files.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":665},"end":{"line":705},"content_hash":"57720b87bdba4cedafb03873842b9eae5e2cd5618d42214ea6dfc6cb8558a74b"},"summary":"Publishing the video as a file of each landing-page version instead of an asset","supersedes":"65f0a3fa136fde57366832ea363e0a5a290c36a022e7db3bac7b1f9335e44fbc","tags":["revisit:asset storage on clax.dev is limited or priced per asset","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:32.316071Z","id":"9d61b8206d9ed2397766d6f352cdbcab31aa736211fef281ac427cd87fc31665","body":{"detail":"A stable URL, but it changes only at releases, 404s when a release lacks the asset, and goes through a redirect GitHub's image proxy may not follow. The landing artifact's reel.gif changes with every upload.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":707},"end":{"line":729},"content_hash":"a2649a35e6acacb4356a3c04b6060aaf13d38320a18a68eff2515a758ddabad3"},"summary":"Hosting the README GIF as releases/latest/download/clax-reel.gif","supersedes":"53652064c92db2cf3a4a71d71a5532312c21b5ccdc2a4ec9f8817a1500530f30","tags":["revisit:the landing artifact's site cannot serve reel.gif to GitHub's image proxy (spec R7)","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:32.410628Z","id":"8118f41323379e061090c4bca6675fe00ac07f535ac99820b9dbf7605b2da186","body":{"detail":"It is uploaded only by hand in GitHub's editor (no API), and its URL changes per upload, so the README would change at every upload. The linked GIF published as reel.gif on the landing artifact keeps one URL across uploads. Open question Q5.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":707},"end":{"line":729},"content_hash":"a2649a35e6acacb4356a3c04b6060aaf13d38320a18a68eff2515a758ddabad3"},"summary":"A GitHub user-attachment MP4 in the README, which plays inline","supersedes":"41e51ea8b24f99a7c97679a4bd1347946be8584cde10e78fdba2ec01c8733744","tags":["revisit:the owner answers Q5 for inline playback","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:54.264468Z","id":"f7b1756d91d5a053717fb0726db67ee087d7f9661051f8bbbc1077008e9423a0","body":{"detail":"A site served at its host's root cannot carry a key in every root-relative URL, and any URL credential leaks through copies, history and logs and outlives a revoked right until it expires. A server-side site session checked on every request ends with the right.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":209},"content_hash":"3a1ebc2522b94640d860ffff31e3c29b209bc0f5b0d9eecd02ee0389478b1cc2"},"summary":"Expiring signed URLs (a short-lived key in the path or query) as the credential for private content","supersedes":"77e156cc37f42481ca98b7304962d75d82d2f8d1d057d7ccd87a2cda645c3489","tags":["revisit:a site needs to be embedded where no cookie can be set or sent","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:54.369536Z","id":"b021034cea75f94acfa215aef0f66353065f4338c878f371209c9f7dea5b4604","body":{"detail":"Accepted (D17, line 58): an ID names one artifact per instance and integrators choose unique IDs; each queue's threads stay its own (lines 344-347), so only the artifact-level fields are shared. On clax.dev two deployers that pick the same ID see and can edit each other's artifact metadata.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":351},"end":{"line":357},"content_hash":"61f93ee664e6c71c0c40768a539d0fe2569ff7b4a1f3aea817002da9374f01c6"},"summary":"Integrators that reuse one external_id share the artifact's title, URL, metadata and revision across their queues","supersedes":"3ad50c23725cea95d54adfa052dc83a5234594bec45dd46ea296f292afafa96a","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:54.472389Z","id":"d0c2863a428c5ffb3fc13de54a561b3e70b619418caf4dcfb7b8e9117ec47e0d","body":{"detail":"Live layers between people are exercised on a hosted daemon today (web/e2e/live-layers.spec.ts, presence.spec.ts: a local daemon's browsers are all its owner). LAN people would show the local shell's chrome exactly, but no test proves live layers there.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"bbc26b490450c9564df7f5fea5771c77ff0156c7af437b3ac7be35eeb8b38aea"},"summary":"A LAN person (people-helpers connect) instead of a hosted daemon for the realtime vignette","supersedes":"0197dfa08a37bb5dc57b84a0f46b907776a6e69524d5e2175036181875e69046","tags":["revisit:the hosted shell's chrome reads differently from a local one in the realtime or share vignette","reel","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:36:03.289833Z","id":"a74bccd6d57a9aa4aa856096719a0c10921ae16f564b2458a662593ccefa4cb4","body":{"detail":"Chosen by the owner, 2026-10-26, over skipping approval of their own first versions. Spec section 7 now says a first version's declaration always needs approval.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"comment","references":"aafa9274d005fc0f50a3a4a5e37abb67e3b6d24f8f7cb72b031a7b4c23cd4906","span":{"start":{"line":301},"end":{"line":302},"content_hash":"77a20b83ad5aeae68e18048480e891f3926f21157ba7e7da630630feca8e3091"},"summary":"Decided: every artifact asks once, the owner's and their agents' included.","supersedes":"f6252ef5e0b1dc01730fc0a149997414103aa7964a2f1aa10996ab0b996d69c4","tags":["status:decided","quickstart","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:36:03.400389Z","id":"6b7d66978757ae6f6d41f2a2ff9b842e4947b2357fc4295a6bc9165e82f3b6fa","body":{"detail":"Chosen by the owner, 2026-10-26, so comments never point at elements a release moved. Spec section 9 updated.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"comment","references":"f53d89149e185e2faaa06768b621d9832e3e9dcff692dac93278487390ffdf0b","span":{"start":{"line":303},"end":{"line":305},"content_hash":"0ededdb1bb4f7a187b554d384c9efc4c3951e96ad47209d4796296cf45b5be0a"},"summary":"Decided: the seeded quickstart stops following releases at the person's first activity on it, a comment or a change.","supersedes":"efe20b4db9141b3d32debbe01e3295a479e662d3d38d717ef1d5504b5d9356d7","tags":["status:decided","quickstart","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-29-feedback-loop-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:40:27.394933Z","id":"2251cf775e6568ca87ea24a9a6bfbbb6d3fe8b6a9e1b8a8bcac0d036d5cdce81","body":{"detail":"Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+B is the browsers' own bookmarks bar (Chrome), Library (Firefox) and Favorites bar (Safari) key, so the shell binds plain F outside text fields and dialogs instead, matching its unmodified C and ? keys and forwarded from the artifact frame like C (web/shell/src/view/keys.ts, web/bridge/src/channel.ts). Shift+F is refused in both. There is no account menu, so a header menu (web/shell/src/feedback/FeedbackMenu.svelte) holds Report a problem and My reports.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":403},"end":{"line":406},"content_hash":"28164815812d0a39e5dc18fd2dfcdfd6a3ab198d004523eb9562fa7c54458a58"},"summary":"Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+B as the shell's report shortcut","tags":["revisit:the shell gains an account menu or a single-key shortcut clashes with an artifact's own keys","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-29-feedback-loop-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:40:27.394999Z","id":"da110c440edb797077915fcfb63fca6effce0ea6ac151ecf2ac5c480c0e86460","body":{"detail":"Milestone 1 reopened a resolved report on a reporter comment. A comment never changes a queue report's state now; only the reopen route (Still broken) does, with its own note, capture and diagnostics, so a reopen is always deliberate and its evidence is kept per capture (crates/clax-store/src/queues.rs). A reporter replying on a resolved report presses Still broken to reopen it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":291},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"0e5608b0a8831a7909081b0becef898e4d7cea1f135e5af3e60730b643f1ec7c"},"summary":"A reporter's comment reopening a resolved or verified report","tags":["revisit:reporters reply on resolved reports expecting them to reopen","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-29-feedback-loop-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T04:48:00.347905Z","id":"2f40a03bb9a40e428fd7a7ac23777557196b402d4c71ba26f645c3f064c12581","body":{"detail":"The owner chose that every signed-in person reports (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-29-feedback-loop-design.md §10.1, crates/clax-server/src/integrations/feedback.rs filer).","kind":"comment","references":"752e5053f2835caabd1d657f4901d472fa60c3723a41f7b07f2db398e6c7d385","summary":"Since e70e638a8 §10.1 lets every signed-in person file, with no flag; a GitHub organisation gate would now narrow that rather than replace a flag","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:40.419448Z","id":"fdea2f1b3f207ec0893c3433777682b8d9805519753abf8ae6bcc74074063b83","body":{"detail":"Rejected by the owner (D11, line 45): employees sign in to the deployer's app and nothing else. The cost is that reporters are not Clax people and have no Clax inbox (§7.5).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":260},"content_hash":"9758c7c819ccffad3ad479d2144815a1df42ae96f2541185e4717ec5cf254dc9"},"summary":"Each employee signs in to the Clax instance (popup sign-in giving an origin-bound grant) before filing","supersedes":"0a7f6ea1a472033202058a170802e9265d2c14fb01d3de800ed315e3fad8b0ef","tags":["revisit:a deployer needs replies to reach reporters in a Clax inbox rather than the overlay or webhooks","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:40.547947Z","id":"da054c98ecc258f92c5dce93e571130e31c463da280a90e32072f39a252c3d83","body":{"detail":"Accepted: the service grant reaches one queue, is revocable (ending every token it minted), and is rate-limited; a deployer's backend that misnames employees misattributes reports only within its own queue.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":249},"end":{"line":256},"content_hash":"44e8585e88050c8f77d635b9d848e3406e44bb76ff54a4a90a5ad986006e2c85"},"summary":"Clax trusts the deployer's backend to name reporters: a service grant can mint a token for any reporter_id","supersedes":"cfc7c90675047e6af31fd527a362b22566e1933f8a00a1c5fffef573fe185c53","tags":["session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:40.679937Z","id":"7e0ee02bc7d7734f253ca03e26277500382b579fcab3a75ddd218fabb9264388","body":{"detail":"Accepted: metadata is opaque and unencrypted by design (D6); docs/contract.md must say it holds no secrets.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":286},"end":{"line":290},"content_hash":"003a4b1d9692640c0ec1dc637f0dab4eec6aa2c0c3f3d1c560be0b230b42ad11"},"summary":"Artifact metadata is readable by everyone who may read the artifact","supersedes":"f562976337bd4f3386c87abc0fa8c5c00dbba8eb1e7b04d80d271a2edcf4cf3a","tags":["session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:40.851318Z","id":"4d0ec71c71a17162abb257c76b566a90e29ddabef0400e8c4f5857aa27b959a6","body":{"detail":"Rejected by the owner (D10, line 41): an agent that stops working without ending its session would hold a report indefinitely; a lease that expires, renewed by working, frees it.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":391},"end":{"line":408},"content_hash":"02d83c491767768560cac301ca3940ac6e4bf6c001d36dcfcc25a644fd94f8be"},"summary":"Claims as today's thread ownership, held until handoff or the claimant's session ends","supersedes":"181e90dfdbe57e631fe26c6382d3d8bf6281aaf3a4c981269d5c5ff9ce972714","tags":["revisit:lease expiry releases reports from agents that are still working on them","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:41.142595Z","id":"776b09ddd96c49d65c2cd152f7e084c1c99617142d399c8aab83b409917dcaae","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the browser asks the employee on every capture, against D11 (line 45); DOM-rendered clips need no prompt but can be partial (§8.2).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":435},"end":{"line":446},"content_hash":"61232b045d05c05e20c4b8fdb06f462c20683c681b22cd1c519f56994768a55e"},"summary":"getDisplayMedia screenshots as the overlay's default clip","supersedes":"1fb32306f94eb39dc0666e26506e0bd428d82e9822b524fd4c5fb909c3bacbf2","tags":["revisit:most clips in a queue are reported partial","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:41.496119Z","id":"d99008442e195932834c2163b53aacdce97641c308488f763732e1df142a0a60","body":{"detail":"Accepted: clips are always taken (D9) without a prompt (D11); what was not rendered is listed with the clip, and the extension's pixel-exact capture is used when it is installed.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":437},"end":{"line":440},"content_hash":"a78daa7b0b8e00c2b450bc6824ef2f38dea7dc294f37b0c95392aa406b26d618"},"summary":"Overlay clips rendered from the DOM can be partial (cross-origin images, canvas, video, cross-origin iframes)","supersedes":"f8be6a52b37f17f5c7dd89e721745309f53278568af4ace71b0edaefa1e281e1","tags":["session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:41.845807Z","id":"35a75e2810253af1d9f97a07ab7a26be500704537c90f1ab6dfad61c171fb679","body":{"detail":"Deferred by the owner (D5, line 31): version 1 keeps current identity systems; reporter tokens minted by the deployer's backend (§5.3) cover filing without a Clax identity.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":475},"end":{"line":475},"content_hash":"d57e8df1c79607b1e70dfc4ec2addbe90e02b723af407580d7b1af1e26d68141"},"summary":"Deployer-defined identity: OIDC sign-in and RFC 8693 token exchange against the deployer's IdP","supersedes":"87d8bd65c7c418cd0b4a56ef1840d0d54752ad17b4bee7cc2207a7f3121bec84","tags":["revisit:a deployer without a backend (a pure SPA) needs to mint reporter tokens","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:42.194285Z","id":"6f37f866edc09de5432f68ed7780540650c1bf52d4e3c6b4d37eb6b9ff6d6498","body":{"detail":"Accepted for version 1: running it in Kubernetes is out of scope (D4), and one replica with a persistent volume is the supported shape.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":476},"end":{"line":477},"content_hash":"397d8aa0be732f8bdee5662903082203c70572dd00e73312b7102ff38628f5a1"},"summary":"A deployer's Clax runs as one replica: the store is SQLite with one writer","supersedes":"eb45f77904811fed4f28186a792c05a1f8f0175ea35f5d119efd8615234b0c16","tags":["session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:42.469496Z","id":"b366fac37e9a5e180bdae58d81edd9c9ab92c8456d2de890c51922fd3b9caf83","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner asked for opaque metadata Clax does not interpret (D6, line 33); a schema and an index are only needed once Clax filters by it.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":479},"end":{"line":479},"content_hash":"4660a2ab6bcfdb863d8dd3f20eda5f87cef2cf69bfe528e0b659cb140e638dd2"},"summary":"Registered sources with a JSON Schema for metadata, and queries over metadata","supersedes":"8599ebe4b6b0ba9991c4a1da968aca1197ac7ba70f019d725250eba93189dd79","tags":["revisit:an agent or app needs to list reports by a metadata field","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:42.783415Z","id":"571bbe7479f0abb0cf440883a0536f87f4d888a3aaa5fbf326e551487a923b72","body":{"detail":"Not now: it needs a migration of the live-page tables, which installed databases have; external artifacts are a new kind beside live instead.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":480},"end":{"line":480},"content_hash":"1ba59b3f3f5075ec0d89d733f34a2b50e0305c59a45fbb75fed5640d62d84968"},"summary":"Make live pages external artifacts of a built-in web source, one model instead of two","supersedes":"13895b78ae5443b5cc087b00cca7bbbb729e22dd5fc4c31a28b91acd7f7e7253","tags":["revisit:a fix has to be made twice, once for live pages and once for external artifacts","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:46:43.161451Z","id":"d6ba7979fed29240e3a9bab07d745c430436bb0e4164fbdaed1c8f9edf2418d9","body":{"detail":"Accepted (D17, line 58): an ID names one artifact per instance and integrators choose unique IDs; each queue's threads stay its own (lines 344-347), so only the artifact-level fields are shared. On clax.dev two deployers that pick the same ID see and can edit each other's artifact metadata.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf)'s record.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged after the fixes of the review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02 SDK findings moved its lines; first recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":368},"end":{"line":374},"content_hash":"61f93ee664e6c71c0c40768a539d0fe2569ff7b4a1f3aea817002da9374f01c6"},"summary":"Integrators that reuse one external_id share the artifact's title, URL, metadata and revision across their queues","supersedes":"b021034cea75f94acfa215aef0f66353065f4338c878f371209c9f7dea5b4604","tags":["session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:33:52.175499Z","id":"2115adaa62c5fcf8732f4ac10e8e6c986d780ffb45a851502e39abd67aa0b163","body":{"detail":"Under every UrlRule, a planted page can list many links (?d=a, ?d=b, ...) and the model can leak data by which it fetches; the per-run fetch cap (web.max_fetches_per_run) bounds it. Search queries are model-written text sent to the provider (Ceramic, Exa or Linkup). Accepted as the owner's call per this spec's §5.4; the Settings page must say so beside the web switches. Anthropic's web_fetch leaves the same channels open (https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/web-fetch-tool, URL validation).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":349},"content_hash":"9fb2f5536d0a953e11c1be9b7d9fc745b3ee9ce7abc0983ca1d6dc4d4c509fa5"},"summary":"Fetch link choice and search query text remain exfiltration channels","tags":["security","claxbot-web","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:33:52.175584Z","id":"7e8463c56426158d4322e3cc5afb767ba10d8ba3cd100ac1d7299a481d8b41af","body":{"detail":"ClaxBot would read only what it searched for or the sender linked, closing the link-choice channel of §5.4 at the cost of following links. Not in v1: Sourced already refuses every model-written URL, and following links is the common case.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":603},"end":{"line":607},"content_hash":"c5140471d5dfdc4c8fe9667c1ad7574e368b28a474f41fef9db41a5e57b8b0be"},"summary":"A UrlRule without fetched pages as a source","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:an instance admin asks for web use without link following, or an exfiltration through fetched-page links is reported","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:33:52.175625Z","id":"3eeda13836f566edb2b83c3f48626e5a588934304588a320ccc1805776f1dd3e","body":{"detail":"Refused in §5.2: a version is what an earlier run or any agent published, so one run could publish a URL carrying private data and a later run fetch it. Counting only versions a person published by hand was also considered; Clax does not record whether a version's text was written by a person or their agent.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":608},"end":{"line":610},"content_hash":"a5a275426ad8015fc0759c0f3238cc26b765ae73351b60a9218ffdb8a20e5067"},"summary":"The published artifact as a source of fetchable URLs","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:people ask ClaxBot to check their page's links often enough that pasting them into a comment is a burden","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:33:52.175659Z","id":"68234c9eea5f884cd064564fffa0f361363593e4426f94f496085d5afcb6074d","body":{"detail":"Little code (ClaxBot already speaks the Messages API), but $10 per thousand searches against Ceramic's $0.25, Anthropic's API only, billed to a person's own key when they use one, and outside the call journal and the URL rule of §5.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":592},"end":{"line":597},"content_hash":"6805210480dfc3078e60fd2a51961a57c40284edb50f1ca3a53bda9a47438737"},"summary":"Anthropic's server-side web_search/web_fetch as the web source","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:an instance runs only on Anthropic's API and its admin prefers it to configuring Cloudflare","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:33:52.175692Z","id":"3b57e0de3e72d98dc9c3d6729a3f205282f9f152f1bc81775e6491b34369b6e4","body":{"detail":"The Worker is Rust compiled to wasm; the package adds a JavaScript bundling step to its build and gives the daemon nothing. Its request checks, windowing, snippet trimming and error codes are ported to Rust in clax-bot (§4.3).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":589},"end":{"line":591},"content_hash":"31793ac147f66f6524601d5255a4672637124fb8dee3154d0e47be0c765e2ad3"},"summary":"Cloudflare's npm agents package (agents/webfetch, agents/websearch) in the Worker","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:the package gains behaviour too large to port, such as new content conversions","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:33:52.175725Z","id":"6fb079d00731c25515f239d291f67b36ff7d2adc9367560944c860a470429306","body":{"detail":"Would save fetch charges, but one person's fetches could be inferred from another's results and timing. v1 keeps pages per run only (§6.2).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":598},"end":{"line":600},"content_hash":"a3d426a53584803cf95483f6e7ab193d69f1c895ab82ccb5641d8376b1ca2d3b"},"summary":"A fetch cache shared across runs","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:web.fetch spending is a material share of an instance's ClaxBot costs","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:12.010199Z","id":"96edb7dc9bfb6750bcf32cf60c5b986646adf1f39478da73acc7881083b85a3e","body":{"detail":"Under every UrlRule, a planted page can list many links (?d=a, ?d=b, ...) and the model can leak data by which it fetches; the per-run fetch cap (web.max_fetches_per_run) bounds it. Search queries are model-written text sent to the provider (Ceramic, Exa or Linkup). Accepted as the owner's call per this spec's §5.4; the Settings page must say so beside the web switches. Anthropic's web_fetch leaves the same channels open (https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/web-fetch-tool, URL validation).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":341},"end":{"line":357},"content_hash":"9fb2f5536d0a953e11c1be9b7d9fc745b3ee9ce7abc0983ca1d6dc4d4c509fa5"},"summary":"Fetch link choice and search query text remain exfiltration channels","supersedes":"2115adaa62c5fcf8732f4ac10e8e6c986d780ffb45a851502e39abd67aa0b163","tags":["security","claxbot-web","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:12.140770Z","id":"85355066917fb616ddcd99e8c33f353c97ec0dc57ec6fa08d8d2279a0616036b","body":{"detail":"The Worker is Rust compiled to wasm; the package adds a JavaScript bundling step to its build and gives the daemon nothing. Its request checks, windowing, snippet trimming and error codes are ported to Rust in clax-bot (§4.3).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":610},"end":{"line":612},"content_hash":"31793ac147f66f6524601d5255a4672637124fb8dee3154d0e47be0c765e2ad3"},"summary":"Cloudflare's npm agents package (agents/webfetch, agents/websearch) in the Worker","supersedes":"3b57e0de3e72d98dc9c3d6729a3f205282f9f152f1bc81775e6491b34369b6e4","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:the package gains behaviour too large to port, such as new content conversions","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:12.271669Z","id":"a3d49c56758ef9ab51ce029be6795a63b6f2652d07fe3ea91da1334ec06a8ec4","body":{"detail":"Little code (ClaxBot already speaks the Messages API), but $10 per thousand searches against Ceramic's $0.25, Anthropic's API only, billed to a person's own key when they use one, and outside the call journal and the URL rule of §5.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":613},"end":{"line":618},"content_hash":"6805210480dfc3078e60fd2a51961a57c40284edb50f1ca3a53bda9a47438737"},"summary":"Anthropic's server-side web_search/web_fetch as the web source","supersedes":"68234c9eea5f884cd064564fffa0f361363593e4426f94f496085d5afcb6074d","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:an instance runs only on Anthropic's API and its admin prefers it to configuring Cloudflare","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:12.402646Z","id":"f59f71c36f09f9a3b692c40c6be67f968b8e104d880d6eea0ebb50f803690493","body":{"detail":"Would save fetch charges, but one person's fetches could be inferred from another's results and timing. v1 keeps pages per run only (§6.2).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":619},"end":{"line":621},"content_hash":"a3d426a53584803cf95483f6e7ab193d69f1c895ab82ccb5641d8376b1ca2d3b"},"summary":"A fetch cache shared across runs","supersedes":"6fb079d00731c25515f239d291f67b36ff7d2adc9367560944c860a470429306","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:web.fetch spending is a material share of an instance's ClaxBot costs","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:12.534639Z","id":"d7300126dc0a98914db60810f8b68eb68d3afd792a8142343742e85f493cae42","body":{"detail":"ClaxBot would read only what it searched for or the sender linked, closing the link-choice channel of §5.4 at the cost of following links. Not in v1: Sourced already refuses every model-written URL, and following links is the common case.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":624},"end":{"line":628},"content_hash":"c5140471d5dfdc4c8fe9667c1ad7574e368b28a474f41fef9db41a5e57b8b0be"},"summary":"A UrlRule without fetched pages as a source","supersedes":"7e8463c56426158d4322e3cc5afb767ba10d8ba3cd100ac1d7299a481d8b41af","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:an instance admin asks for web use without link following, or an exfiltration through fetched-page links is reported","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T07:58:12.665021Z","id":"bee6b339f0cab448877ef2d660e81d2e2ce369d9f1555b247867ea5845a11a9e","body":{"detail":"Refused in §5.2: a version is what an earlier run or any agent published, so one run could publish a URL carrying private data and a later run fetch it. Counting only versions a person published by hand was also considered; Clax does not record whether a version's text was written by a person or their agent.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":629},"end":{"line":631},"content_hash":"a5a275426ad8015fc0759c0f3238cc26b765ae73351b60a9218ffdb8a20e5067"},"summary":"The published artifact as a source of fetchable URLs","supersedes":"3eeda13836f566edb2b83c3f48626e5a588934304588a320ccc1805776f1dd3e","tags":["claxbot-web","revisit:people ask ClaxBot to check their page's links often enough that pasting them into a comment is a burden","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-11-04T05:40:37.914861Z","id":"d3622b29c4fac2f64be51d2e788affbcc35526821d8c031776a4ccb59d621d5c","body":{"detail":"I accept that the bot can leak information given every other bot people use has this issue as well","kind":"comment","references":"96edb7dc9bfb6750bcf32cf60c5b986646adf1f39478da73acc7881083b85a3e","summary":"Decided: accepted. A fetch's link choice and a search's query text stay open as exfiltration channels, bounded by the per-run caps, as in other bots that search and fetch.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T05:05:01.708163Z","id":"dccc4f801d04a2fd4359f18fd4db2a5266d435ed6f6a7762740dd13de81f4a50","body":{"detail":"`OpSpec::args_schema`, `result_schema` and the `schema` function under them were deleted from crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs with `OPS` and `Ty`: nothing outside that file's own tests called them (`git grep -n 'args_schema\\|result_schema'` found api.rs alone). `clax-surface` has no JSON Schema output. The manifest notation (\"Two notations\", step 3 of \"Steps\") therefore starts from nothing in the tree; the deleted function is the mapping it described (integer, number, string enum, `prefixItems` with `minItems`/`maxItems`, `additionalProperties: false`, `anyOf`), in the history of crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs before the commit \"refactor(claxbot): the script API is read from clax.d.ts\".","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":226},"content_hash":"ce0c41edbc25d58c73bc5e027f5c2f6bb5eff109a5042822b3bce7338d951242"},"summary":"`OpSpec::args_schema`, which this paragraph says already writes the manifest's subset of JSON Schema, no longer exists","tags":["claxbot-surfaces","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T05:37:41.317155Z","id":"212ae9d81eeb473fb6821a8f801a64c2cec396bdd6cd309b33f697ca80515d80","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs no longer has `Ty`, `Field`, `Param` or `OPS`: the types are `clax_surface::Ty`'s and the operations are crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts. Lines that describe them as present: this document :15 (`one table of operations (crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs, OPS)`), :179 (`Types are those api::Ty has`), :226 (`OpSpec::args_schema`, record dccc4f80); docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md:92-95 (`OpSpec`: its name, parameters, result type …, where `OpSpec` now holds name, access, performer, errors and the definition's operation). Lines :601 and :1023 say the file replaces `OPS`, which is now done, and docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools.md:367 is a finished plan's step.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":182},"content_hash":"a6dca116138777418328da16d2d0c913bd37d7fbeadaec7a670725e1596edca0"},"suggested_fix":"Name `clax_surface::Ty` at :179 and say at :15 what the table was; point the web-tools design at clax.d.ts.","summary":"The design still says types are those `api::Ty` has and that the operations are a table `OPS`, neither of which exists","tags":["claxbot-surfaces","docs","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T06:03:09.305948Z","id":"6d5adec73799f7ca216bdfb103d018f50135addbc81cd2d2884ba1e882a5907e","body":{"detail":"Commit \"docs(claxbot): the surfaces design speaks of the operation table as gone\". \"Intent\" now names crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts and says the table `OPS` came before it; \"Types are those `clax_surface::Ty` has, which the operation table's `api::Ty` had before it\"; \"`crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts` has replaced `OPS` and its `Ty` statics\"; step 1 reads \"`clax.d.ts` has replaced `OPS`\". Nothing else in the document changed (`git diff` of the commit: 14 lines added, 9 removed).\n\nNot changed: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md:92-95, which still describes `OpSpec` as holding a name, parameters and a result type. `OpSpec` is now `performer` and `operation` (crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs:150), with `name()`, `access()` and `errors()` read from the operation.","kind":"comment","references":"212ae9d81eeb473fb6821a8f801a64c2cec396bdd6cd309b33f697ca80515d80","summary":"Brought up to date in this document: lines 14-16, 180-181, 606 and 1027-1028 speak of `OPS` and `api::Ty` as gone. The web-tools design's lines are untouched. Left open for the owner to close","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T06:03:09.306306Z","id":"40d0e0425883061b75314ec92478350543c15a281af302a8d8a03e8914373283","body":{"detail":"Commit \"docs(claxbot): the surfaces design speaks of the operation table as gone\". Lines 227-231 of the document: \"Nothing in the tree writes that subset: the manifest notation needs a schema writer of its own. (`OpSpec::args_schema` wrote it from the operation table, and was deleted with the table; it is in the history of `crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs`.)\" Step 3 of \"Steps\" is unchanged and still has that writer to build.","kind":"comment","references":"dccc4f801d04a2fd4359f18fd4db2a5266d435ed6f6a7762740dd13de81f4a50","summary":"The paragraph now says that nothing in the tree writes the manifest's subset of JSON Schema and that the manifest notation needs a writer of its own. Left open for the owner to close","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T06:54:11.166524Z","id":"bb66b1ceb9bc0bb0073b1501051bf2b166c61b8b1c086dcf84dc0348d6ea3299","body":{"detail":"The paragraph says the manifest's shape is the one another repository's proposal gave (`service`, `version`, `ops` with `name`, `kind`, `doc`, `args`, `returns`, and `types`). As built (crates/clax-surface/src/lib.rs, \"The manifest notation\"): `clax_surface` is the version of the notation, not of the surface, which has none (line 225 names a definition by its hash), and `name` is the surface's; `operations` for `ops`, with `description`, `access`, `params` and `result`, the words the `.d.ts` notation and `clax_surface::Op` use, and `waits`, `once` and `throws`; a namespace with rules, or with no member, has an entry of its own in `operations`, since a flat list of dotted names cannot place it otherwise; `interfaces` for `types`, since only an interface has a name (`$ref: \"#/interfaces/Name\"`) and the checks' words then fit both notations; `extends` for the interfaces one extends; `additionalProperties: false` is required of every object type, and a schema without it is refused, not read as closed. An MCP tool takes one object and an operation positional parameters: one parameter `args` of an interface made from `inputSchema`. The table's row at line 219 lists `$ref: \"clax:Int\"`: it is read, and `Int` is written `{\"type\": \"integer\"}`. Of the commands (line 807): `check` prints the first mistake, as `clax_surface::parse` finds one, not \"the errors\"; and both commands take `--own`, which reads a file as Clax's own surface, so that crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts can be checked and converted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"ef9a73469685233e4ffa4e2a667a15e009121df0c0b882926cbd5679b16c11db"},"summary":"The manifest as built does not have the shape this paragraph says it has, and the commands differ from the design's table in two places: for the owner to confirm, and the text to follow","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T07:22:06.403084Z","id":"416c43092926f0d79cfb831a8e7abb6a97e4a9e0c6d75e5ae081498ae50b1470","body":{"detail":"The names as built are the better ones. `access` for the proposal's `kind`, which here already means a request kind; `description` for `doc`, as JSON Schema and MCP say it; `params` and `result` as the model and the `.d.ts` notation say them; `interfaces` for `types`, so that `$ref` is a real JSON Pointer into the document, where the proposal's `#/types/Window[]` was not; `clax_surface: 1` names the document and its version in one member, and cannot be taken for a version of the surface. `extends` as a keyword of the notation's own is right for the reason record edbccb1f gives. `params` as a list keeps positions, which a call has. Namespaces as entries of `operations`, with members that must follow one another, is the strict reading, and it can be loosened later without breaking a manifest, where the reverse cannot; the refusal names the namespace and the entry. What to settle now: (1) the manifest's bound on its text (concern on crates/clax-surface/src/manifest.rs:1614-1622: a `.d.ts` of 23 KiB has no manifest); (2) what bytes are hashed (concern on crates/clax-surface/src/manifest.rs:1505-1511); (3) an operation's `name` is dotted below the surface (`settings.set`) while `allow`, every message and `clax bot surface check --ops` name it with the surface (`shell.settings.set`): a manifest with `\"name\": \"demo\"` and an operation named `demo.f` is read, without a word, as `demo.demo.f`. A rule that a surface holds no member of its own name, in both notations, would catch it. On `check` printing the first mistake only: for a hand-written file that is one run a mistake; for a bridge it is one run for each kind of keyword a tool list holds (five tools in the shapes MCP servers emit were refused for five different reasons, one a run). The notation's own refusals could be collected and printed together; the checks' cannot without more change.","kind":"comment","references":"bb66b1ceb9bc0bb0073b1501051bf2b166c61b8b1c086dcf84dc0348d6ea3299","summary":"Reviewed the shape as built against the other repository's proposal and MCP: no field name to change; three things to settle while nothing depends on them","tags":["review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T07:53:59.161547Z","id":"ac93d888d104f9cdd9a71f21e6f8692f6e5fd678b443e84e8bd8cba36d599c8d","body":{"detail":"`clax_surface::parse_manifest` answers with `Errors` and `clax bot surface check` prints each on a line, or as `{\"file\", \"errors\"}` with `--json` (crates/clax-commands/src/commands/bot.rs); a `.d.ts` file's reader still stops at its first. `clax_surface::canonical_manifest` gives the bytes to hash (line 225 of the design, \"a definition's hash (over its canonical JSON)\"). A namespace directly on a surface may not have the surface's name, in either notation (crates/clax-surface/src/check.rs, `Notation::repeats_surface`).","kind":"comment","references":"bb66b1ceb9bc0bb0073b1501051bf2b166c61b8b1c086dcf84dc0348d6ea3299","summary":"Three things this record said have changed: `check` now says every entry's first mistake of a manifest; a definition's name is its canonical bytes, not the laid-out manifest; and an operation's `name` may not start with its surface's","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:24:31.893326Z","id":"1738b80d240cda7024dbde9d8867172886a036a594558c942e68362bb1fb9ae4","body":{"detail":"1. The example delivers `ask` with `\"call\": \"read\"`; `shell.d.ts` declares `ask` `@effect`, and a call's `call` is the operation's access as declared (`clax_surface::wire::CallKind::of`). 2. No message here names a registration, though many of one name may be live: `serve` and `runs` take an optional `registration`, and without it mean the name's newest (`Hub::find`, crates/clax-bot/src/bot_surfaces.rs). 3. 'returns as soon as there is a call' and 'a call not answered goes out again on the next serve' together would make a host spin while one call waits for a person: a `serve` returns at once only for something its host has not been sent (`Hub::ready`), and what was sent before goes out again when a `serve` is answered for any reason, its wait's end among them. 4. An `ended` has an `id` and is acknowledged by an answer that names it, which the design does not say (\"Providers\": 'delivered until the provider acknowledges it'). docs/contract.md, \"ClaxBot surfaces\", states all four.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":773},"end":{"line":797},"content_hash":"4ce4c3179894f8972c579831fb88e82b345c10dfa82d3b4076fa3b34678e6ab8"},"summary":"Four places where the protocol as built differs from this block or reads it one way","tags":["claxbot-surfaces","design","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:54:59.623784Z","id":"7e3abc9158a521e1488ffaf6df2c62d2c0341636b4a399c5e72e2e0973f80f63","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs no longer has `Ty`, `Field`, `Param` or `OPS`: the types are `clax_surface::Ty`'s and the operations are crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts. Lines that describe them as present: this document :15 (`one table of operations (crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs, OPS)`), :179 (`Types are those api::Ty has`), :226 (`OpSpec::args_schema`, record dccc4f80); docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools-design.md:92-95 (`OpSpec`: its name, parameters, result type …, where `OpSpec` now holds name, access, performer, errors and the definition's operation). Lines :601 and :1023 say the file replaces `OPS`, which is now done, and docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools.md:367 is a finished plan's step.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":184},"content_hash":"2797bbccda4fc765e9adc9cfabbee56fc96d28d579a78e8bfbd6f11beff3ff44"},"suggested_fix":"Name `clax_surface::Ty` at :179 and say at :15 what the table was; point the web-tools design at clax.d.ts.","summary":"The design still says types are those `api::Ty` has and that the operations are a table `OPS`, neither of which exists","supersedes":"212ae9d81eeb473fb6821a8f801a64c2cec396bdd6cd309b33f697ca80515d80","tags":["claxbot-surfaces","docs","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
