does not have the shape this paragraph says it has, and the commands differ from the design's table in two places: for the owner to confirm, and the text to follow","supersedes":"bb66b1ceb9bc0bb0073b1501051bf2b166c61b8b1c086dcf84dc0348d6ea3299","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:55:00.022925Z","id":"866f72c909dca1452b922f86b545a59873f381baa1fcf4e44eb0154a82e54ac7","body":{"detail":"`OpSpec::args_schema`, `result_schema` and the `schema` function under them were deleted from crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs with `OPS` and `Ty`: nothing outside that file's own tests called them (`git grep -n 'args_schema\\|result_schema'` found api.rs alone). `clax-surface` has no JSON Schema output. The manifest notation (\"Two notations\", step 3 of \"Steps\") therefore starts from nothing in the tree; the deleted function is the mapping it described (integer, number, string enum, `prefixItems` with `minItems`/`maxItems`, `additionalProperties: false`, `anyOf`), in the history of crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs before the commit \"refactor(claxbot): the script API is read from clax.d.ts\".","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":237},"content_hash":"0f6e978bf32758e4d20044e78af78922b54dd3303bf168e60aacb301f392e521"},"summary":"`OpSpec::args_schema`, which this paragraph says already writes the manifest's subset of JSON Schema, no longer exists","supersedes":"dccc4f801d04a2fd4359f18fd4db2a5266d435ed6f6a7762740dd13de81f4a50","tags":["claxbot-surfaces","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-timeline-sidebar-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-13T16:12:04.517393Z","id":"a04802571d545c7ec506bd19558b92fc340c5126e688226a187d4e97cffed536","body":{"detail":"The timeline counts a thread a version addressed as not pending (web/shell/src/view/timeline-model.ts, ThreadState 'addressed'), so the sidebar is calm without a change to the data, but the thread's status stays \"open\" for agents (comments_read), the Threads tab's Open section and every other view. The alternative is for the daemon to resolve an addressed thread when the next version publishes with no follow-up on it. That changes what status means for every reader of a thread and is a daemon change, so it was not built.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":479},"end":{"line":484},"content_hash":"f8fe0735bd32319c222aa1c67186ce6b7cfb006c8d023816c5580e1d81477d39"},"summary":"Whether silence settles a thread: an addressed thread stays open until someone resolves it","tags":["status:needs-decision","timeline-sidebar","session:claude-code:ed7d5258-2c86-46a9-8e5a-cd958e24dd71"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-timeline-sidebar-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-13T16:12:04.517453Z","id":"35d532ca0604530725fb28da38ed7ecc62888d5ead3099b26e4e4217eddaffaf","body":{"detail":"The card under a row (web/shell/src/ui/Timeline.svelte, the `card` snippet) already has a reply box, and a reply on a sent thread already goes to its agent; web/e2e/timeline.spec.ts 'a thread sent and addressed by v2 …' shows such a reply puts the row back to 'sent'. A second control for the same action was not added.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":485},"end":{"line":487},"content_hash":"ad07038e7c5791125477985d58a1343a082b62936002c383accb7ca2b058e751"},"summary":"A \"Not quite…\" control on a timeline row that opens a reply box","tags":["revisit:people reply 'not quite' often enough that opening the card first is the slow step","timeline-sidebar","session:claude-code:ed7d5258-2c86-46a9-8e5a-cd958e24dd71"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-timeline-sidebar-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-13T16:12:04.517480Z","id":"ea0f2ecbf7de36b4ff887a0eefd95269e2242437714a6be3ee22eee14cb9706f","body":{"detail":"With no threads the closed sidebar leaves no strip and the page keeps its full width (railShows in web/shell/src/ui/sidebar-chunk.ts:32; web/e2e/timeline.spec.ts 'an artifact with no threads leaves no strip'). With threads, the strip stays while the drawer is docked left or right; docking at the bottom or floating is the only way to have none.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":488},"end":{"line":489},"content_hash":"be61946ae347493724a7bfdde30f4f344347877fc7e24af6dcdffbca1fb92dc0"},"summary":"A strip for an artifact with no threads, and a way to dismiss the strip while docked at a side","tags":["revisit:someone asks for the page's full width with threads present, or for the strip on an artifact with none","timeline-sidebar","session:claude-code:ed7d5258-2c86-46a9-8e5a-cd958e24dd71"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-timeline-sidebar-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-13T16:12:04.517504Z","id":"e394189ac1a9a964fd97c1c0d05b668473557cf174eb80aa637352e3504a6cac","body":{"detail":"web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte mounts Sidebar.svelte without the `view` prop and shows the thread list alone, as before. Giving it the two views would load SidebarViews.svelte in the panel and grow extPanel (web/perf/bundle-budget.json; see cffd2f27 on what the views already cost it).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":490},"end":{"line":490},"content_hash":"4dba21a4467419136e23ac7b8503941c55037aa35a3c4cfcc3a228d0b9a2143e"},"summary":"The Timeline and Threads views in the extension's side panel","tags":["revisit:the side panel's users ask for the timeline, or the panel is redesigned","timeline-sidebar","session:claude-code:ed7d5258-2c86-46a9-8e5a-cd958e24dd71"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-timeline-sidebar-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-13T16:12:04.517526Z","id":"6afd16e9c390bda9122acbfb092f68aff72c9dd30da2f39d05a09a5e22be543f","body":{"detail":"The daemon writes a `sends` entry only for a batch (crates/clax-store/src/batches.rs); a single Send, an @agent mention and a send to ClaxBot set `sent_to_agent` alone. The timeline then reads such a thread as with the agent from the moment it was made and writes no sent line for it (web/shell/src/view/timeline-model.ts). A `sent_at` on the thread view would fix it, and is a daemon and API change. Related: e9c351b1 (a sent line cannot name the agent), which the same daemon change could carry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":491},"end":{"line":493},"content_hash":"2620123e930f160cdce988a1c53c9f6b12dad67ef6f1764d238be9b683a06abf"},"summary":"A single Send records no time, so the timeline cannot show when a comment was sent or how long it sat unsent","tags":["status:needs-decision","timeline-sidebar","session:claude-code:ed7d5258-2c86-46a9-8e5a-cd958e24dd71"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-timeline-sidebar-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-13T16:12:04.517548Z","id":"24f76a206bde1094cb1629338bfb25bae19f1eab2591db79265983183a158761","body":{"detail":"The band in the strip takes one fixed 18 px step per line (web/shell/src/ui/Rail.svelte) and, in the expanded timeline, each line's measured centre (web/shell/src/ui/Timeline.svelte). Event order is compact, and the mock (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-13-timeline-sidebar-vignette.html) that spaced by clock time read worse.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":494},"end":{"line":495},"content_hash":"157c4b56e90a0539f4ecadca8bbf6e215fe605dcb9c8127c5b5869d72de3e510"},"summary":"The band spaced by clock time instead of one step per line","tags":["revisit:people read the band as time and are misled by it","timeline-sidebar","session:claude-code:ed7d5258-2c86-46a9-8e5a-cd958e24dd71"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-15-site-own-content-policy-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-15T07:17:55.641928Z","id":"e6e5e100c72cf983d471a7743d6bc6d39cfd9194b0431cde77b6d23434e12b0c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: one switch says what is being decided (the clax is trusted as a site), while a list of CDN hosts tells the person approving little and is fiddly for an agent to maintain. own lifts the lockdown wholesale (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs policy_of) and a page that wants a narrower policy writes its own <meta> one.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"9244639e383174760c94e0bb113824e116698165059eb2c87490cb2687e2eb5c"},"summary":"Per-origin allowlists (hosts per CSP directive) instead of one own switch","tags":["revisit:people ask to trust a clax for named hosts only, or a page's own <meta> policy proves too weak a way to narrow an own site","session:claude-code:b9f94772-0463-4668-a532-bfded61f18de"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-15-site-own-content-policy-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-18T20:04:09.639924Z","id":"be6b29a7a070586edeb518e799946d29741220d2e78425c86fdde80cfbdaec91","body":{"detail":"Not taken: one setting says what is being decided (the clax is trusted as a site), while a list of CDN hosts tells the person approving little and is fiddly for an agent to maintain. unrestricted lifts the lockdown wholesale (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs policy_of) and a page that wants a narrower policy writes its own <meta> one.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":48},"end":{"line":50},"content_hash":"e882a37853bdf3d490f847c5917e757dad8e5c31ad8d8c0af70c43e79102a906"},"summary":"Per-origin allowlists (hosts per CSP directive) instead of one unrestricted setting","supersedes":"e6e5e100c72cf983d471a7743d6bc6d39cfd9194b0431cde77b6d23434e12b0c","tags":["revisit:people ask to trust a clax for named hosts only, or a page's own <meta> policy proves too weak a way to narrow an unrestricted site","session:claude-code:b9f94772-0463-4668-a532-bfded61f18de"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.776946Z","id":"78f39245bdc452c62618d9fa5c87d097fe1eebb66720197cce7d2293ed1d9d1b","body":{"detail":"web.fetch's URL-source rule (crates/clax-bot/src/web/access.rs `sources`), Markdown conversion, page store and `WebSource` are not used, because the web tools' scope is expected to be loosened (raw HTML, not only Markdown). Only generic machinery is reused: `Access::Spend` and `Store::spend_journaled` (crates/clax-store/src/bot_web.rs), credits, settings, the sealed Cloudflare credentials, run content. The web-named pieces it needs are generalised in place (§4.6). Design decision for the owner to confirm or overturn.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":157},"content_hash":"ba743e72362d389c4a77cfbba3844fb08b86dd8791fabac7cda5d66e974babe9"},"summary":"Decision: the browser is its own `clax.browser` namespace with its own grant, settings, codes, cost line and audit kind, built on none of web.fetch's internals","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777018Z","id":"9ae624fe5550ed11ab56850686f8541e0b4f2afc7855529903c11106ddb9c0c5","body":{"detail":"Rejected for v1: Quick Actions return no console messages or page errors, run no actions (click, type, assertions), and make Cloudflare fetch the page itself, which cannot reach a private artifact or a daemon on localhost. CDP with Fetch-domain interception (§4.3, §6) serves the page from the host instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":173},"end":{"line":177},"content_hash":"947d400f62c81b190573301bc385d474213fc572e47ba809b60571236590414d"},"summary":"Quick Actions REST (/screenshot, /content, /scrape) instead of CDP over a WebSocket","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:Browser Run's REST API gains console, errors and request interception","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777054Z","id":"7f2fb7b4e216ad57c3c0fde8154304d0319b707bb8f04650b8942a003c1d755d","body":{"detail":"The endpoint is wss://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/{id}/browser-run/devtools/browser per the 2026-11 docs, but other pages of the same docs use `browser-rendering`. The design makes it one constant (`BROWSER_RUN_PATH`) pinned by the daemon test against a fake server, which cannot tell which spelling Cloudflare accepts: only the opt-in live test (`just browser-live`) can. If Cloudflare answers 404 on the upgrade, switch the constant.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":185},"end":{"line":187},"content_hash":"41e24a51f232e6b870cb844e47e06785001ea98a039d6ef01c23209a588d1c16"},"summary":"Browser Run's docs spell the CDP path segment both `browser-run` and `browser-rendering`","tags":["claxbot-browser","risk","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777084Z","id":"d3100720ac247d8d9ada145037b00d7d6787003681c2ad983a016f4c3e384542","body":{"detail":"The session ends the browser itself (`Browser.close`) on every path out of the driver; a process that dies cannot. keep_alive is set to its minimum (10 s) and Browser Run's idle timeout is 60 s, so an orphan costs at most about a browser-minute ($0.0015 at list price), absorbed by the instance and not charged to the person (the Spend transaction never ran).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"3ba3b75082671bfeec96dd78e7e0c6677af31f0ee14857ac58ac774ac40cd48f"},"summary":"A browser orphaned by a daemon crash mid-test stays on Browser Run until keep_alive or the idle timeout, billed to the instance","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777113Z","id":"a4a92ac50b01e727098993edaf46291eb6cf5cdcf4fd62e54888a5c554424f99","body":{"detail":"Keeps the policy host-independent and testable against an in-memory fake Chrome, as `WebSource` did for web (spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §4.3). `clax_core::wrap` and the store are reachable from clax-bot, so the page set is built there; the bridge's hashed part files, the site CSP (clax-http) and `/_clax/api/` are the server's, so they are trait methods. Check against scripts/check-crate-layers.py: no new crate edge.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":222},"end":{"line":270},"content_hash":"c1803f0df07c4be329b8703c895c8b7c42bff3d3d3931d7291df07a7e3a89e3b"},"summary":"Decision: the CDP driver, request policy, steps and result shaping live in clax-bot `browser/`; a host provides only a `CdpTransport`, Clax's UI files, the site's headers and its read-only API","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777145Z","id":"1e3c57f677f55c2b639bbb3b1b2cd14920df0f69adc336ef3eb7ce6bfe80279b","body":{"detail":"One Cloudflare account per instance; the token gains the Browser Rendering - Edit permission. The setting's key stays web-named; the admin pages label it \"Cloudflare account\".","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":309},"end":{"line":309},"content_hash":"759b0c8a0f44491c6342dd7bf0f5eb5b4ba02c1b7b8fd4f3cf9584bd65f7d580"},"summary":"Decision: reuse `web.cloudflare.account_id` and `SecretSlot::Cloudflare` for Browser Run rather than adding browser credentials","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777170Z","id":"e1165f1bd16fe04d675194a398992afb76810b8a49730b6c0df867da863ef7a4","body":{"detail":"Not now: a key rename needs a migration of stored settings and of `[bot.web]` config overrides, unrelated to the browser. The browser reads the existing key.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":309},"end":{"line":309},"content_hash":"759b0c8a0f44491c6342dd7bf0f5eb5b4ba02c1b7b8fd4f3cf9584bd65f7d580"},"summary":"Rename the setting `web.cloudflare.account_id` to `cloudflare.account_id`, shared by web and browser","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a third Cloudflare-backed feature reads the account ID","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777197Z","id":"bdf65886abaf6c4ca472b873307e15e0409124b936eec67a710b95413b7d7052","body":{"detail":"`.invalid` never resolves (RFC 6761), so a request that escapes interception fails closed; https makes it a secure context like the real site. Fulfilling https requests from Fetch.requestPaused is standard CDP practice but untested against Browser Run until the live test runs.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":435},"end":{"line":444},"content_hash":"78d7ecb8685b763498f6fbf827e35a75d604fc8761075cae2c90149686887e13"},"summary":"Decision: claxen load at https://<artifact ID>.clax-test.invalid/, every request answered by the host through the CDP Fetch domain","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777221Z","id":"f10e6a2c979120f8f6cc6a538e65ebe837b30e7a826950326621f51dd69a1530","body":{"detail":"v1 answers GETs as the run's person and refuses writes (403 read_only_test), so a test never changes people's documents; a page whose first render writes shows that failure. The scratch copy needs a hidden draft artifact per test and its cleanup.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":465},"end":{"line":475},"content_hash":"96fe5568d9aabe04563f4b5599c963e6094e1ad0fc486daca925948b57247ef8"},"summary":"A writable scratch copy of the artifact's documents during a test, as the Clax app's drafts make (POST /api/drafts), instead of a read-only /_clax/api/","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:ClaxBot tests a db-writing page and the read-only refusals hide real failures","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777251Z","id":"4d8ee9bb538b3496813eaf99ec669dd023265f57cfab2837f4738b88731a311a","body":{"detail":"Clax's page contract serves every page under `default-src 'self' data: blob:` (docs/contract.md, \"Sites\"), so no CDN host can load on the real site; an allowlist would let a test pass where the page fails for its viewers. Navigations, which CSP does not govern, are failed at the Fetch domain; CSP refusals are reported through a securitypolicyviolation listener. Departs from the earlier idea of a page-contract CDN allowlist: there is no such list in Clax.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":476},"end":{"line":501},"content_hash":"a4c71e0e6b7ce405902f309dd4adaa3cc2f90b2f552c3945ec736b01fe335705"},"summary":"Decision: no CDN allowlist; a page under test reaches its synthetic origin alone, every other request (navigations included) is failed and reported","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777280Z","id":"2c32e21258161f23b6086db27f3213f35543885994040481334e2fa27c171171","body":{"detail":"Chrome's DNS prefetch and preconnect happen outside the CDP Fetch domain and outside CSP, so a page under test can make Browser Run's resolver look up <data>.evil.example. WebRTC is closed by the preamble removing RTCPeerConnection; DNS is not closable from CDP. The artifact's content, documents read through /_clax/api/, and screenshots are processed by Cloudflare as a sub-processor, as search queries already are. Accepted: a person viewing the page in their own browser has the same DNS channel.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":495},"end":{"line":501},"content_hash":"d8670a13f3d6e8565ee6b13d6efa8a5abbda1ecd3eb8cadff66d9dbac88ee11e"},"summary":"DNS prefetch, speculative connections and Cloudflare's processing of the page stay open as channels","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777305Z","id":"005307b28a150ee65115dbd3a53e163b3d002efe6af8a6fbdd822c4db036e7bb","body":{"detail":"Rejected: the Clax app's inspect view already runs `tests/<name>.test.js` with the bridge harness (docs/contract.md \"The inspect view\", web/bridge/src/harness.ts). A second format would be less expressive and not run by the app. `steps` remain for one-call checks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":513},"end":{"line":517},"content_hash":"841ffe69ff15602f05b9631710ee5ed2323098f821d2ba42867c678356580ba4"},"summary":"A declarative JSON test file in the `steps` format for durable tests","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the harness's JS tests prove hard for ClaxBot to write correctly","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777334Z","id":"1c3fa7d3b6b1c3057307a7b41ffc4f5e1447141c75daf7339789a6c9ed8d41c3","body":{"detail":"The driver evaluates a fixed expression against a hook defined only when window.name is `clax-test`. A bridge change that renames or reshapes it breaks browser tests silently unless the fake-Chrome test of the expression and the bridge unit test of the hook agree. The hook adds bytes to the eager bridge, which is already over its gzip budget (thread 1014d9d7 on web/bridge/src/bridge.ts): keep it a few lines that delegate to the test part.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":526},"end":{"line":538},"content_hash":"cb329874ec24f2bfda101986a75214296b2b561cc7e12c54a6cdf8c6c57041be"},"summary":"The bridge hook `window.claxTest.run` couples ClaxBot's driver to the bridge's lazy test part and to an eager-bridge byte budget","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777358Z","id":"d925d7cb9bf21d4be1a9093dfdde6a88f171f7e42a9bdc2390fa3305992461c8","body":{"detail":"The run panel shows ClaxBot's test results; the Clax app's inspect view runs the same files on its drafts; nothing in the web shell lets an artifact's owner run `tests/*.test.js`. Follow-up: a Run tests button on the artifact page (needs a browser-run route outside a ClaxBot run, and who pays for it).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":539},"end":{"line":544},"content_hash":"dec2bb9fcba73540ccb0e79909bdf15b031492aaef47a2d31cea4b7eba76297b"},"summary":"People cannot run an artifact's tests themselves in v1","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:deferred","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777382Z","id":"66b42c3c2f733a81ae4735c306eeae1d9455f90cd8d2d702988d744c2aa7d094","body":{"detail":"Cloudflare bills $2.00 per concurrent browser beyond 10 (monthly average) on top of browser-hours. It cannot be attributed to one test, so `browser.time` charges hours only. `browser.max_concurrent` (default 2) bounds the exposure.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":555},"end":{"line":556},"content_hash":"c740944ad7979051b85934b7d0ea15ded124c13289887692984a5c8b3021d014"},"summary":"Browser Run's concurrency charge is not metered per test; the instance absorbs it","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777409Z","id":"c80fad7d589683e744370ea75aa2d9c2053b2de82dabb6f6cd47bd3887a84663","body":{"detail":"The time cap bounds what one test can cost, so a person cannot run past their week mid-test; at list price a 60 s cap is 0.0015 USD. Measured from the WebSocket upgrade to its close by the provider's injected clock. A test that never opened (401, 429, socket error, browser_busy) is not charged but counts toward the cap when it reached Browser Run.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":564},"end":{"line":586},"content_hash":"ce205f859878fc4ced943353fca80c677ec9775377b7d6fe5df8f990046e05bd"},"summary":"Decision: pre-check that the person can pay for the call's whole time cap, not the minimum charge; charge measured time rounded up to the second, whenever a browser opened","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777436Z","id":"5ee4dbf8e9562869d6d2ccb8c090c409e07a6dcfd3e73f63fcc1a1e651d51f7a","body":{"detail":"The operation shape, steps and result are shared with `test`, so the marginal work is a URL rule, an egress mode and a setting. The phase can be cut without touching earlier tasks. For the owner to confirm.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":589},"end":{"line":597},"content_hash":"b0b8679f5e0bdc8e963663817f9969703c3376bebfcc60ae695a9b784ee8a594"},"summary":"Decision: `clax.browser.browse` (public URLs) ships in v1 behind `browser.browse.enabled`, off by default, in the plan's last phase","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777460Z","id":"3ef67464c2cc7e1e1deea9d721a7c6a36d57ebfbd290344a287d2da454c9df8c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: little marginal code, off by default, and it exercises the computer-use path the owner wants kept open.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":589},"end":{"line":597},"content_hash":"b0b8679f5e0bdc8e963663817f9969703c3376bebfcc60ae695a9b784ee8a594"},"summary":"Defer browsing public URLs to a later version","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the browse phase slips or its waiver is judged too wide before release","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777483Z","id":"7b40db959130f5b51338e16e87e2483b0feeccd52d6a751bd3b2aa96f2607a95","body":{"detail":"`sender` admits a start or goto URL only when it equals a URL in a from_sender comment or the brief, by the browser's own scan of RequestContext; web::access::sources is not used, so loosening the web tools does not change browsing. PublicUrl and OwnHosts (host safety) apply under every rule.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":598},"end":{"line":614},"content_hash":"740b1dbf59133fbdae1db79095897dd2b947054f0c45b132259ecd7992ec06e3"},"summary":"Decision: browse has its own URL rule (`sender` by default, `allowlist`, `any_public`), independent of web.fetch's","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777507Z","id":"e688825fccfd07256447a20ee628aafe713986b56d540526c678c0fcd1cc94b5","body":{"detail":"Inherent to computer use: `type`, `eval` and `goto` are model-written. Defences: the admin switch (off by default), both person switches (browser and web), the `sender` rule by default, the per-run browse cap, the prompt rule that page text is data. The admin page states the risk beside the switch.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":624},"end":{"line":632},"content_hash":"d5d843c4142d2f2fa189fff5004f2035976a6e637883700f119ac432448659f6"},"summary":"Browsing lets a steered model type data into third-party forms, and under any_public put it in URLs","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777530Z","id":"e4dc1bbb842b3c8640f11809563a6a47e97d0fff881a827dba908de919b5971e","body":{"detail":"Testing one's own page reaches no third party and has its own price; the web switch's scope is expected to change. One switch for both was considered; browse reaches the web, so it needs both.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":657},"end":{"line":665},"content_hash":"00b1929c426844cd235e1587ba5e0d1b018eb449c991cda7486ebcb085ca36c2"},"summary":"Decision: a separate person switch for the browser (`bot_person_prefs.browser`), with browse needing the web switch too","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777552Z","id":"388e4d3ff7eabdda470b583b1fc01c675c4da8b6e36fbe29f299c4ea02930240","body":{"detail":"Deferred: the Worker's content stores keep no blobs (open concern on crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs), so screenshots could not be kept, and its CDP transport is a change of its own. The Worker answers NotConfigured.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":680},"end":{"line":684},"content_hash":"b77199698fbeb575a9216d176b91a6a0e0e792cadc0b8138a8f674856894cfae"},"summary":"Browser use on the Worker in v1 (outbound WebSocket via fetch Upgrade, or the BROWSER binding)","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the Worker's content store keeps blobs","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:05:14.777579Z","id":"7281343205961fccb9c7539b6784a9da46b5da4991806907786f42e275f139db","body":{"detail":"No route today lets the shell read a run's content (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot_content.rs serves hosts with the daemon token). The plan adds GET /api/bot/runs/<run>/content/<id> for whoever may view the run, images only, under a sandbox CSP. A 'Tested' list in finish, like web's Sources, is a follow-up.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":689},"end":{"line":708},"content_hash":"b2f7585bf29747edb24ac0aff54ed6c7e600537dc6512b34944105824c6aa181"},"summary":"Run-panel thumbnails need a new person-facing content route","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:38:30.820426Z","id":"c7d2ee56ef9acde201d86a46db84e2829d43edfa3939e35c8ba81f3902ca8b07","body":{"detail":"Tests in crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs: a_test_answers_and_is_charged_its_measured_time (8.4 s measured, 9,000 ms charged), the_cap_and_credits_refuse_before_opening (credits_exhausted with no browser opened), a_failure_before_opening_is_not_charged_but_counts (browser_busy not counted, browser_unavailable counted, neither charged). The time is measured from run_test's start, right after BrowserSource::open answered, which on the daemon is the WebSocket's upgrade.","kind":"comment","references":"c80fad7d589683e744370ea75aa2d9c2053b2de82dabb6f6cd47bd3887a84663","summary":"Built in crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs: the pre-check prices opts.timeout_s at browser.time's rate (browser_ctx), the charge is (closed_at - opened_at) rounded up to the whole second (whole_seconds) whenever open succeeded, and a refusal from open counts unless it is browser_busy or a cancelled run","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:45:48.589486Z","id":"4be61de3ec63dc2c50224ad6d4228b1aaa5dd4bbb682399de2074d169b71b937","body":{"detail":"The hook is a few lines in the eager bridge that delegate to the test part's run (web/bridge/src/parts/test.ts); the window name is protocol.ts TEST_WINDOW on the bridge's side and preamble_js on the driver's. Its cost to the eager bridge is measured on thread 1014d9d7.","kind":"comment","references":"1c3fa7d3b6b1c3057307a7b41ffc4f5e1447141c75daf7339789a6c9ed8d41c3","summary":"Built: the coupling is pinned on both sides, web/bridge/test/bridge-clax-test.test.ts (the hook exists only in a top-level window named clax-test, is read-only and answers TestResults) and crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs saved_tests_run_through_the_bridge_hook (the exact expression saved_tests_js evaluates)","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:10:22.541131Z","id":"924556dfa4b400124b8f787b73b5ea35bb09bfcfd8d32f00cc0442a937cd73ef","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7281343205961fccb9c7539b6784a9da46b5da4991806907786f42e275f139db","span":{"start":{"line":689},"end":{"line":708},"content_hash":"b2f7585bf29747edb24ac0aff54ed6c7e600537dc6512b34944105824c6aa181"},"summary":"Built: GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/content/<item> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs run_content), image items of that run of the four raster types only, under Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src 'none' and nosniff, 404 otherwise. Tests: api_claxbot::run_content_is_served_to_the_runs_viewers_only, api_claxbot::a_non_image_item_is_not_served. It admits the person the run acts for and admins who read its artifact, not readers (see the alternative on run_content).","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:24:00.153735Z","id":"a66b7e66c016212c06ea46b9e867e047cd78c98c64b637ed91df5b11f91bc818","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7f2fb7b4e216ad57c3c0fde8154304d0319b707bb8f04650b8942a003c1d755d","summary":"The check exists but has not run: crates/clax-server/tests/live_browser_run.rs (just browser-live) opens /client/v4/accounts/<account>/browser-run/devtools/browser through DaemonBrowser and asserts a whole test, Browser.close answered. No Cloudflare credentials were available when it was written; run without them it skips and passes (integration__6: live_browser_run: skipped ... ok). The thread stays open until someone runs just browser-live with an account and a Browser Rendering - Edit token.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:49:36.650076Z","id":"16a6ba8b860baac4ca83b2ede0f39551defdd392069bb21b1ee1d790c3a62447","body":{"detail":"See the records on crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs:32:38 (the narrowing and why), browse.rs:39:44 (the resolver waiver) and crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:235 (sockets). Under any_public the section holds as written, plus the name check.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":615},"end":{"line":622},"content_hash":"569b55a6fee4783d247a474eb9d6765290a4d6713e9fb55745e0ba884128e67e"},"summary":"The code departs from §9.3: under sender and allowlist a browsed page's requests are held to the rule's hosts, names are checked by the daemon's resolver, and WebSocket and WebTransport are removed","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:49:36.650892Z","id":"83552a8c13e8833fc47ec5941af409d05f20aefad07e153c79502591c19fe996","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e688825fccfd07256447a20ee628aafe713986b56d540526c678c0fcd1cc94b5","summary":"The waiver's boundary is now enforced: under sender and allowlist a browsed page's every request goes only to the rule's hosts (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs BrowseScope::admits_host), so data can leave only for a host the rule names; under any_public, anywhere public. The admin page's risk line says so (web/shell/src/bot/AdminBrowser.svelte).","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:52.054913Z","id":"d69c778b05346db138579fb292cccbb37b6cffdfe61a656b726bb998c2d3fcb6","body":{"detail":"web.fetch's URL-source rule (crates/clax-bot/src/web/access.rs `sources`), Markdown conversion, page store and `WebSource` are not used, because the web tools' scope is expected to be loosened (raw HTML, not only Markdown). Only generic machinery is reused: `Access::Spend` and `Store::spend_journaled` (crates/clax-store/src/bot_web.rs), credits, settings, the sealed Cloudflare credentials, run content. The web-named pieces it needs are generalised in place (§4.6). Design decision for the owner to confirm or overturn.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1038},"end":{"line":1039},"content_hash":"d834d6317c0b68bf4d7501bc9808c4610d82db56dfea4a3cf5a86ef8ee16ad88"},"summary":"Decision: the browser is its own `clax.browser` namespace with its own grant, settings, codes, cost line and audit kind, built on none of web.fetch's internals","supersedes":"78f39245bdc452c62618d9fa5c87d097fe1eebb66720197cce7d2293ed1d9d1b","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:52.268594Z","id":"7ec11e93dd3b7eb6c3727627dc2805d43b1cfcc7573b113dde11ef8bca7ef2b7","body":{"detail":"Rejected for v1: Quick Actions return no console messages or page errors, run no actions (click, type, assertions), and make Cloudflare fetch the page itself, which cannot reach a private artifact or a daemon on localhost. CDP with Fetch-domain interception (§4.3, §6) serves the page from the host instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":639},"end":{"line":643},"content_hash":"807ae5b3522eaac112f1473fc9d75f9d06e9c523a221cc95d6ec2115ccf41b26"},"summary":"Quick Actions REST (/screenshot, /content, /scrape) instead of CDP over a WebSocket","supersedes":"9ae624fe5550ed11ab56850686f8541e0b4f2afc7855529903c11106ddb9c0c5","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:Browser Run's REST API gains console, errors and request interception","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:52.466279Z","id":"88b76c21d24850e57b353726771261f79c87479039d36a6eb5f98b3eca723bc9","body":{"detail":"The endpoint is wss://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/{id}/browser-run/devtools/browser per the 2026-11 docs, but other pages of the same docs use `browser-rendering`. The design makes it one constant (`BROWSER_RUN_PATH`) pinned by the daemon test against a fake server, which cannot tell which spelling Cloudflare accepts: only the opt-in live test (`just browser-live`) can. If Cloudflare answers 404 on the upgrade, switch the constant.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":639},"end":{"line":641},"content_hash":"6a2e226dedb88600452b1c9947f520f60123ebce3e1d14f24032899c5880990b"},"summary":"Browser Run's docs spell the CDP path segment both `browser-run` and `browser-rendering`","supersedes":"7f2fb7b4e216ad57c3c0fde8154304d0319b707bb8f04650b8942a003c1d755d","tags":["claxbot-browser","risk","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:52.669179Z","id":"70f545711f859101ee0d277a670f893439b81eacaa266a1e8ffff14dd9ed4df7","body":{"detail":"The session ends the browser itself (`Browser.close`) on every path out of the driver; a process that dies cannot. keep_alive is set to its minimum (10 s) and Browser Run's idle timeout is 60 s, so an orphan costs at most about a browser-minute ($0.0015 at list price), absorbed by the instance and not charged to the person (the Spend transaction never ran).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":885},"end":{"line":888},"content_hash":"4bd18242a8b6a06aae591c550c865171dae22e229799396965aebe64f4684abe"},"summary":"A browser orphaned by a daemon crash mid-test stays on Browser Run until keep_alive or the idle timeout, billed to the instance","supersedes":"d3100720ac247d8d9ada145037b00d7d6787003681c2ad983a016f4c3e384542","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:52.863405Z","id":"9fe06730836715bc4b39e0d8c82c7b7c48e8187ff62f67f841263f913afa0f04","body":{"detail":"Keeps the policy host-independent and testable against an in-memory fake Chrome, as `WebSource` did for web (spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §4.3). `clax_core::wrap` and the store are reachable from clax-bot, so the page set is built there; the bridge's hashed part files, the site CSP (clax-http) and `/_clax/api/` are the server's, so they are trait methods. Check against scripts/check-crate-layers.py: no new crate edge.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":682},"end":{"line":694},"content_hash":"a4021daa009fe5dee0fdb2750ac060c80cd5b0eeacb902774962fdb6e8a40abf"},"summary":"Decision: the CDP driver, request policy, steps and result shaping live in clax-bot `browser/`; a host provides only a `CdpTransport`, Clax's UI files, the site's headers and its read-only API","supersedes":"a4a92ac50b01e727098993edaf46291eb6cf5cdcf4fd62e54888a5c554424f99","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:53.055693Z","id":"6e85a317d5866e87a5d9d7b06018eda4c679a781e1a5acad341e8678de0f1b05","body":{"detail":"One Cloudflare account per instance; the token gains the Browser Rendering - Edit permission. The setting's key stays web-named; the admin pages label it \"Cloudflare account\".","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":373},"end":{"line":380},"content_hash":"8fd63349173de04dd6c72509ad7923474ee83f9c2eff529cb01f6879b91622e5"},"summary":"Decision: reuse `web.cloudflare.account_id` and `SecretSlot::Cloudflare` for Browser Run rather than adding browser credentials","supersedes":"1e3c57f677f55c2b639bbb3b1b2cd14920df0f69adc336ef3eb7ce6bfe80279b","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:53.249597Z","id":"c97268ac3c6bed0088503678c143209731668f70af27e8670fb73e0217d2227c","body":{"detail":"Not now: a key rename needs a migration of stored settings and of `[bot.web]` config overrides, unrelated to the browser. The browser reads the existing key.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":380},"end":{"line":380},"content_hash":"454c17a4c3102d022cf09d105884a29f31c51fad288774fbc535910eb7ac893a"},"summary":"Rename the setting `web.cloudflare.account_id` to `cloudflare.account_id`, shared by web and browser","supersedes":"e1165f1bd16fe04d675194a398992afb76810b8a49730b6c0df867da863ef7a4","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a third Cloudflare-backed feature reads the account ID","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:53.441977Z","id":"5169d27aa537cf4c40813dfe43e5e53f77ebdfe2216ec76b6865804cac44a196","body":{"detail":"`.invalid` never resolves (RFC 6761), so a request that escapes interception fails closed; https makes it a secure context like the real site. Fulfilling https requests from Fetch.requestPaused is standard CDP practice but untested against Browser Run until the live test runs.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":721},"end":{"line":730},"content_hash":"9a77ec62bb7868200ed0a55446654500bd368413d4c2fadf8c6c133b3f91813e"},"summary":"Decision: claxen load at https://<artifact ID>.clax-test.invalid/, every request answered by the host through the CDP Fetch domain","supersedes":"bdf65886abaf6c4ca472b873307e15e0409124b936eec67a710b95413b7d7052","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:53.635687Z","id":"b2d7c91de7c01b6afed224002435ee036bed44f104542e3c32f0c708d08b41c0","body":{"detail":"v1 answers GETs as the run's person and refuses writes (403 read_only_test), so a test never changes people's documents; a page whose first render writes shows that failure. The scratch copy needs a hidden draft artifact per test and its cleanup.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":754},"end":{"line":759},"content_hash":"254873fb34a94bb19ca34727f047f95b0bd8cea8a052ea5a54bb452051f6c80d"},"summary":"A writable scratch copy of the artifact's documents during a test, as the Clax app's drafts make (POST /api/drafts), instead of a read-only /_clax/api/","supersedes":"f10e6a2c979120f8f6cc6a538e65ebe837b30e7a826950326621f51dd69a1530","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:ClaxBot tests a db-writing page and the read-only refusals hide real failures","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:53.841186Z","id":"980c1d88178e97a4211f5ee2b05f06bc450034ddfbc15c0f49c969b290683ebf","body":{"detail":"Clax's page contract serves every page under `default-src 'self' data: blob:` (docs/contract.md, \"Sites\"), so no CDN host can load on the real site; an allowlist would let a test pass where the page fails for its viewers. Navigations, which CSP does not govern, are failed at the Fetch domain; CSP refusals are reported through a securitypolicyviolation listener. Departs from the earlier idea of a page-contract CDN allowlist: there is no such list in Clax.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":763},"end":{"line":771},"content_hash":"c9668f84333a38be10644f1b0b9a307b3c9532870903b2cb1d7164a5935c8c04"},"summary":"Decision: no CDN allowlist; a page under test reaches its synthetic origin alone, every other request (navigations included) is failed and reported","supersedes":"4d8ee9bb538b3496813eaf99ec669dd023265f57cfab2837f4738b88731a311a","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:54.046295Z","id":"4b64bc2d9dcb4a52759e009dde592c477cde4d2db15f73fb9d3d94d587f4cce3","body":{"detail":"Chrome's DNS prefetch and preconnect happen outside the CDP Fetch domain and outside CSP, so a page under test can make Browser Run's resolver look up <data>.evil.example. WebRTC is closed by the preamble removing RTCPeerConnection; DNS is not closable from CDP. The artifact's content, documents read through /_clax/api/, and screenshots are processed by Cloudflare as a sub-processor, as search queries already are. Accepted: a person viewing the page in their own browser has the same DNS channel.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":787},"end":{"line":791},"content_hash":"22050267ef151e4e86d03973c03db3e6ed480c547415a803e74ea3653b51d542"},"summary":"DNS prefetch, speculative connections and Cloudflare's processing of the page stay open as channels","supersedes":"2c32e21258161f23b6086db27f3213f35543885994040481334e2fa27c171171","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:54.246042Z","id":"a92abf1ece99d74225d479c8261ec954a86432d77e78cc7ee82c4308c223e26d","body":{"detail":"Rejected: the Clax app's inspect view already runs `tests/<name>.test.js` with the bridge harness (docs/contract.md \"The inspect view\", web/bridge/src/harness.ts). A second format would be less expressive and not run by the app. `steps` remain for one-call checks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":810},"end":{"line":815},"content_hash":"c149b0bcda665c0facd51069cc716bce47b468a603bf32e400306ef9a84777ba"},"summary":"A declarative JSON test file in the `steps` format for durable tests","supersedes":"005307b28a150ee65115dbd3a53e163b3d002efe6af8a6fbdd822c4db036e7bb","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the harness's JS tests prove hard for ClaxBot to write correctly","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:54.457374Z","id":"2502441776618b87bbe82688891ec89857022b9c05955ced4d3c59636f0c4df1","body":{"detail":"The driver evaluates a fixed expression against a hook defined only when window.name is `clax-test`. A bridge change that renames or reshapes it breaks browser tests silently unless the fake-Chrome test of the expression and the bridge unit test of the hook agree. The hook adds bytes to the eager bridge, which is already over its gzip budget (thread 1014d9d7 on web/bridge/src/bridge.ts): keep it a few lines that delegate to the test part.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":825},"end":{"line":832},"content_hash":"106abefc8c1e97e1be133761228e4c6bae1251f5423f8a6822454cb970470cfb"},"summary":"The bridge hook `window.claxTest.run` couples ClaxBot's driver to the bridge's lazy test part and to an eager-bridge byte budget","supersedes":"1c3fa7d3b6b1c3057307a7b41ffc4f5e1447141c75daf7339789a6c9ed8d41c3","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:54.674144Z","id":"ade240242ebe30f5d8ac8e69b0e4fe2162d0bbb1dc763c6be041d8fbf517bf63","body":{"detail":"The run panel shows ClaxBot's test results; the Clax app's inspect view runs the same files on its drafts; nothing in the web shell lets an artifact's owner run `tests/*.test.js`. Follow-up: a Run tests button on the artifact page (needs a browser-run route outside a ClaxBot run, and who pays for it).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":834},"end":{"line":838},"content_hash":"e5343ec1efbd1e1d93c39a987dad48bef180e7dac9a343da1b840b6bd68d6a4a"},"summary":"People cannot run an artifact's tests themselves in v1","supersedes":"d925d7cb9bf21d4be1a9093dfdde6a88f171f7e42a9bdc2390fa3305992461c8","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:deferred","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:54.906405Z","id":"82070d4abb9462b68041d69ffd33fe64e89da657f1007d4dc3d6cf3f0b96a098","body":{"detail":"Cloudflare bills $2.00 per concurrent browser beyond 10 (monthly average) on top of browser-hours. It cannot be attributed to one test, so `browser.time` charges hours only. `browser.max_concurrent` (default 2) bounds the exposure.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":849},"end":{"line":851},"content_hash":"0273cefcc1826cc463dd8683f592fddaa23dfec27d5a4397e99ac08c270c3db9"},"summary":"Browser Run's concurrency charge is not metered per test; the instance absorbs it","supersedes":"66b42c3c2f733a81ae4735c306eeae1d9455f90cd8d2d702988d744c2aa7d094","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:55.134775Z","id":"49c6bb43159f4ed4937ae457ac3113aa8c2df59902083f200190af0b20ea256e","body":{"detail":"The time cap bounds what one test can cost, so a person cannot run past their week mid-test; at list price a 60 s cap is 0.0015 USD. Measured from the WebSocket upgrade to its close by the provider's injected clock. A test that never opened (401, 429, socket error, browser_busy) is not charged but counts toward the cap when it reached Browser Run.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":891},"end":{"line":895},"content_hash":"b51ee6cca45203d59ad1ba1ae79bc08ff083181629ff8f6040a909ddfb4eafb6"},"summary":"Decision: pre-check that the person can pay for the call's whole time cap, not the minimum charge; charge measured time rounded up to the second, whenever a browser opened","supersedes":"c80fad7d589683e744370ea75aa2d9c2053b2de82dabb6f6cd47bd3887a84663","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:55.360719Z","id":"4f9da6258be5b60e60c69f0990ff9dc9c5bb7ffb05989f61b0cf30e7310c39eb","body":{"detail":"Not taken: little marginal code, off by default, and it exercises the computer-use path the owner wants kept open.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":912},"end":{"line":915},"content_hash":"d881a43ce2d3a7bb2bd7190592a416aba4859345ddf5246a4a3b3a0c44577d03"},"summary":"Defer browsing public URLs to a later version","supersedes":"3ef67464c2cc7e1e1deea9d721a7c6a36d57ebfbd290344a287d2da454c9df8c","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the browse phase slips or its waiver is judged too wide before release","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:55.565709Z","id":"e1455c5f3807e932d4e5c31154430ab414d9e0d3d9efc3bacf25139edd1a5f78","body":{"detail":"The operation shape, steps and result are shared with `test`, so the marginal work is a URL rule, an egress mode and a setting. The phase can be cut without touching earlier tasks. For the owner to confirm.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":912},"end":{"line":915},"content_hash":"d881a43ce2d3a7bb2bd7190592a416aba4859345ddf5246a4a3b3a0c44577d03"},"summary":"Decision: `clax.browser.browse` (public URLs) ships in v1 behind `browser.browse.enabled`, off by default, in the plan's last phase","supersedes":"5ee4dbf8e9562869d6d2ccb8c090c409e07a6dcfd3e73f63fcc1a1e651d51f7a","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:55.765082Z","id":"2d74a7508cb87f4a38651548c7383c7afb3224b6a36366b29c16ec1c030f93aa","body":{"detail":"`sender` admits a start or goto URL only when it equals a URL in a from_sender comment or the brief, by the browser's own scan of RequestContext; web::access::sources is not used, so loosening the web tools does not change browsing. PublicUrl and OwnHosts (host safety) apply under every rule.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":266},"end":{"line":293},"content_hash":"e1783a850b4809acdb5bdac35902c22bb1d6a6f081533ae8af0931800b6edf65"},"summary":"Decision: browse has its own URL rule (`sender` by default, `allowlist`, `any_public`), independent of web.fetch's","supersedes":"7b40db959130f5b51338e16e87e2483b0feeccd52d6a751bd3b2aa96f2607a95","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:55.959302Z","id":"c08401b2cd6fe0abac69cae38bcf253c80ce8448a87b47aa7b7f915a654522f7","body":{"detail":"See the records on crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs:32:38 (the narrowing and why), browse.rs:39:44 (the resolver waiver) and crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:235 (sockets). Under any_public the section holds as written, plus the name check.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":772},"end":{"line":781},"content_hash":"47f0b711a0887cb1a12d03c850510aa510c0759a06c04c681e298ba8fdf46667"},"summary":"The code departs from §9.3: under sender and allowlist a browsed page's requests are held to the rule's hosts, names are checked by the daemon's resolver, and WebSocket and WebTransport are removed","supersedes":"16a6ba8b860baac4ca83b2ede0f39551defdd392069bb21b1ee1d790c3a62447","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:56.156741Z","id":"49a8c59e478278828f795b04cb46a56566ff9f4a578865a747ef5d7fc0933336","body":{"detail":"Inherent to computer use: `type`, `eval` and `goto` are model-written. Defences: the admin switch (off by default), both person switches (browser and web), the `sender` rule by default, the per-run browse cap, the prompt rule that page text is data. The admin page states the risk beside the switch.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":772},"end":{"line":781},"content_hash":"47f0b711a0887cb1a12d03c850510aa510c0759a06c04c681e298ba8fdf46667"},"summary":"Browsing lets a steered model type data into third-party forms, and under any_public put it in URLs","supersedes":"e688825fccfd07256447a20ee628aafe713986b56d540526c678c0fcd1cc94b5","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:56.350167Z","id":"074cebbd41025c508c586c16787257e620516c8dc14c28fcf460fdd1bfc3ff9d","body":{"detail":"Testing one's own page reaches no third party and has its own price; the web switch's scope is expected to change. One switch for both was considered; browse reaches the web, so it needs both.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":934},"end":{"line":946},"content_hash":"b7790cd3144fc37b6fd443ffe2e48fd6e48f64eaeb3a1ef27531cafcc37dcc81"},"summary":"Decision: a separate person switch for the browser (`bot_person_prefs.browser`), with browse needing the web switch too","supersedes":"e4dc1bbb842b3c8640f11809563a6a47e97d0fff881a827dba908de919b5971e","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:56.544124Z","id":"76e72a0674629848f64b327d0a9bb391174721a4ff98e08f82ef2f80b87c1953","body":{"detail":"Deferred: the Worker's content stores keep no blobs (open concern on crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs), so screenshots could not be kept, and its CDP transport is a change of its own. The Worker answers NotConfigured.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":961},"end":{"line":963},"content_hash":"0cc49be708c732bb1c6e9972450b2ba1cece2214308f9564a813f9132ce9dd57"},"summary":"Browser use on the Worker in v1 (outbound WebSocket via fetch Upgrade, or the BROWSER binding)","supersedes":"388e4d3ff7eabdda470b583b1fc01c675c4da8b6e36fbe29f299c4ea02930240","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the Worker's content store keeps blobs","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:38:56.738715Z","id":"eff3f0952838348ef08e555829e720c3d044cbf1332945fe7df1bd3e76e10e55","body":{"detail":"No route today lets the shell read a run's content (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot_content.rs serves hosts with the daemon token). The plan adds GET /api/bot/runs/<run>/content/<id> for whoever may view the run, images only, under a sandbox CSP. A 'Tested' list in finish, like web's Sources, is a follow-up.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":975},"end":{"line":979},"content_hash":"ad77ff1bfdf76f0132967f3f410748bbaeb45f179a4824bec45e24e61317beb5"},"summary":"Run-panel thumbnails need a new person-facing content route","supersedes":"7281343205961fccb9c7539b6784a9da46b5da4991806907786f42e275f139db","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.062624Z","id":"93ed4cd2fa4bdf0ae1cbaef6e547ddf2ce35bfe8990eefd2ea27012395c17053","body":{"detail":"The owner decided on 2026-11-19: \"Unify clax.browser and web.fetch infrastructure / APIs.\" and \"Billing is different for just retrieving page contents vs. actively running a browser. The API should reflect this.\" The spec now builds both families on one mechanism (section 4, lines 181-380: capabilities computed one way, one URL rule type, one Spend path, one error style, one audit kind, one Cloudflare credential), with clax.web for retrieval charged per request and clax.browser for a running browser charged by browser time (section 4.1, lines 183-191). Section 15 lines 1038-1039 lists this decision as replaced. Proposed for the owner to close as obsolete.","kind":"comment","references":"d69c778b05346db138579fb292cccbb37b6cffdfe61a656b726bb998c2d3fcb6","summary":"Overturned by the owner: one mechanism under web and browser, two families by billing","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.063569Z","id":"b42ca32385e93ebc323fbeb5df1b499630e2d14d7ff936b496a563fa100df5a7","body":{"detail":"The owner decided on 2026-11-19: \"Why is this one grant? They're different capabilities.\" and \"We should also be able to provide dynamic content _to_ the browser and let ClaxBot navigate / screenshot / etc.\" clax.browser.browse is gone (section 6.8, lines 627-628); a public URL is opened with clax.browser.open({url}) under the capability browser.open.url, off by default (section 4.2 lines 193-212, section 11.1 lines 912-915), and worked one turn at a time through the session operations (section 6). Proposed for the owner to close as obsolete.","kind":"comment","references":"e1455c5f3807e932d4e5c31154430ab414d9e0d3d9efc3bacf25139edd1a5f78","summary":"Overturned by the owner: browse is replaced by browser.open({url}) under its own capability","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.064222Z","id":"2fcf81d10f602fc105191c731bbc3071cff48ca4c08d624f05949b767146e741","body":{"detail":"The owner decided on 2026-11-19: \"Why is this one grant? They're different capabilities.\" and \"browser.open should work on the clax content itself even without web.fetch permission.\" The person now grants or revokes each of web.search, web.fetch, browser.open.url, browser.open.artifact and browser.open.content on its own (section 11.2, lines 934-946; computed as in section 4.3, lines 214-246); no capability needs another, so opening a URL no longer needs the web switch and opening the run's clax or supplied content needs neither web.fetch nor browser.open.url (section 4.2, lines 203-209). bot_person_prefs.browser goes away. Proposed for the owner to close as obsolete.","kind":"comment","references":"074cebbd41025c508c586c16787257e620516c8dc14c28fcf460fdd1bfc3ff9d","summary":"Overturned by the owner: one person grant per capability, and none needs another","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.064866Z","id":"a919f9a4a6057d61042893b3608e7ca998d326099187832397dd3e74773d4ef2","body":{"detail":"The owner decided on 2026-11-19: \"Unify clax.browser and web.fetch infrastructure / APIs.\" and \"Why is this one grant? They're different capabilities.\" There is now one UrlRule type (section 4.5, lines 266-293) with the values sender, sourced, allowlist and any_public, granted separately to web.fetch (web.fetch.url_rule, default sourced as on main) and browser.open.url (browser.open.url.url_rule, default sender), whose rule also governs a goto out of a session (section 8.5). What stays of this decision: the browser's rule is its own grant with its own stricter default. What changes: browse's allowlist of hosts alone is not kept (allowlist means sourced and on the listed hosts, main's meaning), and sourced becomes available to the browser.","kind":"comment","references":"2d74a7508cb87f4a38651548c7383c7afb3224b6a36366b29c16ec1c030f93aa","summary":"Changed by the owner: one URL rule type, granted separately to fetch and to browser.open.url","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.065443Z","id":"f4a0b4c0889482b814e9a8b2a173efe9fcc1f09632661cff8635911270acf4b8","body":{"detail":"Section 8.4, lines 772-781, now says what crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs does: under sender, sourced and allowlist every request a page makes is held to the hosts the session was admitted to (leading www. ignored) or the allowlist's; names are checked by the host's resolver, at most 64 a session; WebSocket and WebTransport are removed by the preamble. The resolver gap is in the waiver at lines 787-791. Proposed for the owner to close as fixed.","kind":"comment","references":"c08401b2cd6fe0abac69cae38bcf253c80ce8448a87b47aa7b7f915a654522f7","summary":"The revised spec states the code's behaviour for URL sessions","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.066005Z","id":"5997381d5fdbf087c259ba26b2bafe1ef23702288eae09b74f8ce7c06af26257","body":{"detail":"With sessions that live across steps (section 6.3), section 10.3 (lines 863-896) charges browser time in contiguous segments: each session call charges from the session's charged-through point to its end, a host's end charges the rest once (Store::end_browser_session). Quantities are milliseconds and nothing is rounded up per call, since rounding each of many short calls up to a second would overcharge. The pre-check (lines 891-895) now covers the time not yet charged, the call's time cap and the idle time, and a refusal closes the session.","kind":"comment","references":"49c6bb43159f4ed4937ae457ac3113aa8c2df59902083f200190af0b20ea256e","summary":"Changed by section 10.3: millisecond segments per session call, no rounding, a wider pre-check","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.066540Z","id":"8d7c7fdb01960301c66fb03ba0ad7c5c7cecd72d20f7d3e13bcb895f058ae61e","body":{"detail":"A session now stays open across model turns, so Browser Run's inactivity timeout must not end it between calls. Section 7.2 (lines 664-680) asks keep_alive=60000 and has the host send Browser.getVersion after 20 s without a command while a session is open; the orphan of a daemon crash lives at most keep_alive. Section 10.3 lines 885-888: the time after the last charged point is the instance's loss and a starting daemon marks the session lost.","kind":"comment","references":"70f545711f859101ee0d277a670f893439b81eacaa266a1e8ffff14dd9ed4df7","summary":"Changed by section 7.2: keep_alive is 60 s with a heartbeat, so an orphan lives at most a minute","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.067111Z","id":"83e9b1ee06d9166fa88149df3c7c6cea138c36cf0648f72a39b11c1825b78ac3","body":{"detail":"The accepted risk applies to sessions opened on a URL (section 8.4, lines 772-781) and to a goto that leaves an artifact or content session (section 8.5, lines 793-804), which needs browser.open.url and passes its rule. Artifact and content sessions that never leave their origin reach their synthetic origin alone and are outside this waiver.","kind":"comment","references":"49a8c59e478278828f795b04cb46a56566ff9f4a578865a747ef5d7fc0933336","summary":"Still holds, now for URL sessions and for a goto out of any session","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.067683Z","id":"25e76947cbe29255bd2d2ad9e43b761e40b1bec8e3979e3a7807fb9609d3b40c","body":{"detail":"See the reply on e1455c5f: clax.browser.browse is replaced by browser.open({url}) under browser.open.url (section 11.1, lines 912-915). Proposed for the owner to close as obsolete.","kind":"comment","references":"4f9da6258be5b60e60c69f0990ff9dc9c5bb7ffb05989f61b0cf30e7310c39eb","summary":"Obsolete: browsing a URL is now its own capability, browser.open.url, off by default","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070527Z","id":"cc4ff90eff18ce3a263b4a09e24ea8b0a56e02d141bb6011b99e2f60e9f7beeb","body":{"detail":"Section 4.3 reads a missing bot_person_caps row as the person's grant being live, so an admin turning a capability on gives it to every person's runs at once. That keeps main's behaviour for the web switch (on by default wherever offered, web section 9.2) and needs no write on a read path. The zero-capability design on spec/zero-capability-gnap (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-17-zero-capability-gnap-design.md there) has no implicit defaults: a person would hold nothing until they turned each capability on, or a recorded selector grant issued theirs at a recorded event. Options: (a) keep the default on, as written; (b) default off, every person turns each capability on; (c) the admin chooses per capability whether people's runs hold it until they turn it off or only once they turn it on.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":232},"end":{"line":237},"content_hash":"ab0e46c19900c82a96dc288e11363d777003f292fdc6cdf42b77c49e960a91cb"},"summary":"A person who never chose holds every capability the admin offers, unlike strict zero-capability","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070580Z","id":"d848c013399becb3a95af01330cd07b02f4873096605f66936a905f3f476f316","body":{"detail":"The owner named two price lines, per request and per browser second. Web keeps main's lines (one per search provider, and web.fetch); every browser.open kind is charged on browser.time, since a second of browser costs the instance the same whatever the page. Each capability still has its own grant, cap and switch.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":211},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"4874123bbf61e4bfe5f8c112580662b09046cd0e817ddc883d700450a3543efa"},"summary":"Decision: the three browser.open kinds share one price line, browser.time, per browser second","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070637Z","id":"1343b77cfdeabd9fa313588a0739cfad48545057e359d81d20ae1aac0909a125","body":{"detail":"Would let an admin price testing its own claxen below browsing the web. Not taken: the owner named two price lines, and the instance's cost per browser second does not depend on the source.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1047},"end":{"line":1048},"content_hash":"8a634466987457dc6bde1df80f387a1e31f31112b9791cd78f389617c320da4d"},"summary":"A price line per browser.open kind (browser.time.url, .artifact, .content)","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:an admin asks to price browser kinds apart","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070676Z","id":"d163aa8237a73d237fb1cefe3e30f757454689de157ab143ca987b291e63f541","body":{"detail":"capability::Capabilities::now(store, person, configured) replaces WebAccess::now and BrowserAccess::now. It answers per capability its terms or why it is off. The union of grants has one path today (admin to person to run); the zero-capability store, when it lands, adds grants to the union without changing callers.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":246},"content_hash":"ab71446676852a82e9c371e8ebd9b85462d65163924c7e98e9df27800a178026"},"summary":"Decision: one function computes a run's capabilities from the admin's grant, the person's grant and the source, per capability","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070712Z","id":"df067c3ca60396ba237d183b0ae612cbd03f319c80a35da94b6d550bb0de82b2","body":{"detail":"bot_runs.caps keeps the capabilities live when the run was made, so the prompt and its declaration stay fixed (the prompt cache). Each call re-evaluates. A grant change on the daemon (admin or Me PUT) calls BrowserSessions::reevaluate, which closes and charges every session whose run lost its capability, so a session is treated as state held under a capability. A config file change takes effect at the daemon's next start.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":248},"end":{"line":264},"content_hash":"d8850b6283acc107fdd2cb8cfefdd59978cb330186800a718109f48287a309ad"},"summary":"Decision: declared when the run is made, re-evaluated at each call, and a revoke closes open sessions before it answers","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070747Z","id":"e601beb497b58b6966fdca4907a2c1e97e409bf3afd2b6773617cdc9b0d31df4","body":{"detail":"Main's three values keep their meaning so existing web.fetch settings migrate untouched. The browser's default is the stricter sender because a browser session types, clicks and runs the page's scripts. The first version's browse allowlist (hosts alone, no source needed) is dropped so that allowlist means one thing for both capabilities.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":287},"end":{"line":293},"content_hash":"a44f7a1e98ffb1188ba5092eb30f28d94c8d8120ed10cc3c9de95e2551b5e94b"},"summary":"Decision: UrlRule gains sender for every URL-taking capability; browser.open.url defaults to sender, web.fetch keeps sourced","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070782Z","id":"327dcb389ff388cbdabf435800d538202db4fcaf32fa80a4408a7b00fcd04b0c","body":{"detail":"Would let a computer-use loop goto a link it read in a page. Not taken: clicking already follows a page's own links within the session's egress rule, and recording a session's links would need a page store of its own.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1056},"end":{"line":1057},"content_hash":"58f2c0c061025c4821224b24e91772e0603e94a14d401b687a4c412cad5d511c"},"summary":"Links in pages a browser session showed count as URL sources for sourced and allowlist","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a computer-use flow needs to goto a link it saw rather than click it","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070816Z","id":"a95888d5c5803abd90e52226e30029c4060e4a20ecdc4416686defc2841ccae6","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":296},"end":{"line":329},"content_hash":"22d0cef6c7904f361cf333fc9a2759e3fa98df6799b87aef871feadd72277542"},"summary":"Decision: one Spend sequence in clax/spend.rs with a Performer per operation, replacing the two copies in clax/web.rs and clax/browser.rs","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070851Z","id":"b4b539ce56d8f4d4b43be7a9d96a1229a6b2faad752f27a78fea5649f19a9c1f","body":{"detail":"An action that fails on the page is an answer (ok: false), not an error, so a computer-use loop can look and retry. browser_session_lost (the browser is gone: restart, dropped socket, crash) and browser_session_closed (an end of section 6.3, reason in the message) are neither retryable nor counted; the script opens a new session.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":331},"end":{"line":358},"content_hash":"f9d6140b94185db60f3b33898fcd538067d0105d1ff531a6e6880de272c17be8"},"summary":"Decision: codes are <family>_<condition>, shared where the condition is one; errors carry retryable and the capability; a session adds browser_session_lost and browser_session_closed","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070883Z","id":"bc335300ca9792f71348fd9c22832bcaabec37553e3543e64f620c8df9befcb6","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":371},"content_hash":"bffcb889edd31547b441d9d94e5aea22ae3f7bad36da2ea8e15ad2bad842f976"},"summary":"Decision: one audit kind, bot.spend, for every capability call; bot.web rows stay and are read as bot.spend","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070918Z","id":"bdeaba36c140d7d13447dff1588504cd1a82287efc3a49a5319e4b9b4463c7a5","body":{"detail":"Would leave main's audit rows and any reader of the kind untouched. Not taken: the kind would misname every browser record. bot.spend with a capability field names all of them, and the audit page's filter reads old bot.web rows with it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":371},"content_hash":"bffcb889edd31547b441d9d94e5aea22ae3f7bad36da2ea8e15ad2bad842f976"},"summary":"Keep bot.web as the one audit kind and have browser calls write it too","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:an outside reader of the audit trail depends on the kind bot.web","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070950Z","id":"c5971758f97dc3534059da7dcdc93f2ca0f14808b305e639d386f926d2e5ca41","body":{"detail":"html is the markup decoded to UTF-8 with script, style, noscript, template, comments and event-handler attributes removed and links absolute: the page's structure without code a model would never run. raw stays main's body as it came. auto stays accepted as markdown so main's scripts and journals answer the same. A page store keyed by URL alone could not answer two formats of one page, so migration 67 rebuilds bot_web_pages with the format in its key.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":388},"end":{"line":409},"content_hash":"2f3e7c31858fb869efc3cd8d959b1d01857048f0857253ab1655479892d42bb8"},"summary":"Decision: fetch answers markdown (the default, main's auto), html (cleaned markup, no scripts or styles) or raw; the page store keeps a page per URL and format","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070989Z","id":"633b7b5e16a4591f3a6c383632a6a9666524faba0e883eacb615b1cf8d690141","body":{"detail":"The surface format declares functions of namespaces and the sandboxes pass JSON values (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js), so a value cannot carry methods without a prelude change in every sandbox (clax-bot-js and the Worker's driver).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":415},"end":{"line":417},"content_hash":"b96a22115be87a3a94de1e097812b6c29bf241235c0fd3a7927929f826fef983"},"summary":"Decision: a session is a string handle taken by operations of the browser namespace, not an object with methods","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071069Z","id":"1c6d544d542cc4e97aafe71a21006832c5fd3628a370cb4e4fc55d8d8a14eb40","body":{"detail":"Reads as the owner wrote it. Not taken: every sandbox's prelude would have to wrap handles in objects whose methods call the namespace's operations, a change to the surface format's contract for one namespace.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1044},"end":{"line":1046},"content_hash":"863ea37e2300ed6d8790e6691474d16845805137086077271943f60ec82d9790"},"summary":"Session methods on the value open answers (s.click(...)), made by the prelude","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the surface format gains values with methods","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071204Z","id":"b2f849b966321abd308838c1afef4de55af15fa9d14daf19830492bbd11e3a35","body":{"detail":"The journal keeps an argument hash (CallEntry::args_hash), so content is never written to the store; a replayed open answers from the journal and a later call on a lost session fails rather than reloading content Clax no longer has. Image handles let a script show run content without copying bytes.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":499},"end":{"line":506},"content_hash":"7295515450ec0c526bb369e38fbc85142504daed6dd8ac88f2966ed0eaad756a"},"summary":"Decision: supplied content is held only in the session, has no bridge and no page runtime API, and is capped at 2 MiB of HTML and 16 MiB of files","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071261Z","id":"87804b1affdf53cd6b799f5593f9f6ccf93768fd74bcc3c2e84f08a40bc03864","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":508},"end":{"line":526},"content_hash":"7bf935cadae72e2168cc2d583e108aa42eba77eb5ec7b5e6cc76aa542a27a10f"},"summary":"Decision: a session ends on close, 300 s idle, 1,800 s open, a revoke, a credits refusal or the run's end","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071307Z","id":"26eff3494dcc4bd159785a97f0295762aee8cc656d7e8921adec1317eadb58cd","body":{"detail":"A click or type is not idempotent: when a step's attempt performed a call and failed before the Spend transaction wrote it (a store error), the retried attempt performs it again on the live session. Web fetches have the same window (web section 4.2). Closing it would need a per-call idempotency key the browser cannot honour.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":544},"end":{"line":546},"content_hash":"95e855cb6fd9f8c342002a454f116f30d88a36cdb4f42a1d9fc9203c103343f5"},"summary":"A step retried by the same process performs again a session call whose first attempt was performed but not journaled","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071351Z","id":"c448d9567426ee66444bc5481ceee33f9745a98445a2258691e519b93e0606b5","body":{"detail":"Needs no decoder or encoder in Clax, no new crate, and builds for the Worker unchanged. The model sees at most four frames as images.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":588},"end":{"line":597},"content_hash":"7624638c8e4e3e4c0328f2a9eb880afdf80db8a9d97ec2267075015a1963a377"},"summary":"Decision: a recording is a sequence of the JPEG frames Chrome's screencast sends, with a JSON manifest, played by the run panel as a flipbook","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071392Z","id":"accfbb57e530eddaf2f9ad53bd558718fb7f82f2806df5921e3bf64bd0e5256e","body":{"detail":"One file people can download or attach. Not taken now: GIF needs two new crates and daemon CPU and has 256 colours; MediaRecorder needs a second page in the session driven by a canvas, adding a moving part to every recording.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1054},"end":{"line":1055},"content_hash":"ae3deb231bdcb9b838170ff9c7d46781697456031481c4c5527ccf8dd1d92c5b"},"summary":"Encode a recording as an animated GIF (gif and a JPEG decoder, pure Rust) or as WebM made by the browser's MediaRecorder","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a clip must leave Clax as one file, attached to a reply or downloaded","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071439Z","id":"0a6381ce383a31856ca2762c54b5ba48e06713a6696ff0bbf62fe6e0bff824b3","body":{"detail":"A thinking model keeps its browser slot for up to the idle time (300 s), so with browser.max_concurrent at 2 two runs with open sessions refuse every other open (browser_busy, retryable). The admin raises max_concurrent or lowers the idle time.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":599},"end":{"line":609},"content_hash":"827cb1fc06a9d4c608b54e893515eab23c0061427b408df7786580bd13d71498"},"summary":"Decision: one open session per run by default (up to 4), and the instance's two browsers are held until a session ends","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071480Z","id":"95e6aeb25180b381d7683936b7c42f97706e0f4b51791f984fe632f2b03a9e2b","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":664},"end":{"line":680},"content_hash":"e17c489c805eb26923a8388d7d61b585ed2321f63480f5ac55af574e3377f45a"},"summary":"Decision: keep_alive 60 s and a heartbeat after 20 s without a command, rather than a keep_alive as long as a model turn","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071518Z","id":"d48cf9c081dca001c78a937f6fcacf86d1795206f05d601778ecca11e6c69a29","body":{"detail":"Section 7.2 assumes keep_alive bounds the time without DevTools commands, so a heartbeat keeps a session alive and an orphan lives at most keep_alive. If keep_alive instead runs only after the socket drops, the heartbeat is harmless and the orphan bound still holds; if Browser Run also ends a browser after a fixed lifetime shorter than browser.session.max_seconds, sessions end early and answer browser_session_lost. Only the opt-in live test (just browser-live) can check; it has not been run against Cloudflare.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":666},"end":{"line":670},"content_hash":"a0a715c6352748687ec7c5a172a788480f34050154ae19caea37ac3e7683ee7f"},"summary":"Browser Run's keep_alive semantics and maximum are unchecked: whether it counts inactivity of commands or time after the socket drops, and whether its maximum is 20 minutes","tags":["claxbot-browser","risk","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071560Z","id":"e3f5545029b0e541880dacc2bcfdaafbe8a2246706ea47bd038f6deb298b6c34","body":{"detail":"Simpler: no timer in the host. Not taken: a browser orphaned by a daemon crash would bill up to the idle time (300 s, up to 20 minutes), and a model turn longer than Browser Run's maximum would lose the session.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1051},"end":{"line":1053},"content_hash":"45853c944a7add77a77d21c5f607b16a4c6c271b4be24e7b4bc9eda1addd12fb"},"summary":"Set keep_alive to the session's idle time (at most Browser Run's maximum) and send no heartbeat","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:Browser Run bills or limits heartbeat commands","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071599Z","id":"b7c5fd90542c5e146733cbab9887d1c7c592c476309f64d0b3801ff77128e6fe","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":696},"end":{"line":717},"content_hash":"c3d3ee0d211a03140b3e41e0c4ab7cc81c109864c29ccdd7d57c7804913e7e8a"},"summary":"Decision: open sessions live in a host-owned registry of tasks that own their sockets, serve requests between calls, heartbeat and end themselves","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071636Z","id":"ef116de509ce3dbb73d201e6c2d0cd4eeb8743a0e860d0a05d4b603930599d41","body":{"detail":"So the artifact's read-only API and supplied content are never reachable from a page that can reach the web, and the conversion counts against the URL cap. A goto within the origin needs nothing more.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":793},"end":{"line":804},"content_hash":"b437efa7c240a233221a27dffe98c427f4b5ceb460635f4a00ca2a6eb3c7439a"},"summary":"Decision: a goto out of an artifact or content session needs browser.open.url, converts the session once, and stops serving its synthetic origin","tags":["claxbot-browser","security","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071676Z","id":"83274b4332fece9ba1e12eb83293c10b43c94470ac5dd6618d3d4c1039b35e53","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":863},"end":{"line":896},"content_hash":"70c28cedb2d33bde748043264f70bc223852edb35b592492e9f1fbbaa7b215c8"},"summary":"Decision: browser time is charged in contiguous millisecond segments, each session call charging up to its end and a host's end charging the rest once","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071715Z","id":"63bbbbabc812c2686c61dc78a7cf634927b3c33a166e452dee5a1299d93e2c77","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":900},"end":{"line":932},"content_hash":"183bee25f6c6f4bf6dea81fc1e039ce8e11472a804574476398508bb3669b833"},"summary":"Decision: main's web.* settings stay as they are; the first version's browser.* settings are renamed per capability","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.071754Z","id":"dbf6a832f7f422765f298354d15331f71e65509da337a235056645acdd083337","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":935},"end":{"line":946},"content_hash":"0b184399a7fdca375b945bb2862bf30ba80f8155d3e9c3a2ee300ef04d408395"},"summary":"Decision: person grants in bot_person_caps, one row per choice; main's web switch off becomes web.search and web.fetch rows off","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:43:45.788923Z","id":"524d8b6bef0cc3bee7d559e8299aab71c734e31d28a733aaffb7488e3a46839a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"eff3f0952838348ef08e555829e720c3d044cbf1332945fe7df1bd3e76e10e55","span":{"start":{"line":975},"end":{"line":979},"content_hash":"ad77ff1bfdf76f0132967f3f410748bbaeb45f179a4824bec45e24e61317beb5"},"summary":"Built: GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/content/<item> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs run_content), image items of that run of the four raster types only, under Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src 'none' and nosniff, 404 otherwise. Tests: api_claxbot::run_content_is_served_to_the_runs_viewers_only, api_claxbot::a_non_image_item_is_not_served. It admits the person the run acts for and admins who read its artifact, not readers (see the alternative on run_content).","supersedes":"924556dfa4b400124b8f787b73b5ea35bb09bfcfd8d32f00cc0442a937cd73ef","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:47:58.620494Z","id":"2a97d6203b3b135dfbe6d127beaae4bd43a3edb6b801ad57d3945935bbd9862e","body":{"detail":"web.fetch's URL-source rule (crates/clax-bot/src/web/access.rs `sources`), Markdown conversion, page store and `WebSource` are not used, because the web tools' scope is expected to be loosened (raw HTML, not only Markdown). Only generic machinery is reused: `Access::Spend` and `Store::spend_journaled` (crates/clax-store/src/bot_web.rs), credits, settings, the sealed Cloudflare credentials, run content. The web-named pieces it needs are generalised in place (§4.6). Design decision for the owner to confirm or overturn.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1087},"end":{"line":1088},"content_hash":"d834d6317c0b68bf4d7501bc9808c4610d82db56dfea4a3cf5a86ef8ee16ad88"},"summary":"Decision: the browser is its own `clax.browser` namespace with its own grant, settings, codes, cost line and audit kind, built on none of web.fetch's internals","supersedes":"d69c778b05346db138579fb292cccbb37b6cffdfe61a656b726bb998c2d3fcb6","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:47:58.817289Z","id":"3dcfa2c1229fcf51535857b0ea386d9fd50c2e5872756e9177b4cfd123a2dbad","body":{"detail":"Rejected for v1: Quick Actions return no console messages or page errors, run no actions (click, type, assertions), and make Cloudflare fetch the page itself, which cannot reach a private artifact or a daemon on localhost. CDP with Fetch-domain interception (§4.3, §6) serves the page from the host instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":666},"end":{"line":670},"content_hash":"807ae5b3522eaac112f1473fc9d75f9d06e9c523a221cc95d6ec2115ccf41b26"},"summary":"Quick Actions REST (/screenshot, /content, /scrape) instead of CDP over a WebSocket","supersedes":"7ec11e93dd3b7eb6c3727627dc2805d43b1cfcc7573b113dde11ef8bca7ef2b7","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:Browser Run's REST API gains console, errors and request interception","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:47:59.012189Z","id":"9497ae5b7e443b3801fcae9886aa46ba3cefedef25e45edc18acf59dd2553732","body":{"detail":"The endpoint is wss://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/{id}/browser-run/devtools/browser per the 2026-11 docs, but other pages of the same docs use `browser-rendering`. The design makes it one constant (`BROWSER_RUN_PATH`) pinned by the daemon test against a fake server, which cannot tell which spelling Cloudflare accepts: only the opt-in live test (`just browser-live`) can. If Cloudflare answers 404 on the upgrade, switch the constant.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":666},"end":{"line":668},"content_hash":"6a2e226dedb88600452b1c9947f520f60123ebce3e1d14f24032899c5880990b"},"summary":"Browser Run's docs spell the CDP path segment both `browser-run` and `browser-rendering`","supersedes":"88b76c21d24850e57b353726771261f79c87479039d36a6eb5f98b3eca723bc9","tags":["claxbot-browser","risk","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:47:59.206141Z","id":"10110aad8758e535ea07e20c7a67e894acba94e2398bf5471a23c6b6d93f7db6","body":{"detail":"The session ends the browser itself (`Browser.close`) on every path out of the driver; a process that dies cannot. keep_alive is set to its minimum (10 s) and Browser Run's idle timeout is 60 s, so an orphan costs at most about a browser-minute ($0.0015 at list price), absorbed by the instance and not charged to the person (the Spend transaction never ran).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":912},"end":{"line":915},"content_hash":"4bd18242a8b6a06aae591c550c865171dae22e229799396965aebe64f4684abe"},"summary":"A browser orphaned by a daemon crash mid-test stays on Browser Run until keep_alive or the idle timeout, billed to the instance","supersedes":"70f545711f859101ee0d277a670f893439b81eacaa266a1e8ffff14dd9ed4df7","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:47:59.398680Z","id":"12c2abdf4989fa28c2649a033fbc2ad671c5323eebf9da4bd23c6b7d841ee1ac","body":{"detail":"Keeps the policy host-independent and testable against an in-memory fake Chrome, as `WebSource` did for web (spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §4.3). `clax_core::wrap` and the store are reachable from clax-bot, so the page set is built there; the bridge's hashed part files, the site CSP (clax-http) and `/_clax/api/` are the server's, so they are trait methods. Check against scripts/check-crate-layers.py: no new crate edge.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":709},"end":{"line":721},"content_hash":"a4021daa009fe5dee0fdb2750ac060c80cd5b0eeacb902774962fdb6e8a40abf"},"summary":"Decision: the CDP driver, request policy, steps and result shaping live in clax-bot `browser/`; a host provides only a `CdpTransport`, Clax's UI files, the site's headers and its read-only API","supersedes":"9fe06730836715bc4b39e0d8c82c7b7c48e8187ff62f67f841263f913afa0f04","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:47:59.594004Z","id":"01d8b9d8ebd4f20a4c018bbd89ae353952d491977544b89f22687352973ab8d0","body":{"detail":"One Cloudflare account per instance; the token gains the Browser Rendering - Edit permission. The setting's key stays web-named; the admin pages label it \"Cloudflare account\".","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":400},"end":{"line":407},"content_hash":"8fd63349173de04dd6c72509ad7923474ee83f9c2eff529cb01f6879b91622e5"},"summary":"Decision: reuse `web.cloudflare.account_id` and `SecretSlot::Cloudflare` for Browser Run rather than adding browser credentials","supersedes":"6e85a317d5866e87a5d9d7b06018eda4c679a781e1a5acad341e8678de0f1b05","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:47:59.786452Z","id":"b6f592e4f1ca006c63a6f7ffdac3de10b4fc212b95e4bac8cefeb06605d5901e","body":{"detail":"Not now: a key rename needs a migration of stored settings and of `[bot.web]` config overrides, unrelated to the browser. The browser reads the existing key.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":407},"end":{"line":407},"content_hash":"454c17a4c3102d022cf09d105884a29f31c51fad288774fbc535910eb7ac893a"},"summary":"Rename the setting `web.cloudflare.account_id` to `cloudflare.account_id`, shared by web and browser","supersedes":"c97268ac3c6bed0088503678c143209731668f70af27e8670fb73e0217d2227c","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a third Cloudflare-backed feature reads the account ID","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:47:59.981127Z","id":"0d42ab4c283b6adad244f845cb30c2f44e006c116dfb36cf006ba80089fe616a","body":{"detail":"`.invalid` never resolves (RFC 6761), so a request that escapes interception fails closed; https makes it a secure context like the real site. Fulfilling https requests from Fetch.requestPaused is standard CDP practice but untested against Browser Run until the live test runs.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":748},"end":{"line":757},"content_hash":"9a77ec62bb7868200ed0a55446654500bd368413d4c2fadf8c6c133b3f91813e"},"summary":"Decision: claxen load at https://<artifact ID>.clax-test.invalid/, every request answered by the host through the CDP Fetch domain","supersedes":"5169d27aa537cf4c40813dfe43e5e53f77ebdfe2216ec76b6865804cac44a196","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:00.177919Z","id":"d67a96b9f3265a2eaa85fbc17138a35578670d963e7f20ad8c4b9fb40dbb3ce4","body":{"detail":"v1 answers GETs as the run's person and refuses writes (403 read_only_test), so a test never changes people's documents; a page whose first render writes shows that failure. The scratch copy needs a hidden draft artifact per test and its cleanup.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":781},"end":{"line":786},"content_hash":"254873fb34a94bb19ca34727f047f95b0bd8cea8a052ea5a54bb452051f6c80d"},"summary":"A writable scratch copy of the artifact's documents during a test, as the Clax app's drafts make (POST /api/drafts), instead of a read-only /_clax/api/","supersedes":"b2d7c91de7c01b6afed224002435ee036bed44f104542e3c32f0c708d08b41c0","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:ClaxBot tests a db-writing page and the read-only refusals hide real failures","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:00.369847Z","id":"715c679819b2a6cb9d1a3a2eb42ddb196ed8a921c7ec2125cf8fada07d1002f1","body":{"detail":"Clax's page contract serves every page under `default-src 'self' data: blob:` (docs/contract.md, \"Sites\"), so no CDN host can load on the real site; an allowlist would let a test pass where the page fails for its viewers. Navigations, which CSP does not govern, are failed at the Fetch domain; CSP refusals are reported through a securitypolicyviolation listener. Departs from the earlier idea of a page-contract CDN allowlist: there is no such list in Clax.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":790},"end":{"line":798},"content_hash":"c9668f84333a38be10644f1b0b9a307b3c9532870903b2cb1d7164a5935c8c04"},"summary":"Decision: no CDN allowlist; a page under test reaches its synthetic origin alone, every other request (navigations included) is failed and reported","supersedes":"980c1d88178e97a4211f5ee2b05f06bc450034ddfbc15c0f49c969b290683ebf","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:00.561751Z","id":"a7102a1274dcca562caf215b9fe5a4bf123fdaa8583028e56059e19b8a45fc72","body":{"detail":"Chrome's DNS prefetch and preconnect happen outside the CDP Fetch domain and outside CSP, so a page under test can make Browser Run's resolver look up <data>.evil.example. WebRTC is closed by the preamble removing RTCPeerConnection; DNS is not closable from CDP. The artifact's content, documents read through /_clax/api/, and screenshots are processed by Cloudflare as a sub-processor, as search queries already are. Accepted: a person viewing the page in their own browser has the same DNS channel.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":814},"end":{"line":818},"content_hash":"22050267ef151e4e86d03973c03db3e6ed480c547415a803e74ea3653b51d542"},"summary":"DNS prefetch, speculative connections and Cloudflare's processing of the page stay open as channels","supersedes":"4b64bc2d9dcb4a52759e009dde592c477cde4d2db15f73fb9d3d94d587f4cce3","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:00.755252Z","id":"e2781516bd65e394063ef0e2d380b55fa7c4922c0ae502112e2cd13ed0fcaa49","body":{"detail":"Rejected: the Clax app's inspect view already runs `tests/<name>.test.js` with the bridge harness (docs/contract.md \"The inspect view\", web/bridge/src/harness.ts). A second format would be less expressive and not run by the app. `steps` remain for one-call checks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":837},"end":{"line":842},"content_hash":"c149b0bcda665c0facd51069cc716bce47b468a603bf32e400306ef9a84777ba"},"summary":"A declarative JSON test file in the `steps` format for durable tests","supersedes":"a92abf1ece99d74225d479c8261ec954a86432d77e78cc7ee82c4308c223e26d","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the harness's JS tests prove hard for ClaxBot to write correctly","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:00.950053Z","id":"12891c7e20d7dc7081902e3065d6e24db9dd8d14d8a5b406c3666a7b21994bfa","body":{"detail":"The driver evaluates a fixed expression against a hook defined only when window.name is `clax-test`. A bridge change that renames or reshapes it breaks browser tests silently unless the fake-Chrome test of the expression and the bridge unit test of the hook agree. The hook adds bytes to the eager bridge, which is already over its gzip budget (thread 1014d9d7 on web/bridge/src/bridge.ts): keep it a few lines that delegate to the test part.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":852},"end":{"line":859},"content_hash":"106abefc8c1e97e1be133761228e4c6bae1251f5423f8a6822454cb970470cfb"},"summary":"The bridge hook `window.claxTest.run` couples ClaxBot's driver to the bridge's lazy test part and to an eager-bridge byte budget","supersedes":"2502441776618b87bbe82688891ec89857022b9c05955ced4d3c59636f0c4df1","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:01.144077Z","id":"23711ea8a62a1b21b3387662fcaab434a53cd220c4ed7950c168d43e10dc8378","body":{"detail":"The run panel shows ClaxBot's test results; the Clax app's inspect view runs the same files on its drafts; nothing in the web shell lets an artifact's owner run `tests/*.test.js`. Follow-up: a Run tests button on the artifact page (needs a browser-run route outside a ClaxBot run, and who pays for it).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":861},"end":{"line":865},"content_hash":"e5343ec1efbd1e1d93c39a987dad48bef180e7dac9a343da1b840b6bd68d6a4a"},"summary":"People cannot run an artifact's tests themselves in v1","supersedes":"ade240242ebe30f5d8ac8e69b0e4fe2162d0bbb1dc763c6be041d8fbf517bf63","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:deferred","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:01.336223Z","id":"1ff93cc8d189c2aa828bb35b1bffdb7975940d6c6ba082a9c28bb53dfb25b1cf","body":{"detail":"Cloudflare bills $2.00 per concurrent browser beyond 10 (monthly average) on top of browser-hours. It cannot be attributed to one test, so `browser.time` charges hours only. `browser.max_concurrent` (default 2) bounds the exposure.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":876},"end":{"line":878},"content_hash":"0273cefcc1826cc463dd8683f592fddaa23dfec27d5a4397e99ac08c270c3db9"},"summary":"Browser Run's concurrency charge is not metered per test; the instance absorbs it","supersedes":"82070d4abb9462b68041d69ffd33fe64e89da657f1007d4dc3d6cf3f0b96a098","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:01.529458Z","id":"17ccb6496251b28c81eb9287de2ad400c53512a445ca19f2941e9187f1d9da6d","body":{"detail":"The time cap bounds what one test can cost, so a person cannot run past their week mid-test; at list price a 60 s cap is 0.0015 USD. Measured from the WebSocket upgrade to its close by the provider's injected clock. A test that never opened (401, 429, socket error, browser_busy) is not charged but counts toward the cap when it reached Browser Run.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":918},"end":{"line":922},"content_hash":"b51ee6cca45203d59ad1ba1ae79bc08ff083181629ff8f6040a909ddfb4eafb6"},"summary":"Decision: pre-check that the person can pay for the call's whole time cap, not the minimum charge; charge measured time rounded up to the second, whenever a browser opened","supersedes":"49c6bb43159f4ed4937ae457ac3113aa8c2df59902083f200190af0b20ea256e","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:01.721163Z","id":"aa7f2a1571452f03d3288968ee7679aec2e54b65edd2d0ed36cb48a541386397","body":{"detail":"Not taken: little marginal code, off by default, and it exercises the computer-use path the owner wants kept open.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":939},"end":{"line":942},"content_hash":"d881a43ce2d3a7bb2bd7190592a416aba4859345ddf5246a4a3b3a0c44577d03"},"summary":"Defer browsing public URLs to a later version","supersedes":"4f9da6258be5b60e60c69f0990ff9dc9c5bb7ffb05989f61b0cf30e7310c39eb","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the browse phase slips or its waiver is judged too wide before release","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:01.919385Z","id":"e99783dff572741676bc4aca17b5fd95d10be981119bcd66388b944ad9fc36cd","body":{"detail":"The operation shape, steps and result are shared with `test`, so the marginal work is a URL rule, an egress mode and a setting. The phase can be cut without touching earlier tasks. For the owner to confirm.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":939},"end":{"line":942},"content_hash":"d881a43ce2d3a7bb2bd7190592a416aba4859345ddf5246a4a3b3a0c44577d03"},"summary":"Decision: `clax.browser.browse` (public URLs) ships in v1 behind `browser.browse.enabled`, off by default, in the plan's last phase","supersedes":"e1455c5f3807e932d4e5c31154430ab414d9e0d3d9efc3bacf25139edd1a5f78","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:02.117687Z","id":"073d973efb1244fc2362209bee06e7474a654f691ef5d6cb90762736ec7a1d45","body":{"detail":"`sender` admits a start or goto URL only when it equals a URL in a from_sender comment or the brief, by the browser's own scan of RequestContext; web::access::sources is not used, so loosening the web tools does not change browsing. PublicUrl and OwnHosts (host safety) apply under every rule.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":292},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"e1783a850b4809acdb5bdac35902c22bb1d6a6f081533ae8af0931800b6edf65"},"summary":"Decision: browse has its own URL rule (`sender` by default, `allowlist`, `any_public`), independent of web.fetch's","supersedes":"2d74a7508cb87f4a38651548c7383c7afb3224b6a36366b29c16ec1c030f93aa","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:02.310860Z","id":"42776f3c4e220f0d46e3917c8679c3d1f12e0de53e7da22948007e448126d9c1","body":{"detail":"See the records on crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs:32:38 (the narrowing and why), browse.rs:39:44 (the resolver waiver) and crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:235 (sockets). Under any_public the section holds as written, plus the name check.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":799},"end":{"line":808},"content_hash":"47f0b711a0887cb1a12d03c850510aa510c0759a06c04c681e298ba8fdf46667"},"summary":"The code departs from §9.3: under sender and allowlist a browsed page's requests are held to the rule's hosts, names are checked by the daemon's resolver, and WebSocket and WebTransport are removed","supersedes":"c08401b2cd6fe0abac69cae38bcf253c80ce8448a87b47aa7b7f915a654522f7","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:02.504596Z","id":"352c6a1954d1783ab2270bae2bf612b520155ce03229166c75e1b9be7cb17f40","body":{"detail":"Inherent to computer use: `type`, `eval` and `goto` are model-written. Defences: the admin switch (off by default), both person switches (browser and web), the `sender` rule by default, the per-run browse cap, the prompt rule that page text is data. The admin page states the risk beside the switch.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":799},"end":{"line":808},"content_hash":"47f0b711a0887cb1a12d03c850510aa510c0759a06c04c681e298ba8fdf46667"},"summary":"Browsing lets a steered model type data into third-party forms, and under any_public put it in URLs","supersedes":"49a8c59e478278828f795b04cb46a56566ff9f4a578865a747ef5d7fc0933336","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:02.697560Z","id":"9c42b7e00f31fbd9c47f7143d546ba027b643b928df1c3ec1cbd02298dad94a3","body":{"detail":"Testing one's own page reaches no third party and has its own price; the web switch's scope is expected to change. One switch for both was considered; browse reaches the web, so it needs both.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":961},"end":{"line":993},"content_hash":"9a8c05331115898c7cfefea00b04c6d0a7377d83249826b530995c123590f91f"},"summary":"Decision: a separate person switch for the browser (`bot_person_prefs.browser`), with browse needing the web switch too","supersedes":"074cebbd41025c508c586c16787257e620516c8dc14c28fcf460fdd1bfc3ff9d","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:02.891597Z","id":"a61983e51366a29a8d3d0382dc20964dfe16437d0a87bc356e3440eebb12fe04","body":{"detail":"Deferred: the Worker's content stores keep no blobs (open concern on crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs), so screenshots could not be kept, and its CDP transport is a change of its own. The Worker answers NotConfigured.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1008},"end":{"line":1010},"content_hash":"0cc49be708c732bb1c6e9972450b2ba1cece2214308f9564a813f9132ce9dd57"},"summary":"Browser use on the Worker in v1 (outbound WebSocket via fetch Upgrade, or the BROWSER binding)","supersedes":"76e72a0674629848f64b327d0a9bb391174721a4ff98e08f82ef2f80b87c1953","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the Worker's content store keeps blobs","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:03.084267Z","id":"ed068675ddbe12c47dce16c45f29432955e6ac13a9d299d8c82fbd7498d86a59","body":{"detail":"No route today lets the shell read a run's content (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot_content.rs serves hosts with the daemon token). The plan adds GET /api/bot/runs/<run>/content/<id> for whoever may view the run, images only, under a sandbox CSP. A 'Tested' list in finish, like web's Sources, is a follow-up.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1022},"end":{"line":1026},"content_hash":"ad77ff1bfdf76f0132967f3f410748bbaeb45f179a4824bec45e24e61317beb5"},"summary":"Run-panel thumbnails need a new person-facing content route","supersedes":"eff3f0952838348ef08e555829e720c3d044cbf1332945fe7df1bd3e76e10e55","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:03.276898Z","id":"dc6d983ce44db77bb601649d88c48ea299f7d2eeaa1eb311dc4fc6e0d3d4220b","body":{"detail":"Would let an admin price testing its own claxen below browsing the web. Not taken: the owner named two price lines, and the instance's cost per browser second does not depend on the source.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1096},"end":{"line":1097},"content_hash":"8a634466987457dc6bde1df80f387a1e31f31112b9791cd78f389617c320da4d"},"summary":"A price line per browser.open kind (browser.time.url, .artifact, .content)","supersedes":"1343b77cfdeabd9fa313588a0739cfad48545057e359d81d20ae1aac0909a125","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:an admin asks to price browser kinds apart","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:03.473497Z","id":"c5e8bb3fe2d807d899f45c977e51a9d97ba56dd606b33093636e64f00fee3003","body":{"detail":"capability::Capabilities::now(store, person, configured) replaces WebAccess::now and BrowserAccess::now. It answers per capability its terms or why it is off. The union of grants has one path today (admin to person to run); the zero-capability store, when it lands, adds grants to the union without changing callers.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":271},"content_hash":"44258f8fe3b962d9d5db7031985a2d7df5880d099c0567a965e79362dd0736e2"},"summary":"Decision: one function computes a run's capabilities from the admin's grant, the person's grant and the source, per capability","supersedes":"d163aa8237a73d237fb1cefe3e30f757454689de157ab143ca987b291e63f541","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:03.667232Z","id":"3840b3970781af39c7f66e6a58c7d94039e38674602dc04414fbf5abccf09219","body":{"detail":"bot_runs.caps keeps the capabilities live when the run was made, so the prompt and its declaration stay fixed (the prompt cache). Each call re-evaluates. A grant change on the daemon (admin or Me PUT) calls BrowserSessions::reevaluate, which closes and charges every session whose run lost its capability, so a session is treated as state held under a capability. A config file change takes effect at the daemon's next start.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":273},"end":{"line":290},"content_hash":"879c2ada7d194b41dc050e851dbf8d008311906d1a6ecc24edf17170a9c11ea2"},"summary":"Decision: declared when the run is made, re-evaluated at each call, and a revoke closes open sessions before it answers","supersedes":"df067c3ca60396ba237d183b0ae612cbd03f319c80a35da94b6d550bb0de82b2","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:03.860836Z","id":"4c82e5cfaf1ebd2c2c1d8ba28d6fbd3c3e419cc12751e5ea9bdc17360b051a07","body":{"detail":"Main's three values keep their meaning so existing web.fetch settings migrate untouched. The browser's default is the stricter sender because a browser session types, clicks and runs the page's scripts. The first version's browse allowlist (hosts alone, no source needed) is dropped so that allowlist means one thing for both capabilities.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"a44f7a1e98ffb1188ba5092eb30f28d94c8d8120ed10cc3c9de95e2551b5e94b"},"summary":"Decision: UrlRule gains sender for every URL-taking capability; browser.open.url defaults to sender, web.fetch keeps sourced","supersedes":"e601beb497b58b6966fdca4907a2c1e97e409bf3afd2b6773617cdc9b0d31df4","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:04.060389Z","id":"c7223231be8b316f1be5159735507886115ea68fade5efaa2d143550b93536d1","body":{"detail":"Would let a computer-use loop goto a link it read in a page. Not taken: clicking already follows a page's own links within the session's egress rule, and recording a session's links would need a page store of its own.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1106},"end":{"line":1107},"content_hash":"58f2c0c061025c4821224b24e91772e0603e94a14d401b687a4c412cad5d511c"},"summary":"Links in pages a browser session showed count as URL sources for sourced and allowlist","supersedes":"327dcb389ff388cbdabf435800d538202db4fcaf32fa80a4408a7b00fcd04b0c","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a computer-use flow needs to goto a link it saw rather than click it","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:04.254741Z","id":"dbe1ffe0ea8422ae7d285fa38d329dd8f0ddff032d4a38190311c4c012622363","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":322},"end":{"line":355},"content_hash":"22d0cef6c7904f361cf333fc9a2759e3fa98df6799b87aef871feadd72277542"},"summary":"Decision: one Spend sequence in clax/spend.rs with a Performer per operation, replacing the two copies in clax/web.rs and clax/browser.rs","supersedes":"a95888d5c5803abd90e52226e30029c4060e4a20ecdc4416686defc2841ccae6","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:04.447460Z","id":"212946cbc33da3ad745bb693f1c714f92af452be6dc018dbe81f3215ce5e44d5","body":{"detail":"An action that fails on the page is an answer (ok: false), not an error, so a computer-use loop can look and retry. browser_session_lost (the browser is gone: restart, dropped socket, crash) and browser_session_closed (an end of section 6.3, reason in the message) are neither retryable nor counted; the script opens a new session.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":357},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"f9d6140b94185db60f3b33898fcd538067d0105d1ff531a6e6880de272c17be8"},"summary":"Decision: codes are <family>_<condition>, shared where the condition is one; errors carry retryable and the capability; a session adds browser_session_lost and browser_session_closed","supersedes":"b4b539ce56d8f4d4b43be7a9d96a1229a6b2faad752f27a78fea5649f19a9c1f","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:04.647937Z","id":"c12bde96f7e365ef37fb854b81264d5d34978a9944441dec3686f3f352ce4715","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":386},"end":{"line":398},"content_hash":"0ce469165ea7f79763cec56fa60790582c77cc15a0bf43ad3fb5ab4e8625437b"},"summary":"Decision: one audit kind, bot.spend, for every capability call; bot.web rows stay and are read as bot.spend","supersedes":"bc335300ca9792f71348fd9c22832bcaabec37553e3543e64f620c8df9befcb6","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:04.842572Z","id":"093999417ec67bc8872074787ed4ba298b849bbe92f07158b39c8db34c621df3","body":{"detail":"Would leave main's audit rows and any reader of the kind untouched. Not taken: the kind would misname every browser record. bot.spend with a capability field names all of them, and the audit page's filter reads old bot.web rows with it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":386},"end":{"line":398},"content_hash":"0ce469165ea7f79763cec56fa60790582c77cc15a0bf43ad3fb5ab4e8625437b"},"summary":"Keep bot.web as the one audit kind and have browser calls write it too","supersedes":"bdeaba36c140d7d13447dff1588504cd1a82287efc3a49a5319e4b9b4463c7a5","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:an outside reader of the audit trail depends on the kind bot.web","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:05.036673Z","id":"c05a1419f98296675bfe8533cfe85cd2743b125fa841e349235cb84ef5f429e8","body":{"detail":"html is the markup decoded to UTF-8 with script, style, noscript, template, comments and event-handler attributes removed and links absolute: the page's structure without code a model would never run. raw stays main's body as it came. auto stays accepted as markdown so main's scripts and journals answer the same. A page store keyed by URL alone could not answer two formats of one page, so migration 67 rebuilds bot_web_pages with the format in its key.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":415},"end":{"line":436},"content_hash":"2f3e7c31858fb869efc3cd8d959b1d01857048f0857253ab1655479892d42bb8"},"summary":"Decision: fetch answers markdown (the default, main's auto), html (cleaned markup, no scripts or styles) or raw; the page store keeps a page per URL and format","supersedes":"c5971758f97dc3534059da7dcdc93f2ca0f14808b305e639d386f926d2e5ca41","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:05.233502Z","id":"016bba139ae573ea40c6872ab30d2e2672d269880e53445e313e230b0a1b3f34","body":{"detail":"The surface format declares functions of namespaces and the sandboxes pass JSON values (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js), so a value cannot carry methods without a prelude change in every sandbox (clax-bot-js and the Worker's driver).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":442},"end":{"line":444},"content_hash":"b96a22115be87a3a94de1e097812b6c29bf241235c0fd3a7927929f826fef983"},"summary":"Decision: a session is a string handle taken by operations of the browser namespace, not an object with methods","supersedes":"633b7b5e16a4591f3a6c383632a6a9666524faba0e883eacb615b1cf8d690141","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:05.430264Z","id":"b87421cf4c43f2dd3502ee938da51d4b898730dad11ee1e53db2010cb9252ebc","body":{"detail":"Reads as the owner wrote it. Not taken: every sandbox's prelude would have to wrap handles in objects whose methods call the namespace's operations, a change to the surface format's contract for one namespace.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1093},"end":{"line":1095},"content_hash":"863ea37e2300ed6d8790e6691474d16845805137086077271943f60ec82d9790"},"summary":"Session methods on the value open answers (s.click(...)), made by the prelude","supersedes":"1c6d544d542cc4e97aafe71a21006832c5fd3628a370cb4e4fc55d8d8a14eb40","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the surface format gains values with methods","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:05.634262Z","id":"0ea3431f7e6e88a0c416d0565f4ed0895457a30ddf1f0efb971e02b28dc9c4ee","body":{"detail":"The journal keeps an argument hash (CallEntry::args_hash), so content is never written to the store; a replayed open answers from the journal and a later call on a lost session fails rather than reloading content Clax no longer has. Image handles let a script show run content without copying bytes.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":526},"end":{"line":533},"content_hash":"7295515450ec0c526bb369e38fbc85142504daed6dd8ac88f2966ed0eaad756a"},"summary":"Decision: supplied content is held only in the session, has no bridge and no page runtime API, and is capped at 2 MiB of HTML and 16 MiB of files","supersedes":"b2f849b966321abd308838c1afef4de55af15fa9d14daf19830492bbd11e3a35","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:05.828427Z","id":"fabce9cafb3c8d59814222f4e85ef9fe166f5cff742748ffc0f6b208c82779ca","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":535},"end":{"line":553},"content_hash":"7bf935cadae72e2168cc2d583e108aa42eba77eb5ec7b5e6cc76aa542a27a10f"},"summary":"Decision: a session ends on close, 300 s idle, 1,800 s open, a revoke, a credits refusal or the run's end","supersedes":"87804b1affdf53cd6b799f5593f9f6ccf93768fd74bcc3c2e84f08a40bc03864","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:06.029784Z","id":"7857a3afa48fc1350b56feccd7f593bc352805e43a32eae1c04a2fefac3087bf","body":{"detail":"A click or type is not idempotent: when a step's attempt performed a call and failed before the Spend transaction wrote it (a store error), the retried attempt performs it again on the live session. Web fetches have the same window (web section 4.2). Closing it would need a per-call idempotency key the browser cannot honour.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":571},"end":{"line":573},"content_hash":"95e855cb6fd9f8c342002a454f116f30d88a36cdb4f42a1d9fc9203c103343f5"},"summary":"A step retried by the same process performs again a session call whose first attempt was performed but not journaled","supersedes":"26eff3494dcc4bd159785a97f0295762aee8cc656d7e8921adec1317eadb58cd","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:06.245935Z","id":"9c49faf05cb460df3ad682925e94e12b261a78b51e585eda9aed702629ff222e","body":{"detail":"Needs no decoder or encoder in Clax, no new crate, and builds for the Worker unchanged. The model sees at most four frames as images.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":615},"end":{"line":624},"content_hash":"7624638c8e4e3e4c0328f2a9eb880afdf80db8a9d97ec2267075015a1963a377"},"summary":"Decision: a recording is a sequence of the JPEG frames Chrome's screencast sends, with a JSON manifest, played by the run panel as a flipbook","supersedes":"c448d9567426ee66444bc5481ceee33f9745a98445a2258691e519b93e0606b5","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:06.441737Z","id":"904a3a8a17e9d285990c2c9f4ccb60e5a628770f9099785ee4ac7b2e9356fd0d","body":{"detail":"One file people can download or attach. Not taken now: GIF needs two new crates and daemon CPU and has 256 colours; MediaRecorder needs a second page in the session driven by a canvas, adding a moving part to every recording.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1104},"end":{"line":1105},"content_hash":"ae3deb231bdcb9b838170ff9c7d46781697456031481c4c5527ccf8dd1d92c5b"},"summary":"Encode a recording as an animated GIF (gif and a JPEG decoder, pure Rust) or as WebM made by the browser's MediaRecorder","supersedes":"accfbb57e530eddaf2f9ad53bd558718fb7f82f2806df5921e3bf64bd0e5256e","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a clip must leave Clax as one file, attached to a reply or downloaded","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:06.636322Z","id":"c9ed67c39677d68c5a37e7f74f7ff1c22153403af289802cb4a66c4c3fca9f47","body":{"detail":"A thinking model keeps its browser slot for up to the idle time (300 s), so with browser.max_concurrent at 2 two runs with open sessions refuse every other open (browser_busy, retryable). The admin raises max_concurrent or lowers the idle time.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":626},"end":{"line":636},"content_hash":"827cb1fc06a9d4c608b54e893515eab23c0061427b408df7786580bd13d71498"},"summary":"Decision: one open session per run by default (up to 4), and the instance's two browsers are held until a session ends","supersedes":"0a6381ce383a31856ca2762c54b5ba48e06713a6696ff0bbf62fe6e0bff824b3","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:06.833755Z","id":"aff98448613372321c7cbc78064bf84b71407376c0335d7fe24a2e5634707c97","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":691},"end":{"line":707},"content_hash":"e17c489c805eb26923a8388d7d61b585ed2321f63480f5ac55af574e3377f45a"},"summary":"Decision: keep_alive 60 s and a heartbeat after 20 s without a command, rather than a keep_alive as long as a model turn","supersedes":"95e6aeb25180b381d7683936b7c42f97706e0f4b51791f984fe632f2b03a9e2b","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:07.030512Z","id":"43c68e4ed308d05a1f47ed74d6cb606d4ce7677e6f9ec7223fc905dd5c194613","body":{"detail":"Section 7.2 assumes keep_alive bounds the time without DevTools commands, so a heartbeat keeps a session alive and an orphan lives at most keep_alive. If keep_alive instead runs only after the socket drops, the heartbeat is harmless and the orphan bound still holds; if Browser Run also ends a browser after a fixed lifetime shorter than browser.session.max_seconds, sessions end early and answer browser_session_lost. Only the opt-in live test (just browser-live) can check; it has not been run against Cloudflare.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":693},"end":{"line":697},"content_hash":"a0a715c6352748687ec7c5a172a788480f34050154ae19caea37ac3e7683ee7f"},"summary":"Browser Run's keep_alive semantics and maximum are unchecked: whether it counts inactivity of commands or time after the socket drops, and whether its maximum is 20 minutes","supersedes":"d48cf9c081dca001c78a937f6fcacf86d1795206f05d601778ecca11e6c69a29","tags":["claxbot-browser","risk","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:07.223260Z","id":"817732f2c6e088c92f5885046101cb15c526940e85b3a62a6d54f98cd41203ff","body":{"detail":"Simpler: no timer in the host. Not taken: a browser orphaned by a daemon crash would bill up to the idle time (300 s, up to 20 minutes), and a model turn longer than Browser Run's maximum would lose the session.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1101},"end":{"line":1103},"content_hash":"45853c944a7add77a77d21c5f607b16a4c6c271b4be24e7b4bc9eda1addd12fb"},"summary":"Set keep_alive to the session's idle time (at most Browser Run's maximum) and send no heartbeat","supersedes":"e3f5545029b0e541880dacc2bcfdaafbe8a2246706ea47bd038f6deb298b6c34","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:Browser Run bills or limits heartbeat commands","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:07.422330Z","id":"960b9cd6a18283aa603287482442bd377a181f7163dd38f2f4f65acaa0d6622f","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":723},"end":{"line":744},"content_hash":"c3d3ee0d211a03140b3e41e0c4ab7cc81c109864c29ccdd7d57c7804913e7e8a"},"summary":"Decision: open sessions live in a host-owned registry of tasks that own their sockets, serve requests between calls, heartbeat and end themselves","supersedes":"b7c5fd90542c5e146733cbab9887d1c7c592c476309f64d0b3801ff77128e6fe","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:07.616318Z","id":"b304d23bf5630c1bd951461d27ffa4b69d70be5af1ee16e9ee80d85f329085dc","body":{"detail":"So the artifact's read-only API and supplied content are never reachable from a page that can reach the web, and the conversion counts against the URL cap. A goto within the origin needs nothing more.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":820},"end":{"line":831},"content_hash":"b437efa7c240a233221a27dffe98c427f4b5ceb460635f4a00ca2a6eb3c7439a"},"summary":"Decision: a goto out of an artifact or content session needs browser.open.url, converts the session once, and stops serving its synthetic origin","supersedes":"ef116de509ce3dbb73d201e6c2d0cd4eeb8743a0e860d0a05d4b603930599d41","tags":["claxbot-browser","security","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:07.812216Z","id":"8a6afec97332d80e3efd3036fae78183dbcbf0e04f70ce42aa2c17a9ee304a96","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":890},"end":{"line":923},"content_hash":"70c28cedb2d33bde748043264f70bc223852edb35b592492e9f1fbbaa7b215c8"},"summary":"Decision: browser time is charged in contiguous millisecond segments, each session call charging up to its end and a host's end charging the rest once","supersedes":"83274b4332fece9ba1e12eb83293c10b43c94470ac5dd6618d3d4c1039b35e53","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:08.008210Z","id":"64ef833373b7c370171532ebc39e7c186443253000c8ec4498072534af863c48","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":927},"end":{"line":959},"content_hash":"183bee25f6c6f4bf6dea81fc1e039ce8e11472a804574476398508bb3669b833"},"summary":"Decision: main's web.* settings stay as they are; the first version's browser.* settings are renamed per capability","supersedes":"63bbbbabc812c2686c61dc78a7cf634927b3c33a166e452dee5a1299d93e2c77","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:08.206139Z","id":"c8a7f9b5461c61603ff3421783744a6287599984e4b54e4ef8d6e8c2dad970f6","body":{"detail":"The owner's standing rule: sessions start at zero; capabilities are the union of live grants; revoke re-evaluates transitively. So no person holds a capability by default. Section 4.3 (lines 214-271) computes caps(run) from the admin's switch (the instance offers the capability, with its terms), the admin's grants (to everyone on the instance, or to one person), the person's grant to their runs (an instance-wide grant issues it to each person as a recorded child; the person's switch revokes or re-issues it) and the source. Migration 67 writes main's behaviour as explicit rows: an instance-wide grant of web.search and of web.fetch where that switch was on, and its child for every person except those whose bot_person_prefs.web was off (section 11.2, lines 961-993). The three browser.open kinds get no instance-wide grant; the admin grants each explicitly. Revoking an admin grant ends its children and re-evaluates every run and session under them (section 4.4). This replaces the waiver that read a missing row as a live grant.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":271},"content_hash":"44258f8fe3b962d9d5db7031985a2d7df5880d099c0567a965e79362dd0736e2"},"summary":"Decision: grants are explicit, none implied; main's web default becomes an instance-wide grant the admin holds and can revoke","supersedes":"cc4ff90eff18ce3a263b4a09e24ea8b0a56e02d141bb6011b99e2f60e9f7beeb","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:08.398212Z","id":"a4d4b502e3bb58e0bcb3d74d12d27f0cf12c277a9bf274e25bb8531f57c99b57","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":961},"end":{"line":993},"content_hash":"9a8c05331115898c7cfefea00b04c6d0a7377d83249826b530995c123590f91f"},"summary":"Decision: grants are rows of bot_cap_grants (granter, grantee everyone, a person or a person's runs, parent, status), recorded as bot.grant; main's web switches and choices become explicit rows","supersedes":"dbf6a832f7f422765f298354d15331f71e65509da337a235056645acdd083337","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:08.820865Z","id":"d4b5e606aedd7f5eb2a820ad9bc11eee73580d5c7b2e4c7d593232a164938d08","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ed068675ddbe12c47dce16c45f29432955e6ac13a9d299d8c82fbd7498d86a59","span":{"start":{"line":1022},"end":{"line":1026},"content_hash":"ad77ff1bfdf76f0132967f3f410748bbaeb45f179a4824bec45e24e61317beb5"},"summary":"Built: GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/content/<item> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs run_content), image items of that run of the four raster types only, under Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src 'none' and nosniff, 404 otherwise. Tests: api_claxbot::run_content_is_served_to_the_runs_viewers_only, api_claxbot::a_non_image_item_is_not_served. It admits the person the run acts for and admins who read its artifact, not readers (see the alternative on run_content).","supersedes":"524d8b6bef0cc3bee7d559e8299aab71c734e31d28a733aaffb7488e3a46839a","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:29.545394Z","id":"173536d846d1b1d3934b2a9597726036144af302097f9ac03554e88a4081b980","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e99783dff572741676bc4aca17b5fd95d10be981119bcd66388b944ad9fc36cd","summary":"Still decided by the owner, as the reply b42ca323 says; this record was re-anchored after that reply","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:48:29.545957Z","id":"67746f7b63a388430fa71794f9fbcd305d2ed3f14f4d0fd0ac990be06dc9a465","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2a97d6203b3b135dfbe6d127beaae4bd43a3edb6b801ad57d3945935bbd9862e","summary":"Still decided by the owner, as the reply 93ed4cd2 says; this record was re-anchored after that reply","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:18.443299Z","id":"52de5c49f2edb65bc19a9fbb2d8aff866120d63e4d2558e2918f1724b2168cb8","body":{"detail":"The owner named two price lines, per request and per browser second. Web keeps main's lines (one per search provider, and web.fetch); every browser.open kind is charged on browser.time, since a second of browser costs the instance the same whatever the page. Each capability still has its own grant, cap and switch.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":233},"end":{"line":234},"content_hash":"4874123bbf61e4bfe5f8c112580662b09046cd0e817ddc883d700450a3543efa"},"summary":"Decision: the three browser.open kinds share one price line, browser.time, per browser second","supersedes":"d848c013399becb3a95af01330cd07b02f4873096605f66936a905f3f476f316","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:18.640196Z","id":"c9eea0a852a186ab95795e99c5f217aa20471530ee4be2fd23f8d2bf98f26965","body":{"detail":"web.fetch's URL-source rule (crates/clax-bot/src/web/access.rs `sources`), Markdown conversion, page store and `WebSource` are not used, because the web tools' scope is expected to be loosened (raw HTML, not only Markdown). Only generic machinery is reused: `Access::Spend` and `Store::spend_journaled` (crates/clax-store/src/bot_web.rs), credits, settings, the sealed Cloudflare credentials, run content. The web-named pieces it needs are generalised in place (§4.6). Design decision for the owner to confirm or overturn.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1509},"end":{"line":1510},"content_hash":"d834d6317c0b68bf4d7501bc9808c4610d82db56dfea4a3cf5a86ef8ee16ad88"},"summary":"Decision: the browser is its own `clax.browser` namespace with its own grant, settings, codes, cost line and audit kind, built on none of web.fetch's internals","supersedes":"2a97d6203b3b135dfbe6d127beaae4bd43a3edb6b801ad57d3945935bbd9862e","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:18.836211Z","id":"805e67e34e84a2fe1a31ddcc9aff1651b200aea4f2c9a5ec8e7d90615f15efa7","body":{"detail":"Rejected for v1: Quick Actions return no console messages or page errors, run no actions (click, type, assertions), and make Cloudflare fetch the page itself, which cannot reach a private artifact or a daemon on localhost. CDP with Fetch-domain interception (§4.3, §6) serves the page from the host instead.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1062},"end":{"line":1066},"content_hash":"807ae5b3522eaac112f1473fc9d75f9d06e9c523a221cc95d6ec2115ccf41b26"},"summary":"Quick Actions REST (/screenshot, /content, /scrape) instead of CDP over a WebSocket","supersedes":"3dcfa2c1229fcf51535857b0ea386d9fd50c2e5872756e9177b4cfd123a2dbad","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:Browser Run's REST API gains console, errors and request interception","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:19.033345Z","id":"0c7660f02c02047b742f9a8f66a266c17e723c876ed4125fe650faaa88738964","body":{"detail":"The endpoint is wss://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/{id}/browser-run/devtools/browser per the 2026-11 docs, but other pages of the same docs use `browser-rendering`. The design makes it one constant (`BROWSER_RUN_PATH`) pinned by the daemon test against a fake server, which cannot tell which spelling Cloudflare accepts: only the opt-in live test (`just browser-live`) can. If Cloudflare answers 404 on the upgrade, switch the constant.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1062},"end":{"line":1064},"content_hash":"6a2e226dedb88600452b1c9947f520f60123ebce3e1d14f24032899c5880990b"},"summary":"Browser Run's docs spell the CDP path segment both `browser-run` and `browser-rendering`","supersedes":"9497ae5b7e443b3801fcae9886aa46ba3cefedef25e45edc18acf59dd2553732","tags":["claxbot-browser","risk","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:19.249544Z","id":"43cf96aa41d83ade32b6045357b7ac62a7fa328abddaa55d264fe5102023d7f4","body":{"detail":"The session ends the browser itself (`Browser.close`) on every path out of the driver; a process that dies cannot. keep_alive is set to its minimum (10 s) and Browser Run's idle timeout is 60 s, so an orphan costs at most about a browser-minute ($0.0015 at list price), absorbed by the instance and not charged to the person (the Spend transaction never ran).\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1310},"end":{"line":1313},"content_hash":"4bd18242a8b6a06aae591c550c865171dae22e229799396965aebe64f4684abe"},"summary":"A browser orphaned by a daemon crash mid-test stays on Browser Run until keep_alive or the idle timeout, billed to the instance","supersedes":"10110aad8758e535ea07e20c7a67e894acba94e2398bf5471a23c6b6d93f7db6","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:19.457604Z","id":"0477a64ba6aee471076c59ec58db5f8916fcb363e44448f30e7cf4c260d70a30","body":{"detail":"Keeps the policy host-independent and testable against an in-memory fake Chrome, as `WebSource` did for web (spec 2026-11-02-claxbot-web-tools §4.3). `clax_core::wrap` and the store are reachable from clax-bot, so the page set is built there; the bridge's hashed part files, the site CSP (clax-http) and `/_clax/api/` are the server's, so they are trait methods. Check against scripts/check-crate-layers.py: no new crate edge.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1105},"end":{"line":1119},"content_hash":"8fa59756bb4220c8cae2faefc97254391270bce77b43825d9c3b3bc0f1da8af7"},"summary":"Decision: the CDP driver, request policy, steps and result shaping live in clax-bot `browser/`; a host provides only a `CdpTransport`, Clax's UI files, the site's headers and its read-only API","supersedes":"12c2abdf4989fa28c2649a033fbc2ad671c5323eebf9da4bd23c6b7d841ee1ac","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:19.655244Z","id":"993286c1ff4aaed21ec0afc1109fbb203efee82a32567b86e2ae4bb8abd37061","body":{"detail":"One Cloudflare account per instance; the token gains the Browser Rendering - Edit permission. The setting's key stays web-named; the admin pages label it \"Cloudflare account\".\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":424},"end":{"line":431},"content_hash":"8fd63349173de04dd6c72509ad7923474ee83f9c2eff529cb01f6879b91622e5"},"summary":"Decision: reuse `web.cloudflare.account_id` and `SecretSlot::Cloudflare` for Browser Run rather than adding browser credentials","supersedes":"01d8b9d8ebd4f20a4c018bbd89ae353952d491977544b89f22687352973ab8d0","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:19.851478Z","id":"3106e48857cea30c2e0cacd728945f784e4cfd796f3ff678a398d649b19fb650","body":{"detail":"Not now: a key rename needs a migration of stored settings and of `[bot.web]` config overrides, unrelated to the browser. The browser reads the existing key.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":431},"end":{"line":431},"content_hash":"454c17a4c3102d022cf09d105884a29f31c51fad288774fbc535910eb7ac893a"},"summary":"Rename the setting `web.cloudflare.account_id` to `cloudflare.account_id`, shared by web and browser","supersedes":"b6f592e4f1ca006c63a6f7ffdac3de10b4fc212b95e4bac8cefeb06605d5901e","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a third Cloudflare-backed feature reads the account ID","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:20.047012Z","id":"c93a2c1e67b112a0b73fd97774a23794929804e363f493be518c17dcc95d2378","body":{"detail":"`.invalid` never resolves (RFC 6761), so a request that escapes interception fails closed; https makes it a secure context like the real site. Fulfilling https requests from Fetch.requestPaused is standard CDP practice but untested against Browser Run until the live test runs.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1146},"end":{"line":1155},"content_hash":"9a77ec62bb7868200ed0a55446654500bd368413d4c2fadf8c6c133b3f91813e"},"summary":"Decision: claxen load at https://<artifact ID>.clax-test.invalid/, every request answered by the host through the CDP Fetch domain","supersedes":"0d42ab4c283b6adad244f845cb30c2f44e006c116dfb36cf006ba80089fe616a","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:20.245402Z","id":"c25a86ba1c7276448677ad396cb291576908ff556153de5a171c0b50d6f7aa1a","body":{"detail":"v1 answers GETs as the run's person and refuses writes (403 read_only_test), so a test never changes people's documents; a page whose first render writes shows that failure. The scratch copy needs a hidden draft artifact per test and its cleanup.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1179},"end":{"line":1184},"content_hash":"254873fb34a94bb19ca34727f047f95b0bd8cea8a052ea5a54bb452051f6c80d"},"summary":"A writable scratch copy of the artifact's documents during a test, as the Clax app's drafts make (POST /api/drafts), instead of a read-only /_clax/api/","supersedes":"d67a96b9f3265a2eaa85fbc17138a35578670d963e7f20ad8c4b9fb40dbb3ce4","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:ClaxBot tests a db-writing page and the read-only refusals hide real failures","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:20.447911Z","id":"6d121479b90526a0000d4712d80b8690a750465dbb9ef2dab2c5b94951bcd12f","body":{"detail":"Clax's page contract serves every page under `default-src 'self' data: blob:` (docs/contract.md, \"Sites\"), so no CDN host can load on the real site; an allowlist would let a test pass where the page fails for its viewers. Navigations, which CSP does not govern, are failed at the Fetch domain; CSP refusals are reported through a securitypolicyviolation listener. Departs from the earlier idea of a page-contract CDN allowlist: there is no such list in Clax.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1188},"end":{"line":1196},"content_hash":"c9668f84333a38be10644f1b0b9a307b3c9532870903b2cb1d7164a5935c8c04"},"summary":"Decision: no CDN allowlist; a page under test reaches its synthetic origin alone, every other request (navigations included) is failed and reported","supersedes":"715c679819b2a6cb9d1a3a2eb42ddb196ed8a921c7ec2125cf8fada07d1002f1","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:20.670128Z","id":"9df39506ec82bba9ac78b6305258963aa56fa7035128293e957f623e6cb6fbce","body":{"detail":"Chrome's DNS prefetch and preconnect happen outside the CDP Fetch domain and outside CSP, so a page under test can make Browser Run's resolver look up <data>.evil.example. WebRTC is closed by the preamble removing RTCPeerConnection; DNS is not closable from CDP. The artifact's content, documents read through /_clax/api/, and screenshots are processed by Cloudflare as a sub-processor, as search queries already are. Accepted: a person viewing the page in their own browser has the same DNS channel.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1212},"end":{"line":1216},"content_hash":"22050267ef151e4e86d03973c03db3e6ed480c547415a803e74ea3653b51d542"},"summary":"DNS prefetch, speculative connections and Cloudflare's processing of the page stay open as channels","supersedes":"a7102a1274dcca562caf215b9fe5a4bf123fdaa8583028e56059e19b8a45fc72","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:20.867165Z","id":"a03cadf60fbcbc5d28aa3be86a4529b3cec14cf5951b49db8310910c20033f64","body":{"detail":"Rejected: the Clax app's inspect view already runs `tests/<name>.test.js` with the bridge harness (docs/contract.md \"The inspect view\", web/bridge/src/harness.ts). A second format would be less expressive and not run by the app. `steps` remain for one-call checks.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1235},"end":{"line":1240},"content_hash":"c149b0bcda665c0facd51069cc716bce47b468a603bf32e400306ef9a84777ba"},"summary":"A declarative JSON test file in the `steps` format for durable tests","supersedes":"e2781516bd65e394063ef0e2d380b55fa7c4922c0ae502112e2cd13ed0fcaa49","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the harness's JS tests prove hard for ClaxBot to write correctly","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:21.063629Z","id":"8329a3ef08f14e4c93833edac738e8f4e96dfda223280ec6da434ab4c24a5e94","body":{"detail":"The driver evaluates a fixed expression against a hook defined only when window.name is `clax-test`. A bridge change that renames or reshapes it breaks browser tests silently unless the fake-Chrome test of the expression and the bridge unit test of the hook agree. The hook adds bytes to the eager bridge, which is already over its gzip budget (thread 1014d9d7 on web/bridge/src/bridge.ts): keep it a few lines that delegate to the test part.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1250},"end":{"line":1257},"content_hash":"106abefc8c1e97e1be133761228e4c6bae1251f5423f8a6822454cb970470cfb"},"summary":"The bridge hook `window.claxTest.run` couples ClaxBot's driver to the bridge's lazy test part and to an eager-bridge byte budget","supersedes":"12891c7e20d7dc7081902e3065d6e24db9dd8d14d8a5b406c3666a7b21994bfa","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:21.266124Z","id":"c83c919d268339ff814594ea9f4a8730acfa9454558fbf0865e2d2f43b5f2fa1","body":{"detail":"The run panel shows ClaxBot's test results; the Clax app's inspect view runs the same files on its drafts; nothing in the web shell lets an artifact's owner run `tests/*.test.js`. Follow-up: a Run tests button on the artifact page (needs a browser-run route outside a ClaxBot run, and who pays for it).\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1259},"end":{"line":1263},"content_hash":"e5343ec1efbd1e1d93c39a987dad48bef180e7dac9a343da1b840b6bd68d6a4a"},"summary":"People cannot run an artifact's tests themselves in v1","supersedes":"23711ea8a62a1b21b3387662fcaab434a53cd220c4ed7950c168d43e10dc8378","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:deferred","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:21.473836Z","id":"372671b68cba0fbed672ad33f4992f7ece760125bece3728d4931c2d345e4d6a","body":{"detail":"Cloudflare bills $2.00 per concurrent browser beyond 10 (monthly average) on top of browser-hours. It cannot be attributed to one test, so `browser.time` charges hours only. `browser.max_concurrent` (default 2) bounds the exposure.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1274},"end":{"line":1276},"content_hash":"0273cefcc1826cc463dd8683f592fddaa23dfec27d5a4397e99ac08c270c3db9"},"summary":"Browser Run's concurrency charge is not metered per test; the instance absorbs it","supersedes":"1ff93cc8d189c2aa828bb35b1bffdb7975940d6c6ba082a9c28bb53dfb25b1cf","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:21.686922Z","id":"4767c29ffba281b4b1a76627665419f5afc94961fbd7150e4f518dcabd71fc19","body":{"detail":"The time cap bounds what one test can cost, so a person cannot run past their week mid-test; at list price a 60 s cap is 0.0015 USD. Measured from the WebSocket upgrade to its close by the provider's injected clock. A test that never opened (401, 429, socket error, browser_busy) is not charged but counts toward the cap when it reached Browser Run.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1316},"end":{"line":1320},"content_hash":"b51ee6cca45203d59ad1ba1ae79bc08ff083181629ff8f6040a909ddfb4eafb6"},"summary":"Decision: pre-check that the person can pay for the call's whole time cap, not the minimum charge; charge measured time rounded up to the second, whenever a browser opened","supersedes":"17ccb6496251b28c81eb9287de2ad400c53512a445ca19f2941e9187f1d9da6d","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:21.889039Z","id":"8ef10326e3f0791b04cd596bca07d38ae0a4e642ba53a0d7ba3603ae2c93a6a2","body":{"detail":"Not taken: little marginal code, off by default, and it exercises the computer-use path the owner wants kept open.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1337},"end":{"line":1340},"content_hash":"d881a43ce2d3a7bb2bd7190592a416aba4859345ddf5246a4a3b3a0c44577d03"},"summary":"Defer browsing public URLs to a later version","supersedes":"aa7f2a1571452f03d3288968ee7679aec2e54b65edd2d0ed36cb48a541386397","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the browse phase slips or its waiver is judged too wide before release","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:22.095885Z","id":"5b297734fcf4fa95b6dc81db1099eeb92ef2ec8568d524012442e8c1d7174094","body":{"detail":"The operation shape, steps and result are shared with `test`, so the marginal work is a URL rule, an egress mode and a setting. The phase can be cut without touching earlier tasks. For the owner to confirm.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1337},"end":{"line":1340},"content_hash":"d881a43ce2d3a7bb2bd7190592a416aba4859345ddf5246a4a3b3a0c44577d03"},"summary":"Decision: `clax.browser.browse` (public URLs) ships in v1 behind `browser.browse.enabled`, off by default, in the plan's last phase","supersedes":"e99783dff572741676bc4aca17b5fd95d10be981119bcd66388b944ad9fc36cd","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:22.302117Z","id":"2802102ae5448deca21b4a8e22ff701515386ffe16cc3ab770aea06a5195d4e6","body":{"detail":"`sender` admits a start or goto URL only when it equals a URL in a from_sender comment or the brief, by the browser's own scan of RequestContext; web::access::sources is not used, so loosening the web tools does not change browsing. PublicUrl and OwnHosts (host safety) apply under every rule.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":314},"end":{"line":341},"content_hash":"e1783a850b4809acdb5bdac35902c22bb1d6a6f081533ae8af0931800b6edf65"},"summary":"Decision: browse has its own URL rule (`sender` by default, `allowlist`, `any_public`), independent of web.fetch's","supersedes":"073d973efb1244fc2362209bee06e7474a654f691ef5d6cb90762736ec7a1d45","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:22.507059Z","id":"bd4975fb18a4dc5550737f4673300db4847c931f21e5038001e50311f410bc01","body":{"detail":"See the records on crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs:32:38 (the narrowing and why), browse.rs:39:44 (the resolver waiver) and crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:235 (sockets). Under any_public the section holds as written, plus the name check.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1197},"end":{"line":1206},"content_hash":"47f0b711a0887cb1a12d03c850510aa510c0759a06c04c681e298ba8fdf46667"},"summary":"The code departs from §9.3: under sender and allowlist a browsed page's requests are held to the rule's hosts, names are checked by the daemon's resolver, and WebSocket and WebTransport are removed","supersedes":"42776f3c4e220f0d46e3917c8679c3d1f12e0de53e7da22948007e448126d9c1","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:22.702733Z","id":"4d914569d2cccfff6ba1c1ba08449dceff5543b3ff82e979776e23a560c25bcb","body":{"detail":"Inherent to computer use: `type`, `eval` and `goto` are model-written. Defences: the admin switch (off by default), both person switches (browser and web), the `sender` rule by default, the per-run browse cap, the prompt rule that page text is data. The admin page states the risk beside the switch.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1197},"end":{"line":1206},"content_hash":"47f0b711a0887cb1a12d03c850510aa510c0759a06c04c681e298ba8fdf46667"},"summary":"Browsing lets a steered model type data into third-party forms, and under any_public put it in URLs","supersedes":"352c6a1954d1783ab2270bae2bf612b520155ce03229166c75e1b9be7cb17f40","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:22.904048Z","id":"b275660cb02db97a502b54e8110d5de0292c49398eee16e8b2fdde8360e98c0d","body":{"detail":"Testing one's own page reaches no third party and has its own price; the web switch's scope is expected to change. One switch for both was considered; browse reaches the web, so it needs both.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1359},"end":{"line":1391},"content_hash":"9a8c05331115898c7cfefea00b04c6d0a7377d83249826b530995c123590f91f"},"summary":"Decision: a separate person switch for the browser (`bot_person_prefs.browser`), with browse needing the web switch too","supersedes":"9c42b7e00f31fbd9c47f7143d546ba027b643b928df1c3ec1cbd02298dad94a3","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:23.100796Z","id":"e89fd762347dc53badb00d504491996d4e2097721eb89f68218f05f4e72e02d5","body":{"detail":"Deferred: the Worker's content stores keep no blobs (open concern on crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs), so screenshots could not be kept, and its CDP transport is a change of its own. The Worker answers NotConfigured.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1406},"end":{"line":1408},"content_hash":"0cc49be708c732bb1c6e9972450b2ba1cece2214308f9564a813f9132ce9dd57"},"summary":"Browser use on the Worker in v1 (outbound WebSocket via fetch Upgrade, or the BROWSER binding)","supersedes":"a61983e51366a29a8d3d0382dc20964dfe16437d0a87bc356e3440eebb12fe04","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the Worker's content store keeps blobs","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:23.323479Z","id":"db71c602b908f03856fa386ecd9f5d2477381ef0b5c2057c67ecb16669429e2e","body":{"detail":"No route today lets the shell read a run's content (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot_content.rs serves hosts with the daemon token). The plan adds GET /api/bot/runs/<run>/content/<id> for whoever may view the run, images only, under a sandbox CSP. A 'Tested' list in finish, like web's Sources, is a follow-up.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1423},"end":{"line":1427},"content_hash":"ad77ff1bfdf76f0132967f3f410748bbaeb45f179a4824bec45e24e61317beb5"},"summary":"Run-panel thumbnails need a new person-facing content route","supersedes":"ed068675ddbe12c47dce16c45f29432955e6ac13a9d299d8c82fbd7498d86a59","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:23.531473Z","id":"145cb5d35078ba94df7838b3cf2abee1f9e706a86fa7cad8863d87a7765908ba","body":{"detail":"Would let an admin price testing its own claxen below browsing the web. Not taken: the owner named two price lines, and the instance's cost per browser second does not depend on the source.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1538},"end":{"line":1539},"content_hash":"8a634466987457dc6bde1df80f387a1e31f31112b9791cd78f389617c320da4d"},"summary":"A price line per browser.open kind (browser.time.url, .artifact, .content)","supersedes":"dc6d983ce44db77bb601649d88c48ea299f7d2eeaa1eb311dc4fc6e0d3d4220b","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:an admin asks to price browser kinds apart","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:23.734817Z","id":"971019bddf8ff8c5972638b94accda45ab64a49eae34ae5933652bbc806ebfdb","body":{"detail":"capability::Capabilities::now(store, person, configured) replaces WebAccess::now and BrowserAccess::now. It answers per capability its terms or why it is off. The union of grants has one path today (admin to person to run); the zero-capability store, when it lands, adds grants to the union without changing callers.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":236},"end":{"line":293},"content_hash":"44258f8fe3b962d9d5db7031985a2d7df5880d099c0567a965e79362dd0736e2"},"summary":"Decision: one function computes a run's capabilities from the admin's grant, the person's grant and the source, per capability","supersedes":"c5e8bb3fe2d807d899f45c977e51a9d97ba56dd606b33093636e64f00fee3003","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:23.934617Z","id":"1ca46872041c2d6df45f7f007970508bc0e4a34d9d1aeb63624ee38415e9ab0d","body":{"detail":"bot_runs.caps keeps the capabilities live when the run was made, so the prompt and its declaration stay fixed (the prompt cache). Each call re-evaluates. A grant change on the daemon (admin or Me PUT) calls BrowserSessions::reevaluate, which closes and charges every session whose run lost its capability, so a session is treated as state held under a capability. A config file change takes effect at the daemon's next start.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":295},"end":{"line":312},"content_hash":"879c2ada7d194b41dc050e851dbf8d008311906d1a6ecc24edf17170a9c11ea2"},"summary":"Decision: declared when the run is made, re-evaluated at each call, and a revoke closes open sessions before it answers","supersedes":"3840b3970781af39c7f66e6a58c7d94039e38674602dc04414fbf5abccf09219","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:24.140673Z","id":"77024a88c1e462c66f81b50ac2425778ba0a3d9aa43726408c0481a7d526bb3d","body":{"detail":"Main's three values keep their meaning so existing web.fetch settings migrate untouched. The browser's default is the stricter sender because a browser session types, clicks and runs the page's scripts. The first version's browse allowlist (hosts alone, no source needed) is dropped so that allowlist means one thing for both capabilities.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":335},"end":{"line":341},"content_hash":"a44f7a1e98ffb1188ba5092eb30f28d94c8d8120ed10cc3c9de95e2551b5e94b"},"summary":"Decision: UrlRule gains sender for every URL-taking capability; browser.open.url defaults to sender, web.fetch keeps sourced","supersedes":"4c82e5cfaf1ebd2c2c1d8ba28d6fbd3c3e419cc12751e5ea9bdc17360b051a07","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:24.339881Z","id":"135363c973197149b54e33d4bcf784422e7a5f8e31eb176dcc899e093202a7b5","body":{"detail":"Would let a computer-use loop goto a link it read in a page. Not taken: clicking already follows a page's own links within the session's egress rule, and recording a session's links would need a page store of its own.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1548},"end":{"line":1549},"content_hash":"58f2c0c061025c4821224b24e91772e0603e94a14d401b687a4c412cad5d511c"},"summary":"Links in pages a browser session showed count as URL sources for sourced and allowlist","supersedes":"c7223231be8b316f1be5159735507886115ea68fade5efaa2d143550b93536d1","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a computer-use flow needs to goto a link it saw rather than click it","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:24.541627Z","id":"0034d00df1a7c463dca71c7fce0ca1c75d68acf7651c164fda2a723758019643","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":344},"end":{"line":377},"content_hash":"22d0cef6c7904f361cf333fc9a2759e3fa98df6799b87aef871feadd72277542"},"summary":"Decision: one Spend sequence in clax/spend.rs with a Performer per operation, replacing the two copies in clax/web.rs and clax/browser.rs","supersedes":"dbe1ffe0ea8422ae7d285fa38d329dd8f0ddff032d4a38190311c4c012622363","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:24.746167Z","id":"2820a394158fd671e0925366bfb474650ca1ef7281f881b715047aabb326fa69","body":{"detail":"An action that fails on the page is an answer (ok: false), not an error, so a computer-use loop can look and retry. browser_session_lost (the browser is gone: restart, dropped socket, crash) and browser_session_closed (an end of section 6.3, reason in the message) are neither retryable nor counted; the script opens a new session.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":378},"end":{"line":408},"content_hash":"332cf7202d6345fee04ffc5d18c6e26bf034b4ff756a8a18735ad15c60428327"},"summary":"Decision: codes are <family>_<condition>, shared where the condition is one; errors carry retryable and the capability; a session adds browser_session_lost and browser_session_closed","supersedes":"212946cbc33da3ad745bb693f1c714f92af452be6dc018dbe81f3215ce5e44d5","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:24.953457Z","id":"9d0d7d4ce60601b3ca9301c945dbc6e0d77745ef614cef2b7d6d52582e6c615c","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":410},"end":{"line":422},"content_hash":"0ce469165ea7f79763cec56fa60790582c77cc15a0bf43ad3fb5ab4e8625437b"},"summary":"Decision: one audit kind, bot.spend, for every capability call; bot.web rows stay and are read as bot.spend","supersedes":"c12bde96f7e365ef37fb854b81264d5d34978a9944441dec3686f3f352ce4715","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:25.155438Z","id":"e35f8bfcc679572e50a02b08dd4ebf90c7ead355964babcd2bec520cfb323a59","body":{"detail":"Would leave main's audit rows and any reader of the kind untouched. Not taken: the kind would misname every browser record. bot.spend with a capability field names all of them, and the audit page's filter reads old bot.web rows with it.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":410},"end":{"line":422},"content_hash":"0ce469165ea7f79763cec56fa60790582c77cc15a0bf43ad3fb5ab4e8625437b"},"summary":"Keep bot.web as the one audit kind and have browser calls write it too","supersedes":"093999417ec67bc8872074787ed4ba298b849bbe92f07158b39c8db34c621df3","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:an outside reader of the audit trail depends on the kind bot.web","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:25.358331Z","id":"b8f54236eb2acf1cf6095e64a3c9a83a89a4424d23c977e78ad15c5b52c6bfa8","body":{"detail":"html is the markup decoded to UTF-8 with script, style, noscript, template, comments and event-handler attributes removed and links absolute: the page's structure without code a model would never run. raw stays main's body as it came. auto stays accepted as markdown so main's scripts and journals answer the same. A page store keyed by URL alone could not answer two formats of one page, so migration 67 rebuilds bot_web_pages with the format in its key.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":439},"end":{"line":460},"content_hash":"2f3e7c31858fb869efc3cd8d959b1d01857048f0857253ab1655479892d42bb8"},"summary":"Decision: fetch answers markdown (the default, main's auto), html (cleaned markup, no scripts or styles) or raw; the page store keeps a page per URL and format","supersedes":"c05a1419f98296675bfe8533cfe85cd2743b125fa841e349235cb84ef5f429e8","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:25.559840Z","id":"125210291847e0b10e32a65dacc60309746f6714dc11bed5f416b34b0ccb265d","body":{"detail":"The surface format declares functions of namespaces and the sandboxes pass JSON values (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js), so a value cannot carry methods without a prelude change in every sandbox (clax-bot-js and the Worker's driver).\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1517},"end":{"line":1521},"content_hash":"0a8da119d8b9eabc7553a6242a12719cc388556ea50ec6f987b79c687869d4d1"},"summary":"Decision: a session is a string handle taken by operations of the browser namespace, not an object with methods","supersedes":"016bba139ae573ea40c6872ab30d2e2672d269880e53445e313e230b0a1b3f34","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:25.758026Z","id":"39faeb519dc8625029c24486361bdb1c635d14dbea2ec3cd46b6e72d5cdcac20","body":{"detail":"Reads as the owner wrote it. Not taken: every sandbox's prelude would have to wrap handles in objects whose methods call the namespace's operations, a change to the surface format's contract for one namespace.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1515},"end":{"line":1516},"content_hash":"34cd368c26b43be19e5facf315b85afe1e99fca165e59a82ac15df5af48b81db"},"summary":"Session methods on the value open answers (s.click(...)), made by the prelude","supersedes":"b87421cf4c43f2dd3502ee938da51d4b898730dad11ee1e53db2010cb9252ebc","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:the surface format gains values with methods","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:25.960025Z","id":"4747cd737c357ee233e1cf3fda1c2200ff64522d181f4dad3be02d4b0a1ff649","body":{"detail":"The journal keeps an argument hash (CallEntry::args_hash), so content is never written to the store; a replayed open answers from the journal and a later call on a lost session fails rather than reloading content Clax no longer has. Image handles let a script show run content without copying bytes.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":629},"end":{"line":636},"content_hash":"7295515450ec0c526bb369e38fbc85142504daed6dd8ac88f2966ed0eaad756a"},"summary":"Decision: supplied content is held only in the session, has no bridge and no page runtime API, and is capped at 2 MiB of HTML and 16 MiB of files","supersedes":"0ea3431f7e6e88a0c416d0565f4ed0895457a30ddf1f0efb971e02b28dc9c4ee","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:26.158458Z","id":"cbd988f3c99f2550e03e9e1b168985aaf31cc2b2556ea81812c578e5e8b6bd72","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":638},"end":{"line":656},"content_hash":"e5137da164872e93ece244633c096e08e336bc20f5eaf183456643b6020dda01"},"summary":"Decision: a session ends on close, 300 s idle, 1,800 s open, a revoke, a credits refusal or the run's end","supersedes":"fabce9cafb3c8d59814222f4e85ef9fe166f5cff742748ffc0f6b208c82779ca","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:26.358691Z","id":"844531e12fbe0b8c7aad941d1114bddd5c9f08a552fd954e9dea6a4c80856a89","body":{"detail":"A click or type is not idempotent: when a step's attempt performed a call and failed before the Spend transaction wrote it (a store error), the retried attempt performs it again on the live session. Web fetches have the same window (web section 4.2). Closing it would need a per-call idempotency key the browser cannot honour.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":676},"end":{"line":678},"content_hash":"95e855cb6fd9f8c342002a454f116f30d88a36cdb4f42a1d9fc9203c103343f5"},"summary":"A step retried by the same process performs again a session call whose first attempt was performed but not journaled","supersedes":"7857a3afa48fc1350b56feccd7f593bc352805e43a32eae1c04a2fefac3087bf","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:26.560469Z","id":"348b7cec1d65562b41233f4ff8abc989d81a45b8759b042dbc26b71956c94566","body":{"detail":"Needs no decoder or encoder in Clax, no new crate, and builds for the Worker unchanged. The model sees at most four frames as images.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":799},"end":{"line":808},"content_hash":"7624638c8e4e3e4c0328f2a9eb880afdf80db8a9d97ec2267075015a1963a377"},"summary":"Decision: a recording is a sequence of the JPEG frames Chrome's screencast sends, with a JSON manifest, played by the run panel as a flipbook","supersedes":"9c49faf05cb460df3ad682925e94e12b261a78b51e585eda9aed702629ff222e","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:26.762524Z","id":"8c6f772be5bb765974d6bb3e511343c26d29ace31ecd65b3a968f1153522b404","body":{"detail":"One file people can download or attach. Not taken now: GIF needs two new crates and daemon CPU and has 256 colours; MediaRecorder needs a second page in the session driven by a canvas, adding a moving part to every recording.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1546},"end":{"line":1547},"content_hash":"ae3deb231bdcb9b838170ff9c7d46781697456031481c4c5527ccf8dd1d92c5b"},"summary":"Encode a recording as an animated GIF (gif and a JPEG decoder, pure Rust) or as WebM made by the browser's MediaRecorder","supersedes":"904a3a8a17e9d285990c2c9f4ccb60e5a628770f9099785ee4ac7b2e9356fd0d","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:a clip must leave Clax as one file, attached to a reply or downloaded","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:26.968408Z","id":"357ac36aad5949c9c7e4c0730769a2971bab27131cc84e29788388b86a524e7b","body":{"detail":"A thinking model keeps its browser slot for up to the idle time (300 s), so with browser.max_concurrent at 2 two runs with open sessions refuse every other open (browser_busy, retryable). The admin raises max_concurrent or lowers the idle time.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":810},"end":{"line":820},"content_hash":"827cb1fc06a9d4c608b54e893515eab23c0061427b408df7786580bd13d71498"},"summary":"Decision: one open session per run by default (up to 4), and the instance's two browsers are held until a session ends","supersedes":"c9ed67c39677d68c5a37e7f74f7ff1c22153403af289802cb4a66c4c3fca9f47","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:27.183370Z","id":"015d67dd9c3fd0b8e8a5ec94b99d6e188fb934c03cfc0e64cbc0391187dc4453","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1087},"end":{"line":1103},"content_hash":"e17c489c805eb26923a8388d7d61b585ed2321f63480f5ac55af574e3377f45a"},"summary":"Decision: keep_alive 60 s and a heartbeat after 20 s without a command, rather than a keep_alive as long as a model turn","supersedes":"aff98448613372321c7cbc78064bf84b71407376c0335d7fe24a2e5634707c97","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:27.384914Z","id":"96245f5b080bcd83ab4374a4803c187c3b131cf513821c1c44f6a80450f5aa97","body":{"detail":"Section 7.2 assumes keep_alive bounds the time without DevTools commands, so a heartbeat keeps a session alive and an orphan lives at most keep_alive. If keep_alive instead runs only after the socket drops, the heartbeat is harmless and the orphan bound still holds; if Browser Run also ends a browser after a fixed lifetime shorter than browser.session.max_seconds, sessions end early and answer browser_session_lost. Only the opt-in live test (just browser-live) can check; it has not been run against Cloudflare.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1089},"end":{"line":1093},"content_hash":"a0a715c6352748687ec7c5a172a788480f34050154ae19caea37ac3e7683ee7f"},"summary":"Browser Run's keep_alive semantics and maximum are unchecked: whether it counts inactivity of commands or time after the socket drops, and whether its maximum is 20 minutes","supersedes":"43c68e4ed308d05a1f47ed74d6cb606d4ce7677e6f9ec7223fc905dd5c194613","tags":["claxbot-browser","risk","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:27.594040Z","id":"17aca8e4f4265b5b77ed275fa0032bd9e521d708e41a364ad63e966f57406bc6","body":{"detail":"Simpler: no timer in the host. Not taken: a browser orphaned by a daemon crash would bill up to the idle time (300 s, up to 20 minutes), and a model turn longer than Browser Run's maximum would lose the session.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1543},"end":{"line":1545},"content_hash":"45853c944a7add77a77d21c5f607b16a4c6c271b4be24e7b4bc9eda1addd12fb"},"summary":"Set keep_alive to the session's idle time (at most Browser Run's maximum) and send no heartbeat","supersedes":"817732f2c6e088c92f5885046101cb15c526940e85b3a62a6d54f98cd41203ff","tags":["claxbot-browser","revisit:Browser Run bills or limits heartbeat commands","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:27.796671Z","id":"589f9e7526fd3919f3fa6bb40e272bc9296795bc905cc9da1af5ba0738644954","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1121},"end":{"line":1142},"content_hash":"43e2d08640ddd75cdff190de931682228875ad53895a6ca420f555689e66033b"},"summary":"Decision: open sessions live in a host-owned registry of tasks that own their sockets, serve requests between calls, heartbeat and end themselves","supersedes":"960b9cd6a18283aa603287482442bd377a181f7163dd38f2f4f65acaa0d6622f","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:28.003322Z","id":"2c27e3c80ac571898be08bd80257c71cb29d2aef20d232aa64ce569f38ec26c4","body":{"detail":"So the artifact's read-only API and supplied content are never reachable from a page that can reach the web, and the conversion counts against the URL cap. A goto within the origin needs nothing more.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1218},"end":{"line":1229},"content_hash":"be524ed0cf4ae622c5b577e1194822527d935ed3777c528d815a5e80778942e2"},"summary":"Decision: a goto out of an artifact or content session needs browser.open.url, converts the session once, and stops serving its synthetic origin","supersedes":"b304d23bf5630c1bd951461d27ffa4b69d70be5af1ee16e9ee80d85f329085dc","tags":["claxbot-browser","security","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:28.220598Z","id":"b6bc84ac681a7127eca4daaf1c34933e32ac7441e44fde5f5897d1bb9dd7400c","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1288},"end":{"line":1321},"content_hash":"70c28cedb2d33bde748043264f70bc223852edb35b592492e9f1fbbaa7b215c8"},"summary":"Decision: browser time is charged in contiguous millisecond segments, each session call charging up to its end and a host's end charging the rest once","supersedes":"8a6afec97332d80e3efd3036fae78183dbcbf0e04f70ce42aa2c17a9ee304a96","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:28.422608Z","id":"24fdd71ea74361e953240cddf3272abeb5ecb427111f51ce99f09e60724a976e","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1325},"end":{"line":1357},"content_hash":"183bee25f6c6f4bf6dea81fc1e039ce8e11472a804574476398508bb3669b833"},"summary":"Decision: main's web.* settings stay as they are; the first version's browser.* settings are renamed per capability","supersedes":"64ef833373b7c370171532ebc39e7c186443253000c8ec4498072534af863c48","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:28.622131Z","id":"3f37067616c42541c1131126a5f80fc84a6939043be1d00b212d2056207f0bcb","body":{"detail":"The owner's standing rule: sessions start at zero; capabilities are the union of live grants; revoke re-evaluates transitively. So no person holds a capability by default. Section 4.3 (lines 214-271) computes caps(run) from the admin's switch (the instance offers the capability, with its terms), the admin's grants (to everyone on the instance, or to one person), the person's grant to their runs (an instance-wide grant issues it to each person as a recorded child; the person's switch revokes or re-issues it) and the source. Migration 67 writes main's behaviour as explicit rows: an instance-wide grant of web.search and of web.fetch where that switch was on, and its child for every person except those whose bot_person_prefs.web was off (section 11.2, lines 961-993). The three browser.open kinds get no instance-wide grant; the admin grants each explicitly. Revoking an admin grant ends its children and re-evaluates every run and session under them (section 4.4). This replaces the waiver that read a missing row as a live grant.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":236},"end":{"line":293},"content_hash":"44258f8fe3b962d9d5db7031985a2d7df5880d099c0567a965e79362dd0736e2"},"summary":"Decision: grants are explicit, none implied; main's web default becomes an instance-wide grant the admin holds and can revoke","supersedes":"c8a7f9b5461c61603ff3421783744a6287599984e4b54e4ef8d6e8c2dad970f6","tags":["claxbot-browser","status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:07:28.825680Z","id":"5f932cda24d13ab2e5d10ae1bb6193afba992b897da752109a7c45975b5fe234","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1359},"end":{"line":1391},"content_hash":"9a8c05331115898c7cfefea00b04c6d0a7377d83249826b530995c123590f91f"},"summary":"Decision: grants are rows of bot_cap_grants (granter, grantee everyone, a person or a person's runs, parent, status), recorded as bot.grant; main's web switches and choices become explicit rows","supersedes":"a4d4b502e3bb58e0bcb3d74d12d27f0cf12c277a9bf274e25bb8531f57c99b57","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.687883Z","id":"8e9104bc68db8fe3c0e4f17f2b5c53cc56fd0dc9010a27d44dcee95835df0708","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","references":"db71c602b908f03856fa386ecd9f5d2477381ef0b5c2057c67ecb16669429e2e","span":{"start":{"line":1423},"end":{"line":1427},"content_hash":"ad77ff1bfdf76f0132967f3f410748bbaeb45f179a4824bec45e24e61317beb5"},"summary":"Built: GET /api/bot/runs/<id>/content/<item> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs run_content), image items of that run of the four raster types only, under Content-Security-Policy: sandbox; default-src 'none' and nosniff, 404 otherwise. Tests: api_claxbot::run_content_is_served_to_the_runs_viewers_only, api_claxbot::a_non_image_item_is_not_served. It admits the person the run acts for and admins who read its artifact, not readers (see the alternative on run_content).","supersedes":"d4b5e606aedd7f5eb2a820ad9bc11eee73580d5c7b2e4c7d593232a164938d08","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889470Z","id":"e3168e558eff08783e4ef681265aa3b6c574e8e6881448810b1c5d318e65b837","body":{"detail":"The owner, 2026-11-19: \"Our browser API should probably be pretty similar to the builder system used by playwright.\" The owner approved the proposal that followed: the script API mirrors Playwright's names and signatures as a subset; Page and Locator are a thin layer in the shared sandbox prelude (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js), each method one call of a few flat journaled operations (browser.open, page, act, expect, close), so the journal, charge-once and replay rules are unchanged; locators are plain data resolved at each call, never live element handles, and actions auto-wait as Playwright's do; what is unsupported is not declared rather than failing at run time; the declaration is generated or checked against the flat operations so they cannot drift; browser.test and runTests stay. Spec §0 item 6, §6.1, §6.5, §6.8 to §6.12. It overturns 125210291847 (a session as a string handle taken by one operation per action).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":464},"end":{"line":497},"content_hash":"6e54bfc26d2399e7bd3394786058d896c39609c48145db1ef0e2277d0e032e68"},"summary":"Decision (owner): the browser script API is Playwright's Page, Locator and expect, as a subset, over flat journaled operations","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889546Z","id":"0a68bd347dd19212ab9a3bc17a015a3040c993cd389f42f17845b6ca93bee722","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.5. A Locator carries steps ({css}, {role,name,exact,...}, {text}, {label}, {placeholder}, {testId}, {nth}, {hasText}, {hasNotText}; at most 16; a RegExp as {regex, flags}); each action resolves them again until exactly one element matches and is actionable per the action's table (attached, visible, stable over two animation frames, enabled, receiving events, editable), waiting in the browser on frames and mutations, bounded by BrowserSource::deadline, never by a sleep in Clax. Timeouts: the call's, else setDefaultTimeout, else 10 s; navigations 30 s; expect 5 s; all capped at browser.call_seconds; timeout 0 means the cap. The flat call answers {ok:false, error, timeout}, journaled and charged as any answer (§4.7); the prelude throws TimeoutError or Error with Playwright's message. Strict mode: two matches fail at once, naming them.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":680},"end":{"line":756},"content_hash":"dad47f0fe52d09bba880ccdf2a8a8423a15485aa9bc2b869f5bb6a38fbdd5d3e"},"summary":"Decision: locators are step lists resolved in the page at each call; actions are strict, auto-wait within a timeout, and the prelude throws a failed answer as Playwright would","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889594Z","id":"a6a4be119a8571ea450a763557159771b621cf283ef4f4c4d9daad4dddf69e7e","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.5 evaluate. As in Playwright the function carries no closure. A native or bound function is refused with a TypeError in the prelude before any call. The value is returned by value as JSON, at most 16 KiB. The source is in the call's arguments, so the journal's argument hash covers it. Non-JSON args (Date, Map, BigInt, handles) are not carried (§6.12).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":757},"end":{"line":768},"content_hash":"fd00a383fa2584a87d6c819d87bfbda8fbf587c61a1f045ed08a5d5ef1dbb178"},"summary":"Decision: evaluate sends a function as its source text (the captured Function.prototype.toString), called by Runtime.callFunctionOn with one JSON arg; a string is an expression","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889640Z","id":"0ea8fdf2bb9777e7a44b886d6aaa0a62a4e37110fbb657d4abc1cbd20b10b3cd","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.5 Console and errors, §6.1. Replaces the earlier spec's console() since the previous call and the new counters on every action answer. Each is a charged call. The answers are objects with Playwright's methods (type(), text(), location(); Error's message and stack) and a toJSON so a returned value shows its data. Caps: 100 console entries of 1,000 characters, 50 errors, 100 requests per list.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":769},"end":{"line":772},"content_hash":"ec66a589101c56a52a8a36a66d261d0219bdd193ae4d9dfeed00de54afcc8ff5"},"summary":"Decision: console and page errors through Playwright 1.56's page.consoleMessages() and page.pageErrors(), all collected since the page opened; failed and blocked requests through Clax's own page.failedRequests()","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889681Z","id":"aeb201b7da535f4ae5c4e58dc4301fbf5704a3ff2a1ff84915f8442afbf3c661","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.6. Playwright records a whole context's life to a file from creation to close; a session may be open 30 minutes, so the bounded clip of the frame-sequence format (9c49faf0's decision) stays, under a name that does not pretend to be Playwright's. Listed as Clax's own in §6.1 and §6.12.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":774},"end":{"line":790},"content_hash":"c3eded4d0a69247e1e71e96da266a63aa95ec43e3f9029fb86a52266b024edb5"},"summary":"Decision: recording is Clax's own page.record({seconds}), 1 to 10 s, not Playwright's recordVideo and page.video()","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889720Z","id":"d0c458ee6b098b7c30c1795b9aa96dda061d0e9227bbfa7574f7c1953cdcdce5","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.8. A Page does everything the steps did, so the steps (a second language for the same actions) go. browser.test is kept because it is one call and one journal entry for the check before publishing, holds no session that could bill idle time while the model thinks, runs the saved tests exactly as the inspect view does, and is one line in the run panel. page.runTests(paths?) runs the same tests inside a held session. The alternative of dropping it is recorded on §15.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":822},"end":{"line":858},"content_hash":"d6af9511332b3490ab1438fb62beb5d820d788d2068ad9d685414cae850a492b"},"summary":"Decision: browser.test stays as a one-shot run of the saved tests, without the first version's steps list, html, text and screenshots","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889768Z","id":"b103bb09d03f65f3667558e1e0db2f3490d208f2b964d64a186a0f268a0637c8","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.9. Each method that reaches the browser is one row (class, method, op, action, parameter names) of a table the prelude reads; positional arguments become args by name, opts spread in, the default timeout added. Hand-written: open, close, evaluate, url(), the locator builders, Response, ConsoleMessage, pageErrors, expect. The layer is installed when the ops list includes the five session operations, and only then is the global expect defined. It uses only built-ins captured before the script runs, reads no clock or random number, and is pinned by conformance cases on both sandboxes.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":860},"end":{"line":931},"content_hash":"af5f57ddc4cbd9433cfaa4c7479c92c7c38eb2d9348ede4fa17e51be8b178240"},"summary":"Decision: clax.d.ts declares six flat browser operations (open, page, act, expect, close, test) with action unions; the prelude builds Page, Locator, Keyboard and Mouse from a table and hides page, act, expect and close from the script","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889806Z","id":"64081c340379a003db59d5f1a74b891303709276f4240b9f5b878ede06e1bda0","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.10. Matchers: toBeVisible, toBeHidden, toBeEnabled, toBeDisabled, toBeChecked, toBeFocused, toHaveText, toContainText, toHaveValue, toHaveAttribute, toHaveCount; toHaveURL, toHaveTitle; .not. Value matchers toBe, toEqual, toBeTruthy, toContain, toBeGreaterThan with web/bridge/src/harness.ts's semantics and messages, run in the sandbox with no call, pinned against the harness's own test table. A passing expect that waited is one journal entry charged its time; a replay answers it at once.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":932},"end":{"line":986},"content_hash":"30a0997825db98d91cd95321eea56e182e379ae307465271f6976b3805ce6f31"},"summary":"Decision: expect(locator) and expect(page) are one browser.expect call each, retried in the browser until the timeout; a failure throws an Error named Expected, as the saved-test harness's; expect of other values is the harness's five matchers","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889847Z","id":"3e3c85faa1977c83a3798c27519a853abae399da66982d363e999e37a97868bc","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.11. The surface format refuses methods outside declare const and interface Kinds (crates/clax-surface/src/dts.rs), so Page cannot be written in clax.d.ts. api::dts writes the browser namespace from the table, with only the methods and source kinds the run holds (runTests needs browser.open.artifact). Tests: every row's action is in its op's union and every union member has a row; the prelude's JSON table between marker comments equals the Rust table row for row; the generated declaration compiles with crates/clax-bot/src/browser.examples.ts. The alternative of extending the surface format is recorded on §15.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":987},"end":{"line":1013},"content_hash":"c6d5447623d4f1124368d3f905d22980bef0b35baaa940b28c79abd8796eb1dc"},"summary":"Decision: Page, Locator and expect are declared from one Rust table (browser/layer.rs), generated into the browser namespace in place of the flat operations, and checked against clax.d.ts's action unions, the prelude's table and TypeScript","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889884Z","id":"a978ffa28cf1245302dadb038f2780c718b90cff7436949ba69a111dc72e6b49","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.12 lists each with why. Not declared, so a model writing them is told at once rather than failing at run time. Declared with a different answer: screenshot() resolves an Image handle, not a Buffer; evaluate args and values are JSON; page.url() is the URL the last call answered (navigation between calls is seen at the next call); getByRole reads Chrome's accessibility tree, role typed string; dialogs are accepted, where Playwright dismisses, because no page.on('dialog') exists to accept one; page.close() resolves {ms, cost}; timeout 0 is the cap.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1014},"end":{"line":1051},"content_hash":"9438987fd195b07a4bf51179994349bb6ed5db090fcc439ef1a4d45e0a4c8f01"},"summary":"Decision: the Playwright behaviour not matched: handles, waitForSelector, events and routes, contexts and frames, recordVideo, soft and polling expects, waitForTimeout; screenshots as Image, JSON-only evaluate, page.url() as of the last call, dialogs accepted","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889921Z","id":"3cb2a1f835241db81a06a6f37ea476b4f6fca0d622081b618f30549a73497601","body":{"detail":"This spec's earlier §6.1, replaced by the owner's Playwright-shaped Page over fewer flat operations (§6.1, §6.9). It needed no prelude change and kept every value plain JSON, but taught the model an API of Clax's own and declared one operation per action.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1517},"end":{"line":1521},"content_hash":"0a8da119d8b9eabc7553a6242a12719cc388556ea50ec6f987b79c687869d4d1"},"summary":"Handle-first flat operations: clax.browser.click(session, selector) and one operation per action, the session a string handle","tags":["revisit:the prelude's browser layer cannot stay within the budget of spec §6.9 (10 KiB, 24 KiB in all) or behave the same in the QuickJS and Worker sandboxes","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889956Z","id":"306b1499022624538ace743188b0bc55d9c0fbc5b4b48923d38bc00fcd313222","body":{"detail":"Not taken: a handle cannot be journaled or replayed (a replayed step would get a handle to an element of a page state that no longer exists), and a re-render between model turns kills it. Locators resolved at each call (spec §6.5) cover what scripts need.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1522},"end":{"line":1525},"content_hash":"8bd6e51bc9afd020e3a4929a3ac8f55dfd2bbddfb8c3b49238246cc3bbfbdd51"},"summary":"Live element handles: Playwright's ElementHandle and JSHandle, a remote object kept in the session between calls","tags":["revisit:a flow needs an element that no locator chain can name, such as a canvas-drawn control reached only through evaluate","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.889990Z","id":"dcb76129ca0d7c7f0d7f888b5991d6d658271a82dfec760a480b22ab4dfe6e4f","body":{"detail":"Not taken: crates/clax-surface refuses methods outside the surface and interface Kinds, and changing the format touches every host's surface, the manifest and its checks for one consumer. Spec §6.11 generates the declaration from a Rust table instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1526},"end":{"line":1528},"content_hash":"6a66845417839cd31a71da9ace4e2a2f1978242af4a034ec6abc1233e00f11dc"},"summary":"Declare Page and Locator in clax.d.ts by extending the surface format with interfaces that have methods","tags":["revisit:a host's surface needs values with methods","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.890024Z","id":"8c891ad208f7e8dd16f4884d489f41e7aba4de605d082538f5f4efd23023fae2","body":{"detail":"Not taken: a session lasts up to 30 minutes, so a whole-life recording would be costly to keep and to show. page.record({seconds}) records a bounded clip (spec §6.6).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1529},"end":{"line":1531},"content_hash":"9dc03d55e0d960a617664b72519efc491d1f39fd14bde36d499c403dad6cfecc"},"summary":"Playwright's recordVideo context option and page.video(), recording a whole session to a file","tags":["revisit:a person asks for a whole session's recording, or a clip must cover more than 10 seconds","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.890057Z","id":"d8f7f6d3d5845bba0f1ac8de9098ad57d6a6e7fb29eb44768e899695c2383952","body":{"detail":"Not taken: browser.test is one call and one journal entry, holds no session that bills idle time, runs the saved tests as the inspect view does, and is one run-panel line (spec §6.8).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1532},"end":{"line":1534},"content_hash":"b4f49ba5e4cd2b96ea0803b70d3b50c70757364cad50ad67bdfefbfc9ebef4d0"},"summary":"Drop browser.test: open a Page, call runTests, close","tags":["revisit:the run panel and audit show runs no longer calling browser.test once Page sessions ship","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.890095Z","id":"da63457e8b5b6ee656b3ef90dbdea664102b40c12cd7f0a6fb97f8f36c737a40","body":{"detail":"Not in this version: saved tests run inside the page through the bridge (web/bridge/src/harness.ts) with its ui, and the inspect view runs them the same way. Only expect's value matchers are shared now (spec §6.10).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1535},"end":{"line":1537},"content_hash":"2df8d26c3889dec947e0a7b642d64e54a9ec66ceeae610f39a96e80cdb5a2f4a"},"summary":"Give the saved-test harness a Playwright-shaped page and expect(locator), so saved tests and scripts share one API","tags":["revisit:the inspect view's tests move off ui, or a person asks to keep a script's Page steps as a saved test","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.890132Z","id":"f83e9b518740711fde0f64a21545a1a87cc5d5201e6338fdd3077b0326a838ab","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.9 sets 10 KiB for the layer and 24 KiB for prelude.js (9,866 bytes today), held by a test, with just perf measuring a run's start. The layer is installed whenever the ops list carries the browser operations, which api::op_names gives every Clax run, so a run with no browser capability still parses it. Separately, §6.1's declaration is long; the prompt cache keeps it stable per run, but it is paid in every browser run's first turn. If the layer passes its budget, install it lazily on first use of clax.browser, or trim the table.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":923},"end":{"line":926},"content_hash":"05fd6c91c2ea5bc6c4b5faaea72f3690571a4f9e2456047e011437e23878b654"},"summary":"The prelude's browser layer is evaluated in every run's sandbox and may outgrow its budget; the Page declaration adds about 110 lines to every browser run's prompt","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.890166Z","id":"c2b4608a745b803c6afd55cb8ac296349611e17e270e4db3e503d4353c022a38","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.5 resolves role steps with Accessibility.queryAXTree; Playwright computes roles and accessible names with its own injected engine. Known differences: generic containers, hidden subtrees (includeHidden), names from title or placeholder, and Chrome's ignored nodes. A model reasoning from Playwright docs may get a different match count and a strict-mode error. Name matching (case-insensitive substring unless exact) is done by the driver over the tree's names, so queryAXTree's exact-name filter is not used.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1039},"end":{"line":1044},"content_hash":"bfc33e06fa1abcfe4545fe44dbeece72f9da674801e20810c0fb008e9cee6d7e"},"summary":"getByRole over Chrome's accessibility tree will not always match Playwright's own role and name engine","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.890201Z","id":"7bda2d4c58036a3d6f276d25ab12f290773eb206a4f917976ca5ea8c326990d8","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.5. Headless Chrome on Browser Run may throttle animation frames for a page not in front, so the stable check can stall until the timeout; a hit test at the centre misses an element whose centre is covered but whose edge is not (Playwright retries the point too); framework-controlled inputs and contenteditable may not take Input.insertText as Playwright's fill does. Each is pinned by a FakeChrome test, but only the live test (just browser-live) shows Chrome's behaviour.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":705},"end":{"line":732},"content_hash":"a88cbbaaad49bef82090192416474855ddec6dec4694f174f49706b15246312c"},"summary":"Playwright's actionability checks are approximated over CDP: stability by two animation frames, receiving events by a hit test at one point, fill by select-and-insert","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.890235Z","id":"a12371429a9d5eeee4826a758cac7a49db6dcc062a71e112218245317f650bf5","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.5 sends a function as its source text read by the captured Function.prototype.toString. V8 (the Worker sandbox) keeps source; QuickJS returns it only when the function was compiled with its source kept (crates/clax-bot-js builds a patched QuickJS and evaluates scripts with eval_with_options). If the native sandbox strips it, every evaluate(fn) is refused as a native function. The prelude task's conformance case must run evaluate(fn) on both sandboxes before anything relies on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":757},"end":{"line":768},"content_hash":"fd00a383fa2584a87d6c819d87bfbda8fbf587c61a1f045ed08a5d5ef1dbb178"},"summary":"evaluate(fn) depends on Function.prototype.toString returning the source in QuickJS, which a build that strips debug information does not","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.891013Z","id":"392979c3ebbc4326570648b4bf1c5798354852ce54c4e92b705273e5e7a16121","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"125210291847e0b10e32a65dacc60309746f6714dc11bed5f416b34b0ccb265d","summary":"Overturned by the owner: the session is held by a Playwright-shaped Page made by the prelude, over flat operations that take the session internally (spec §0 item 6, §6.1, §6.9)","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T18:08:30.891430Z","id":"04129c3b0a4e77ecce1e40d28f3b2a39f050ff9c049d1d2ba0acc5dab22ad72e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"39faeb519dc8625029c24486361bdb1c635d14dbea2ec3cd46b6e72d5cdcac20","summary":"Taken by the owner's direction: methods on the value open answers, as Playwright's Page, made by the prelude (spec §6.1, §6.9); this alternative is no longer a path not taken, and closing it as obsolete is the owner's","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:35:26.563116Z","id":"0e2b12d84631ebeb2fa863e1638ba7966b5170a3b63023196c3cf65a5b399d4e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b6bc84ac681a7127eca4daaf1c34933e32ac7441e44fde5f5897d1bb9dd7400c","summary":"Built in 5691d84f6: bot_browser_sessions (migration 67), SessionSpend in the Spend transaction, Store::end_bot_browser_session and Store::lose_open_bot_browser_sessions; tests bot_web::tests::segments_of_a_session_sum_to_its_open_time, a_replayed_call_charges_nothing, a_host_end_with_no_open_step_charges_once, a_second_end_charges_nothing, a_point_before_the_charged_one_is_refused, a_start_marks_open_sessions_lost (bazel test //crates/clax-store/...: 13 tests pass)","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:39:11.870161Z","id":"a57223fe40021c786bbf14d5de78068a65aee7bbb97ea1df942bb11234e82a39","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"589f9e7526fd3919f3fa6bb40e272bc9296795bc905cc9da1af5ba0738644954","summary":"Built in 9176150e9: crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs, BrowserSessions (open, call, close, end_run, reevaluate, ended) and one task per session owning its Cdp; tests live::tests (requests served between calls, idle and lifetime ends by the source's deadline, a crashed page lost, a revoke and the run's end queued for the store).","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:39:11.871594Z","id":"9aaa31a3df9d04381681c41d53ae228ed3156d64551eab69be8291f2a2840d33","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"015d67dd9c3fd0b8e8a5ec94b99d6e188fb934c03cfc0e64cbc0391187dc4453","summary":"The heartbeat half is built in 9176150e9: a session's task sends Browser.getVersion once no command has gone to the browser for 20 s (HEARTBEAT_AFTER_MS, test live::tests::the_heartbeat_is_sent_after_twenty_idle_seconds); keep_alive=60000 on the daemon's socket is Task 17 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-unify.md.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:54:44.327838Z","id":"3f32e6e83535fb1f29a924e720b87ac679f84527159462981ddcb8bb282282a7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4747cd737c357ee233e1cf3fda1c2200ff64522d181f4dad3be02d4b0a1ff649","summary":"Built in 066100591: crates/clax-bot/src/browser/serve.rs ContentSite (the content's own origin, CONTENT_HEADERS, no /_clax/), ContentPolicy, content_files; crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs parse_source with the html, files and bytes caps; tests serve::tests::content_is_served_at_its_own_origin, content_reaches_nothing_else, opts::tests::content_files_take_text_base64_and_images, content_over_its_caps_is_invalid_args.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:54:44.416900Z","id":"4e76729bea9f5a93fbd2b18b5ced227fd7bd9bf481b3389b4dacca3b9b312662","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2c27e3c80ac571898be08bd80257c71cb29d2aef20d232aa64ce569f38ec26c4","summary":"Built in 066100591 on the session's side: BrowserSessions::leaves says whether a goto leaves the synthetic origin; the call carries the URL session's policy (CallCtx::leave) once browser.open.url and its rule admit the URL, and the session swaps to serve::Left (every request to the old origin failed, why left) and the browse preamble, once, answering kind url; runTests then answers browser_disabled (test live::tests::a_goto_out_converts_the_session_once). The capability check, the rule's admission and counting it as a URL session are Task 14's performer (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-unify.md).","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T21:00:26.059711Z","id":"f876dfdb4dd4d0a7784329cd97298899cec5b55139195fcd4404cdb0f7971d7e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c2b4608a745b803c6afd55cb8ac296349611e17e270e4db3e503d4353c022a38","summary":"Pinned in 38d46e622: crates/clax-bot/src/browser/locate.rs lists the approximations (roles and names are Chrome's accessibility tree's, nodes it ignores excluded unless includeHidden; text is textContent, not innerText; CSS pierces open shadow roots one root at a time; no iframes). Tests act::tests::role_names_match_as_substrings_unless_exact, each_step_kind_resolves_as_the_spec_says, a_regex_step_matches_in_the_page pin the matching; they run against FakeChrome's accessibility tree, so where Chrome and Playwright disagree is still for a live check. The close is the owner's.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T21:00:26.069055Z","id":"ec7fe82d3c918a1cf5167eaf550fa29efac5cd6198de54b45a887702ba687df9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7bda2d4c58036a3d6f276d25ab12f290773eb206a4f917976ca5ea8c326990d8","summary":"Pinned in 38d46e622: crates/clax-bot/src/browser/act.rs lists the approximations (visible is a box with a size, so visibility: hidden and opacity: 0 count as visible; stable is the same box across one wait in the page, not two consecutive frames; receiving events is DOM.getNodeForLocation at one point; enabled and editable read from attributes; networkidle is load and a settle). Tests act::tests::click_waits_until_the_cover_is_gone, click_times_out_naming_the_cover, an_unstable_box_is_waited_for, fill_selects_and_inserts pin each. The close is the owner's.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T21:00:26.141388Z","id":"3828fc6f4656cd5e4738b2b969fa00ff459fcb794c38c49b46c60fcf2f1a128d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0a68bd347dd19212ab9a3bc17a015a3040c993cd389f42f17845b6ca93bee722","summary":"Built in 38d46e622 in the driver: crates/clax-bot/src/browser/locate.rs and act.rs (locators resolved per call, strict, auto-waiting actions; failures as ok false with Playwright's message).","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T21:00:26.142609Z","id":"8b8dbe5fbc22c43fc31783aaff070d0a4c4a9431e774169d1e41a111bafaf907","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"64081c340379a003db59d5f1a74b891303709276f4240b9f5b878ede06e1bda0","summary":"Built in 38d46e622 in the driver: act::expect retries a matcher (with not) inside one call, waiting in the page between checks, and answers once (tests act::tests::expect_retries_in_the_browser_and_answers_once, expect_not_waits_for_the_condition_to_stop, to_have_text_with_an_array_matches_in_order).","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T21:00:26.145065Z","id":"3e4ee13d16a2333e60867af1de25447bbd961bd5c7943af79046fbb5f5f09fb4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a6a4be119a8571ea450a763557159771b621cf283ef4f4c4d9daad4dddf69e7e","summary":"The driver's half is built in 38d46e622 (and 9176150e9): a function's source is called in the page with arg as its one argument and its value answered as JSON of at most 16 KiB (test act::tests::evaluate_calls_the_source_with_its_arg). It is sent as one Runtime.evaluate of (source)(arg as JSON), not Runtime.callFunctionOn, which would need an object to call it on; the effect is the same, the function seeing only arg and the page.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T21:51:45.967098Z","id":"1760d87e43a1bf661c9a9e0aba596b8fe6e86c3c9bee4398c36f15a12e76f081","body":{"detail":"The case runs page.evaluate(function add(x) { return x.n + 1; }, { n: 1 }) and expects the browser.page call's args.source to be that text exactly; clax-bot-js compiles scripts with eval_with_options (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, eval_options), which keeps source, and only module bytecode written with JS_WRITE_OBJ_STRIP_SOURCE drops it (third_party/clax-rquickjs-core/src/value/module.rs), a path the sandbox does not take. evaluate_refuses_a_native_function pins the other side: Math.max and a bound function read as [native code] and throw a TypeError before any call. The Worker's V8 keeps source by the specification; the same cases run there through crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/checks.rs.","kind":"comment","references":"a12371429a9d5eeee4826a758cac7a49db6dcc062a71e112218245317f650bf5","summary":"QuickJS keeps a function's source: clax_bot_sandbox::conformance case evaluate_sends_a_functions_source passes in //crates/clax-bot-js:integration (c6adff348)","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T21:51:45.968653Z","id":"fd701fdc60c1721722a2a7935a14501cb121981211ec9f60189d3ec7eeb3a1e9","body":{"detail":"Before the layer crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js was 10,038 bytes. The table of 63 rows (one per method reaching the browser) is about 3.7 KiB of it, the harness's value matchers about 2 KiB. The test the_prelude_stays_within_its_budget (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs) holds the whole file to 24 KiB; nothing holds the layer alone to 10 KiB. Plan Task 16 adds Page.record's row (about 50 bytes), which still fits. Growing further needs either a larger budget, a terser table (an action defaulting to the method's name), or minifying the layer, whose lines the reserved-segment test reads as written.","kind":"comment","references":"f83e9b518740711fde0f64a21545a1a87cc5d5201e6338fdd3077b0326a838ab","summary":"The prelude with the layer is 24,448 bytes, under PRELUDE_BUDGET_BYTES (24 KiB) by 128; the layer adds 14,410 bytes, over §6.9's 10 KiB (c6adff348)","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T22:57:04.518110Z","id":"36272d225b528625d77ebfa1df3d0c8cdf1fc3297f793bf6b878ce387d96c7c6","body":{"detail":"Each script runs in a fresh sandbox, so the Page an open answered is gone when the script ends. crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js gives P.Page a toJSON of {session, url} (a script that returns its page shows the model the ID) and clax.browser.session(id), which builds the Page of that session with no call; its url() is empty until its first call answers. The registry and the performers already reach a session by ID (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs SessionOp). Pinned by the conformance case a_returned_page_shows_its_session_and_a_later_script_reaches_it and by tests/browser.rs a_session_lives_across_steps_and_its_time_is_charged_once. The name is Clax's own (Playwright has no equivalent); plan Task 15 declares it beside open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":638},"end":{"line":656},"content_hash":"e5137da164872e93ece244633c096e08e336bc20f5eaf183456643b6020dda01"},"summary":"A session outlives its script, but the spec gives a later script no way to reach it: the build adds clax.browser.session(id) and a Page whose JSON is {session, url}","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T22:57:04.531722Z","id":"7471981d5c51ed58ab7c16624b082ef2a81c153b26806045c4dfbb4deaa8a0d5","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-surface refuses a required parameter whose type admits null (null means left out), and no optional parameter may come before matcher, so clax.d.ts declares expect(session, locator: Record<string, unknown>[], matcher, args?) and the prelude sends [] for expect(page). Each action's args are checked by its row of crates/clax-bot/src/browser/layer.rs (an option a row does not take is invalid_args). A call on a session that ended is refused at admission, uncharged (BrowserSessions::check), so a call after a credits close answers browser_session_closed rather than credits_exhausted again.","kind":"comment","references":"b103bb09d03f65f3667558e1e0db2f3490d208f2b964d64a186a0f268a0637c8","summary":"The six flat operations are built behind the prelude's Page (Task 14 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-unify.md); browser.expect's locator is [] for the page, not null","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T23:16:48.947933Z","id":"15f2a05471379f222ac7a03fbe177cc2a3779d474861c37c2f0f7efd912a0701","body":{"detail":"The layer's ROWS (flat operation, action, parameters, args check) and DECLS (signature, doc, capability) are two tables in one file, joined by class and method and held together by layer::tests::every_row_is_declared_once_and_every_declared_member_is_a_row_or_local. The TypeScript test compiles each golden src/api.browser-{artifact,content,url-artifact-content}.d.ts.golden alone, and the full one with src/browser.examples.ts, with the TypeScript compiler API under ES2022's library; crates/clax-bot exports them through :browser_declarations_bin. The declared clax.browser has open (answering a Page), session(id) and, with browser.open.artifact, test.","kind":"comment","references":"3e3c85faa1977c83a3798c27519a853abae399da66982d363e999e37a97868bc","summary":"Built in 9b504d34c: DECLS in crates/clax-bot/src/browser/layer.rs holds every declared member with its signature and doc; api::dts writes the Page layer from it, and the TypeScript check is a //web:unit test (web/scripts/claxbot-browser-dts.test.ts), not a tsc target in crates/clax-bot","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T23:16:48.949100Z","id":"f42ca8572decec7f8d4066bd456090f9cf6e5aaa7b50be0f306b22536201154b","body":{"detail":"Measured on src/api.browser-url-artifact-content.d.ts.golden from `type BrowserSource =` to the last generated interface. Most members carry no doc; the docs are on the ones whose behaviour differs from Playwright or is Clax's own. The prelude has 8 bytes of room left after record's row and clax.browser.session: the next row needs the budget raised or the layer made terser.","kind":"comment","references":"f83e9b518740711fde0f64a21545a1a87cc5d5201e6338fdd3077b0326a838ab","summary":"The Page layer of the declaration is 133 lines and 7,923 bytes for a run holding every source kind (9b504d34c), about 140 with record's row and BrowserClip (694cac5f7); the prelude ends at 24,568 of its 24,576-byte budget","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T23:16:48.950092Z","id":"cfb4c492b802365e31194e5bc410ee9d0becf370eb5009ff1151e595517e847e","body":{"detail":"Tests act::tests::every_frame_is_acknowledged, ten_seconds_is_the_most, record::tests::frames_are_kept_at_most_eight_a_second, four_evenly_spaced_frames_are_returned, the_manifest_names_each_frame_and_its_time, tests/browser.rs a_recording_keeps_its_frames_and_a_manifest, and the conformance case page_record_makes_one_call. A frame is timed by the session's clock when it arrives (not Chrome's metadata.timestamp), and the frame that arrives at or after the window's end is acknowledged and not kept. The manifest is stored as a content item with no change to clax-store (it checks no media type).","kind":"comment","references":"aeb201b7da535f4ae5c4e58dc4301fbf5704a3ff2a1ff84915f8442afbf3c661","summary":"Built in 694cac5f7: page.record({seconds}) in crates/clax-bot/src/browser/record.rs; seconds outside 1 to 10 is invalid_args at the performer, and the driver clamps to 10","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-11-20T02:56:19.131840Z","id":"c2e00840aeb2ee834442a2b1ce4d01700b76745cad49e7c23bd7af420b8f6e76","body":{"detail":"yes, load it only for browser runs","kind":"comment","references":"fd701fdc60c1721722a2a7935a14501cb121981211ec9f60189d3ec7eeb3a1e9","summary":"Decided: the Page/Locator/expect layer loads only in runs granted a browser.open capability; the prelude budget is raised for those runs alone","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-11-20T02:56:19.132292Z","id":"70eababf7e85d0e51169b14dddf111852c6e29f3e21e2bf00fd18b14a6207034","body":{"detail":"Maybe we should have some idea of persistent script state that can carry for the session?  A sort of session object that serializes across scripts?  Kind of like the window object across handlers in teh browser? / Having persistent sessions for the browser system still seems necessary but the state object gives a way to hold onto a cyrptographic capability to control the session across turns.  Browser sessions also should only live as long as their session handle","kind":"comment","references":"36272d225b528625d77ebfa1df3d0c8cdf1fc3297f793bf6b878ce387d96c7c6","summary":"Decided: no clax.browser.session(id); a run-scoped `state` object persists across scripts and holds an unforgeable session capability, and a browser session lives only as long as its handle","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:25.898034Z","id":"53825349be390872a0012d914c249b81b19dfa5a7a4e8c7a755c19e034ea9726","body":{"detail":"An action that fails on the page is an answer (ok: false), not an error, so a computer-use loop can look and retry. browser_session_lost (the browser is gone: restart, dropped socket, crash) and browser_session_closed (an end of section 6.3, reason in the message) are neither retryable nor counted; the script opens a new session.\nRe-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":378},"end":{"line":408},"content_hash":"31b70895d9ba57f9fe615b883f94202cad396d9d012ad07b14352b61de482f9a"},"summary":"Decision: codes are <family>_<condition>, shared where the condition is one; errors carry retryable and the capability; a session adds browser_session_lost and browser_session_closed","supersedes":"2820a394158fd671e0925366bfb474650ca1ef7281f881b715047aabb326fa69","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:26.101105Z","id":"b58cb28d20ee4d94a304e3444e7aa9365bd838a4210aad69d49bf7261a566a72","body":{"detail":"Each script runs in a fresh sandbox, so the Page an open answered is gone when the script ends. crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js gives P.Page a toJSON of {session, url} (a script that returns its page shows the model the ID) and clax.browser.session(id), which builds the Page of that session with no call; its url() is empty until its first call answers. The registry and the performers already reach a session by ID (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs SessionOp). Pinned by the conformance case a_returned_page_shows_its_session_and_a_later_script_reaches_it and by tests/browser.rs a_session_lives_across_steps_and_its_time_is_charged_once. The name is Clax's own (Playwright has no equivalent); plan Task 15 declares it beside open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":638},"end":{"line":656},"content_hash":"e9a3346be242272e70706300084fe342dc3b718d8ca9b4f892e4e0fdeff89375"},"summary":"A session outlives its script, but the spec gives a later script no way to reach it: the build adds clax.browser.session(id) and a Page whose JSON is {session, url}","supersedes":"36272d225b528625d77ebfa1df3d0c8cdf1fc3297f793bf6b878ce387d96c7c6","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:26.313990Z","id":"8f30a76f3b841c8f3924604859c8eb1d5d23b2a09ed2c55b686fa27842d6b5e6","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":638},"end":{"line":656},"content_hash":"e9a3346be242272e70706300084fe342dc3b718d8ca9b4f892e4e0fdeff89375"},"summary":"Decision: a session ends on close, 300 s idle, 1,800 s open, a revoke, a credits refusal or the run's end","supersedes":"cbd988f3c99f2550e03e9e1b168985aaf31cc2b2556ea81812c578e5e8b6bd72","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:26.530246Z","id":"4b32bda8d1a5c5e1e2513f7fd123be9a398d84cfe9a9cf56ea4786e14a79c2ba","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.9. Each method that reaches the browser is one row (class, method, op, action, parameter names) of a table the prelude reads; positional arguments become args by name, opts spread in, the default timeout added. Hand-written: open, close, evaluate, url(), the locator builders, Response, ConsoleMessage, pageErrors, expect. The layer is installed when the ops list includes the five session operations, and only then is the global expect defined. It uses only built-ins captured before the script runs, reads no clock or random number, and is pinned by conformance cases on both sandboxes.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":860},"end":{"line":931},"content_hash":"4a0a092f91e3335f3ae8c8d267c9ded2b54c8ed9e6f372aa92990660db23c04e"},"summary":"Decision: clax.d.ts declares six flat browser operations (open, page, act, expect, close, test) with action unions; the prelude builds Page, Locator, Keyboard and Mouse from a table and hides page, act, expect and close from the script","supersedes":"b103bb09d03f65f3667558e1e0db2f3490d208f2b964d64a186a0f268a0637c8","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:26.743143Z","id":"4b318c23cbfad82419a729e02435b9530853e930c2c0e1568dab6d1b006a9780","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.9 sets 10 KiB for the layer and 24 KiB for prelude.js (9,866 bytes today), held by a test, with just perf measuring a run's start. The layer is installed whenever the ops list carries the browser operations, which api::op_names gives every Clax run, so a run with no browser capability still parses it. Separately, §6.1's declaration is long; the prompt cache keeps it stable per run, but it is paid in every browser run's first turn. If the layer passes its budget, install it lazily on first use of clax.browser, or trim the table.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":923},"end":{"line":926},"content_hash":"d00a2e6604d06157ca900a81b442e2172a71deebfc0e42b179223cb15ba9a247"},"summary":"The prelude's browser layer is evaluated in every run's sandbox and may outgrow its budget; the Page declaration adds about 110 lines to every browser run's prompt","supersedes":"f83e9b518740711fde0f64a21545a1a87cc5d5201e6338fdd3077b0326a838ab","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:26.963946Z","id":"e4c1cd473fef934a9b418d70d87922d0b2b8b7e8c8b177e32c338a4c6c2fd11d","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the spec's revision for a Playwright-shaped browser API (§0 item 6, §6) moved its lines; unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1121},"end":{"line":1142},"content_hash":"232834d59147e13a1e80640208a0f4f6cd338a6ed25a398d59fc24d92075f11c"},"summary":"Decision: open sessions live in a host-owned registry of tasks that own their sockets, serve requests between calls, heartbeat and end themselves","supersedes":"589f9e7526fd3919f3fa6bb40e272bc9296795bc905cc9da1af5ba0738644954","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:27.175707Z","id":"53314e3ae0aa80f6b26c032805fa36e119e43c0534434f50f72e3821d857088a","body":{"detail":"Spec §17.1. 65,536 bytes is the sandbox's default result limit (clax_bot_sandbox::Limits::max_result_bytes, 64 KiB), so a state is never larger than what one script may return, and it is stored in every script step's payload that writes one. Leaving out the largest top-level members until it fits keeps the rest, page handles included, where refusing the whole state would close every page it held (§17.4). Each member left out is listed in the script's result as `too large (N bytes)`, so nothing is dropped silently.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1613},"end":{"line":1615},"content_hash":"94111373ec355fc1bdd6beb971c0db05268f378799204f25d632032cbe080b7c"},"summary":"Decision: a run's state is capped at 64 KiB of encoded JSON; over it the host leaves out top-level members, largest first, each listed","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:27.175781Z","id":"7d29f5b72660512ad9fff3d5ae3b558c3105e99d5f22d2ec96dcfc4ab63ceb5b","body":{"detail":"Spec §17.3. The owner asked for the way the secret is stored at rest to be decided, suggesting an opaque reference the host maps to the session, or the token's hash. The handle is 256 bits from the OS, drawn by crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs at the open; the journal keeps the open's answer and each call's argument hash, and the committed state keeps it in its handle entries. Nothing at rest reaches a session after its process ends (the registry is in memory, spec §6.4), and the handle is honoured only for the run that opened it. It never reaches events, the run panel, bot.spend records, logs, error messages or the model, which see the session's ID or \"<browser page>\".","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1677},"end":{"line":1687},"content_hash":"3d530f65f627d9134f04ac915a14b3ddefd35a5268d5a0d600e04c3bacf75571"},"summary":"Decision: a session's handle is stored at rest as itself (an opaque reference only its process's registry maps, for its own run, while the session lives), not as its hash","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:27.175834Z","id":"ed9ce42948d7b810e5969a3075a88e05ebdc34f358db5d42dd8ef42c7c198b81","body":{"detail":"Spec §17.3. The journal answers a replayed browser.open with what it stored, and the calls after it must hash as they did (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs compares args_hash), also after a restart (spec §6.4: a replayed step answers from its journal, the first new call answers browser_session_lost). With only the hash stored, the host would have to put the hash in place of the handle in every answer it journals and every argument hash it computes, for a value that reaches nothing once its process is gone.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1682},"end":{"line":1687},"content_hash":"e8ba05ce18574cb2ee6d250ecf965c4582c536b47ff1243edac8b966b00ef236"},"summary":"Keep only a session handle's SHA-256 at rest, the raw handle in memory and in the sandbox","tags":["revisit:browser sessions survive a daemon restart","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:27.175884Z","id":"6147856362024a84ae16d0edae52779408d334772db26e3b52e71e68e3d491ab","body":{"detail":"Spec §17.4. The run loop tells each binding's provider the handles of the state a script step committed, after the commit (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs); Clax's provider closes, dropped, every open session of the run not among them. Closing before the commit would close sessions a step that fails to commit, and is executed again from the same journal, still holds. A crash between the commit and the close leaves the session to the next step's commit, the idle time, or the restart that loses it.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1691},"end":{"line":1700},"content_hash":"8500f5f68215c0044b1ce4c3fe98fb99d6f9690a982aacd31f843493ab845741"},"summary":"Decision: a session not held by the committed state is closed after the step's commit, not when the script ends","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T03:07:27.175927Z","id":"ff39469b68c6ecfc1005aaf44801607ae04617fbfb32d86880297ca644ca4d63","body":{"detail":"Spec §17.5, the numbers for the owner's decision c2e00840 (raise the budget for browser runs alone). 24 KiB is PRELUDE_BUDGET_BYTES as the build had it (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs), now for the base alone, which state's codec joins; 20 KiB leaves the layer (14.4 KiB in c6adff348, with record's row and state's codec about 16 KiB) room for a few more rows.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1718},"end":{"line":1720},"content_hash":"4b19ddc46013441d6257eccbde475b92dccb54bb13656642f44cfcec7dd0fd10"},"summary":"Decision: prelude.js stays at most 24 KiB in every run, browser.js (the Page layer, browser runs only) at most 20 KiB","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T04:12:43.958045Z","id":"32915361f759094cdb8d13f97a208a915498ee6c53df42629d879e27ecd3a413","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js keeps the global state and writes it out when a script ends (84c47a5c0); crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/browser.js encodes each Page, Locator, Keyboard, Mouse and assertion as a handle entry and restores it live. crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs keeps the state with the step and starts the next script from it (527da655c). A Page's JSON is \"<browser page>\" (fd62e2eb5), its session is named by a 256-bit handle the registry draws (c23a0c2b5), and a session no committed state holds closes dropped (d1e688363). Tests: conformance a_page_and_its_locator_in_state_restore_live_as_one_page, there_is_no_session_from_a_string, a_returned_page_shows_no_capability; crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs a_session_lives_across_steps_and_its_time_is_charged_once, a_page_in_state_lives_into_the_next_script, an_open_answers_a_handle_no_record_names; crates/clax-server/tests/api_claxbot_run.rs a_session_across_two_steps_through_the_daemon.","kind":"comment","references":"b58cb28d20ee4d94a304e3444e7aa9365bd838a4210aad69d49bf7261a566a72","span":{"start":{"line":638},"end":{"line":656},"content_hash":"e9a3346be242272e70706300084fe342dc3b718d8ca9b4f892e4e0fdeff89375"},"summary":"Built as the owner decided (70eababf): a later script reaches a session through `state`; clax.browser.session(id) is removed (c23a0c2b5)","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T04:12:43.958547Z","id":"0a6033134ceaa4fa546847eaf4e3c3f3a33d24c1c8457aedd156f6fcb484a08a","body":{"detail":"clax_bot_sandbox::prelude_source(browser) splices the layer at prelude.js's `// browser-layer` line for a Script with `browser` set; crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs sets it when a binding has the five session operations among its own. The base grew by state's codec (spec §17.1). Tests: lib.rs the_prelude_and_the_layer_stay_within_their_budgets, the_layer_is_spliced_only_for_a_browser_script; conformance the_layer_is_absent_without_browser; crates/clax-bot/tests/browser.rs a_run_without_a_browser_capability_has_no_page_layer.","kind":"comment","references":"4b318c23cbfad82419a729e02435b9530853e930c2c0e1568dab6d1b006a9780","span":{"start":{"line":923},"end":{"line":926},"content_hash":"d00a2e6604d06157ca900a81b442e2172a71deebfc0e42b179223cb15ba9a247"},"summary":"Built as the owner decided (c2e00840): the layer is crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/browser.js, spliced in only for browser runs; prelude.js is 15,027 bytes of 24 KiB, browser.js 16,234 of 20 KiB (fd62e2eb5, 84c47a5c0)","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T04:15:37.044997Z","id":"b215c1b89bbfb8c34eac69f6ad26739943f28e79f8a4d340da3ceef903a1b4ce","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c23a0c2b5","summary":"Fixed as the owner decided in 70eababf: clax.browser.session(id) is removed and a later script reaches a session through state (84c47a5c0, 527da655c, c23a0c2b5). Evidence: conformance there_is_no_session_from_a_string and a_page_and_its_locator_in_state_restore_live_as_one_page pass in //crates/clax-bot-js:integration; tests/browser.rs a_session_lives_across_steps_and_its_time_is_charged_once and api_claxbot_run.rs a_session_across_two_steps_through_the_daemon pass; just check at 0742c11b1: 407 tests pass.","supersedes":"b58cb28d20ee4d94a304e3444e7aa9365bd838a4210aad69d49bf7261a566a72","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T04:15:37.119994Z","id":"c9eb643cfaf874ccf62b7344adb6e6e46bf7f5757184e0b7733a8fa84d2d4f55","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fd62e2eb5","summary":"Fixed as the owner decided in c2e00840: the layer is crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/browser.js, loaded only for browser runs, with its own 20 KiB budget beside prelude.js's 24 KiB (fd62e2eb5). Evidence: clax_bot_sandbox the_prelude_and_the_layer_stay_within_their_budgets passes (prelude.js 15,027 bytes, browser.js 16,234); tests/browser.rs a_run_without_a_browser_capability_has_no_page_layer passes; just check at 0742c11b1: 407 tests pass.","supersedes":"4b318c23cbfad82419a729e02435b9530853e930c2c0e1568dab6d1b006a9780","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
